INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('6ff7bcea-86ef-5478-bea4-dbb766c01247', 'Applied Engineer, Evaluations Role', 'Mercor', 'Finance', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$100 - $120/hr', 'Mercor is seeking software engineers to build and refine evaluations. You’ll turn completed pull requests into engineering tasks and use our in-house evaluation framework to multiple  frontier coding agents, including Claude Code, Codex and more.

We work alongside an in-house research team and have produced industry leading benchmarks to compare the performance of frontier large language models. 

In this role, you will:

- Identify repositories with enough substantive work to support challenging evaluations, and select suitable completed PRs.
    
- Investigate each problem, its reference solution, and the repository’s architecture, tests, and conventions.
    
- Write task prompts and build evaluations using automated tests, shell commands, and LLM grading prompts.
    
- Validate evaluations against reference solutions and deliberately flawed implementations. Find missing checks, incorrect grades, and criteria that unnecessarily constrain how a problem can be solved.
    
- Run evaluations repeatedly across multiple models and harnesses. Investigate whether failures come from the agent’s solution, the environment, or the grading, and establish that tasks expose meaningful weaknesses in agent performance.
    
- Refine evaluations through repeated testing and review. Document findings and grading decisions, and work through feedback.
    

You’ll need:

- Strong programming fundamentals and practical experience working in substantial and complex codebases. Languages we create evals for include TypeScript/JavaScript, Python, Java, Kotlin, Go, Ruby, PHP, C++ and Rust
    
- The ability to understand unfamiliar code, investigate subtle behavior, and assess whether different implementations solve the same problem correctly.
    
- Experience writing meaningful tests, including edge cases and regression coverage.
    
- Attention to detail and patience for repeated investigation and refinement.
    
- Practical experience using AI coding tools, with the judgment to verify their output and catch mistakes.
    
- Confidence using Git, test runners, and CI tooling.
    
- Clear and fluent written and verbal communication with the ability to own a task independently while raising questions when requirements are ambiguous.
    

Relevant experience can come from open-source, private, or enterprise repositories. Familiarity with a particular language or ecosystem is helpful; the ability to learn the repository and make sound engineering judgments matters more than its popularity or your public contribution history.

We provide onboarding to the evaluation framework and ongoing review feedback. After onboarding, you’ll be expected to own task selection, evaluation development, and iteration without step-by-step direction.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Commitment: Part-Time', '["Python", "JavaScript", "TypeScript", "Rust", "LLM Evaluation"]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Applied Engineer, Evaluations Role", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABlzI3p6G_LDaGWuNNEa6l?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('3497794e-d08d-5dc2-8c37-9440a12eb2fc', 'Applied Physics Benchmark Specialist', 'Mercor', 'Science', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$61 - $77/hr', '**Role Overview**

We are seeking expert physicists to author and review high-quality academic assessment content for an AI research initiative. You will write and verify rigorous multiple-choice questions across core physics domains, evaluate solution quality, and help establish gold-standard benchmarks used to advance AI capabilities.

You will be assigned one of two task types:

- **Question Authoring** — Create original, challenging multiple-choice questions in your area of physics expertise, rate their difficulty, and submit them for review.
    
- **Question Verification** — Review pre-written questions for accuracy, clarity, and rigor. Edit where needed, rate difficulty, and document any changes made.
    

**Physics Domains Covered**

Semiconductor Physics, Nanoelectronics & Spintronics, Photonics, Quantum Optics & Ultrafast, Quantum Sensing & Metrology, Plasma Physics & Fusion Energy, Nonlinear Dynamics & Turbulence, Geophysics & Reservoir Simulation.

**Key Responsibilities**

- Author original physics questions that test deep conceptual understanding, not surface-level recall
    
- Ensure questions are unambiguous, self-contained, and precisely defined — all necessary information must be in the problem statement
    
- Rate each question''s difficulty: Medium (intro undergraduate), Hard (advanced undergraduate), or Expert (post-graduate and above)
    
- Provide 1 correct answer and 9 plausible but subtly incorrect alternatives that challenge expert-level solvers
    
- Write step-by-step Chain-of-Thought solutions with clear, concise intermediate steps in markdown format
    
- Supply 1–5 academic references per question from reputable sources (peer-reviewed journals, university repositories)
    
- For verification tasks: flag issues with clarity, completeness, precision, or solvability and justify any edits made
    

**Ideal Qualifications**

- PhD or doctoral candidate in Physics, Applied Physics, Astrophysics, or a closely related field
    
- Master''s degree considered for candidates with exceptional depth in a specific subdomain
    
- Strong command of graduate-level physics concepts and mathematical formalism
    
- Experience with rigorous academic problem design or physics olympiad writing is a strong plus
    
- Excellent written English and ability to express complex ideas clearly and concisely
    

**More About the Opportunity**

- Expected commitment: 10+ hours/week
    
- Asynchronous, fully remote work


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Commitment: Hourly', '[]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Applied Physics Benchmark Specialist", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABn_yIA7lRhn_Aos9LS7jE?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('add476d2-2ad6-54b8-9f34-b99b8111b290', 'Arabic Linguistic Experts', 'Mercor', 'Languages', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$50/hr', 'Mercor is seeking experienced Arabic Linguistic Experts to join a cutting-edge AI research project in partnership with a leading research lab. This role centers on evaluating how effectively a large language model (LLM) performs in Arabic-language tasks and on curating high-quality Arabic linguistic data to train and improve the model''s understanding and generation capabilities.

**Key Responsibilities:**

- Evaluate the quality and accuracy of LLM-generated Arabic text across various use cases (e.g., translation, summarization, dialogue, grammar correction).
    
- Edit, refine, or rewrite Arabic content to meet linguistic and cultural standards.
    
- Annotate Arabic text for grammatical, syntactic, and semantic features.
    
- Identify model errors and language gaps, and collaborate with AI researchers to improve LLM performance.
    
- Provide detailed linguistic feedback and analysis to guide ongoing model training efforts.
    

**You''re a strong fit if you have:**

- Native or near-native fluency in Arabic, with excellent command over grammar, syntax, and stylistics.
    
- Professional experience in translation, editing, linguistic annotation, or NLP data work in Arabic.
    
- Strong understanding of linguistic nuances, regional variations, and context-appropriate usage.
    
- Interest in AI and LLM-driven language technologies (preferred but not required).
    
- Excellent attention to detail and ability to spot subtle errors or unnatural phrasing.
    
- Clear communication skills and experience working in distributed, remote teams.
    

**Why Join**

- Contribute to cutting-edge AI research in partnership with a leading research lab.
    
- Work on high-impact projects that directly support the development of advanced AI systems.
    
- Gain hands-on exposure to state-of-the-art AI research and development.
    
- Join a fast-moving project where your expertise and judgment can have a meaningful impact.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Commitment: Part-Time', '["LLM Evaluation", "Translation"]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Arabic Linguistic Experts", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoXlyRHc9GXoJIl5D2ZLc?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('54d93efd-b683-58cf-93d4-ca71bec7de55', 'Arts & Design Expert', 'Mercor', 'Finance', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$60 - $80/hr', 'The research teams behind the best-known AI models come to Mercor for design and creative judgment they can''t generate on their own. Your standards and expertise become the rubric that frontier AI is graded against.

This is a standing listing for designers and creative professionals who want AI training and evaluation work, not a specific job opening. It stays open whether or not a matching project is running this week.

New projects start on short notice, so instead of posting and pulling a listing each time, we keep one open per field and draw from it when one begins.

**What the work looks like**

We match creative professionals in the network to projects like:

- Writing a brief from work you have delivered, with the audience, the constraints, and the standard the result had to meet, plus the reference answer a model''s attempt gets graded against
- Grading model-generated design, writing, and imagery on craft: whether the hierarchy works, whether the type and colour choices are deliberate, whether the prose earns its length
- Flagging where a model''s output is technically competent and would not ship, given brand, accessibility, licensing, or what the medium actually allows

Creative listings on Mercor have posted at $60 to $80 an hour, set per project by scope and depth.

**What we''re looking for**

- Professional experience in design, writing, or a creative production discipline
- Clear written communication, since most of the work involves explaining your reasoning
- Comfort with ambiguous tasks, and willingness to flag unclear instructions

**What this covers**

This pool spans arts and design, including:

- Graphic and UX/UI design
- Visual arts, including painting and sculpture
- Performing arts, including music and theatre
- Film and media production; photography
- Fashion and textile design
- Writing and editing

A portfolio matters more than a credential here. What we most need is your ability to say why something works.

**How it works**

Apply here with your resume and confirm where you work from, then take a short AI interview, about 20 minutes total.

We verify your background and add you to the arts and design pool.

When a project needs your discipline, we invite matching people from the pool to that specific listing. It names the rate, the hours, and the client, and any hiring decision is made there.

**What to expect**

This listing does not accept or reject candidates, so you will not get a decision on it. We reach out when a project matches your background. Depending on what our clients are running, that can be within a week or several months.

Finishing the domain expert interview and joining every network you qualify for both improve your odds of being matched. You only need to sign up once to be eligible across all of them.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Expected Hours: 40 hrs/week
• Commitment: Part-Time', '[]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Arts & Design Expert", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoKOQYnwSIWKGcHtHKYnW?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('760845b0-0b94-589a-968c-c7b24aed213a', 'Asset & Wealth Management Expert', 'Mercor', 'Finance', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$100 - $130/hr', 'The research teams behind the best-known AI models come to Mercor for investment management judgment they can''t generate on their own. Your standards and expertise become the rubric that frontier AI is graded against.

This is a standing listing for asset and wealth managers who want AI training and evaluation work, not a specific job opening. It stays open whether or not a matching project is running this week.

New projects start on short notice, so instead of posting and pulling a listing each time, we keep one open per field and draw from it when one begins.

**What the work looks like**

We match asset and wealth managers in the network to projects like:

- Writing an investment case or a client scenario from your own mandate or book, with the thesis, the constraints, and the risk budget, plus the reference answer a model''s attempt gets graded against
- Grading model-built portfolio construction, allocation, and tax strategy: whether the factor exposures are intended, whether the benchmark is the right one, whether the withdrawal sequencing holds, whether the attribution actually explains the return
- Flagging where a model''s recommendation is defensible on paper and would breach a real mandate or fail a real client, given liquidity, concentration limits, drawdown tolerance, or time horizon

Comparable investment management projects have posted at $100 to $130 an hour, set per project by scope and depth.

**What we''re looking for**

- Professional experience in portfolio management, buy-side research, multi-asset allocation, financial planning, or private client advisory
- Clear written communication, since most of the work involves explaining your reasoning
- Comfort with ambiguous tasks, and willingness to flag unclear instructions

**Where people in this pool have worked**

The most common backgrounds, though the pool is broader than this:

- Long-only asset managers and mutual fund complexes
- Hedge funds and multi-strategy platforms
- Pension, endowment, and sovereign allocators
- Private banks and wirehouse wealth management
- Registered investment advisors and multi-family offices
- Trust, estate, and fiduciary practices

The firm name matters less than whether you made the calls yourself, recently enough to explain the tradeoffs behind them.

**How it works**

Apply here with your resume and confirm where you work from, then take a short AI interview, about 20 minutes total.

We verify your background and add you to the asset and wealth management pool.

When a project needs asset or wealth management expertise, we invite matching people from the pool to that specific listing. It names the rate, the hours, and the client, and any hiring decision is made there.

**What to expect**

This listing does not accept or reject candidates, so you will not get a decision on it. We reach out when a project matches your background. Depending on what our clients are running, that can be within a week or several months.

Finishing the domain expert interview and joining every network you qualify for both improve your odds of being matched. You only need to sign up once to be eligible across all of them.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Expected Hours: 40 hrs/week
• Commitment: Part-Time', '["Taxation"]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Asset & Wealth Management Expert", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoKMi5yd-bKOyjYtOUZox?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('c93ea4a4-2323-531d-80d3-90915625b71a', 'Atomic Layer Deposition (ALD) Experts', 'Mercor', 'Data Annotation & RLHF', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$84/hr', 'Mercor is seeking experts in Atomic Layer Deposition (ALD) and thin-film processes to support a frontier AI research lab building models for semiconductors and the physical sciences. This is hands-on, expert-level work: you''ll apply deep, specialized knowledge to generate, structure, and evaluate the scientific data these models learn from — and your input will directly shape how advanced models reason about deposition, materials, and semiconductor processes.

Key Responsibilities:

* Contribute domain expertise across ALD process development, precursor chemistry, and thin-film characterization to build high-quality training and evaluation data.
* Review and evaluate AI-generated scientific reasoning, catching errors and improving technical accuracy.
* Design and solve challenging, expert-level problems in ALD and semiconductor processing.
* Rate and rank model outputs against defined scientific criteria, with clear written reasoning.
* Structure technical knowledge — process parameters, recipes, characterization results — into well-organized, model-ready data.
* Deliver reliable, high-quality work within defined timelines.

You''re a strong fit if you have:

* Hands-on experience developing, optimizing, or troubleshooting ALD processes.
* Deep knowledge of thin-film deposition for semiconductor or advanced-packaging applications.
* A strong grasp of precursor chemistry and surface reaction mechanisms.
* Experience with materials characterization (XRD, SEM, TEM, XPS, ellipsometry, etc.).
* An advanced degree (PhD/MS) or equivalent hands-on experience in materials science, chemistry, chemical engineering, or physics.
* Clear written English and the ability to explain technical reasoning precisely.

