INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('790f8c56-c9bc-562b-ba9c-92e4fba17ffa', 'Biochemistry & Life Sciences Domain Expert', 'Mercor', 'Science', 'Bay Area, CA', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$65 - $105/hr', '**Join a leading AI lab''s cutting-edge GenAI team to be at the core of the AI revolution, where your expertise fuels the development of the most advanced AI models.**

## 1\. Overview

We are hiring a senior **biochemistry and life sciences domain expert** to work directly with a leading AI lab''s research and program management teams, improving how frontier AI models reason about real life sciences research work.

Your scientific expertise is the substance of this role. You will review the quality of life sciences knowledge work tasks, write the instruction specs and golden solutions that define what "correct" looks like, and build the benchmarks that show whether the model is genuinely improving. We are looking for a practicing specialist rather than a generalist.

This is a full-time W-2 employment position with Cincinnatus LLC, with the opportunity to be placed at a leading AI lab as part of their extended workforce. You will be provisioned with client-issued accounts and equipment, and will work inside the client''s own tools alongside their research teams.

**Location:** This is a **hybrid** role based in the **Bay Area, California**. You must live in the Bay Area and work on-site with the client''s team multiple days each week, when required. This is not a remote role. If you do not currently live in the Bay Area, you must be willing to relocate there at your own cost before the engagement starts. Relocation assistance is not provided.

## 2\. Key Responsibilities

- **Data QA and reviews:** Vet the quality of life sciences knowledge work tasks and model outputs, spotting missing behaviors, thin reasoning, mechanistic hand-waving, unsupported causal claims, and answers that read well but would not survive peer review.
    
- **Instruction specs and golden datasets:** Write high-quality instruction specs, produce golden solutions to life sciences problems, and define new tasks that reflect how the research is actually done in practice.
    
- **Benchmarks and domain depth:** Design challenging life sciences tasks and evaluation sets, and help build domain-specific skills and tools together with the research team.
    
- **Calibration:** Work with client researchers and specialists in adjacent fields to keep standards consistent, translating tacit scientific judgment into explicit, teachable criteria.
    

## 3\. Core Qualifications

- **Education:** PhD in biochemistry, molecular or cell biology, genetics, immunology, neuroscience, or a closely related life science.
    
- **Experience:** 4+ years of substantive research experience at a recognized institution, for example a research university, an academic medical center, a national laboratory, or an industrial research organization. Graduate coursework alone does not count.
    
- **Domain depth:** Genuine specialization in at least one area, for example molecular and cell biology, biochemistry and structural biology, immunology and immuno-oncology, genetics and genomics, neuroscience, or systems biology.
    
- **Seniority:** Clear progression to a senior level, for example Senior Scientist, Staff Scientist, Research Scientist, Instructor, Principal Investigator, or a faculty appointment, with real ownership of research direction.
    
- **Research record:** A record of peer-reviewed publications, ideally including first-author work in strong journals. Strongly preferred.
    
- **AI fluency:** Hands-on working use of large language models in your professional work, and the judgment to tell a well-reasoned answer from a plausible-sounding wrong one.
    
- **Availability:** Able to commit reliably to 40 hours per week for an initial engagement of 6 months.
    
- **Location:** Living in the Bay Area, California, and able to work on-site with the client''s team multiple days each week, when required. Candidates not currently based in the Bay Area must be willing to relocate there at their own cost. Relocation assistance is not provided.
    
- Excellent written communication, and the ability to give precise, well-structured written feedback.
    

## About Cincinnatus LLC

Cincinnatus LLC is an enterprise staffing company that partners with leading technology companies to source and employ highly skilled professionals for contingent and contract-based opportunities. Cincinnatus serves as the employer of record for these engagements, providing W-2 employment, payroll, benefits, and compliance, while placing employees directly within client teams to work on high-impact initiatives.

Roles hired through Cincinnatus are not project-based or freelance engagements. They are structured, role-based positions that typically involve part-time or full-time commitments, close collaboration with a client''s internal teams, and integration into standard enterprise workflows.

Cincinnatus is a legal entity separate from Mercor. While opportunities may be discovered through Mercor''s platform, employment, onboarding, payroll, and benefits for these roles are administered by Cincinnatus LLC.

## Equal Employment Opportunity

Cincinnatus is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, reproductive health decisions, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, genetic information, political views or activity, or any other legally protected characteristic.

Cincinnatus is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities and disabled veterans throughout the job application process.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Expected Hours: 40 hrs/week
• Commitment: Full-Time
• Eligible Locations: USA', '["LLM Evaluation", "Compliance", "Biochemistry", "Molecular Biology"]', '["**Data QA and reviews:** Vet the quality of life sciences knowledge work tasks and model outputs, spotting missing behaviors, thin reasoning, mechanistic hand-waving, unsupported causal claims, and answers that read well but would not survive peer review."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoBt8bMBAKZ7C0OhMPqh8?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('344ea27c-502a-5ba4-a6d7-37d0abd4d118', 'Biologist Talent Network', 'Mercor', 'Science', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$60 - $80/hr', '**About Mercor’s talent network**

Join our Biologist Expert Network to connect with leading AI labs and companies seeking your expertise. **This is an open application for future contract opportunities that match your background and interests.**

Once you complete your profile and pass our AI interview, you''ll be eligible for relevant projects as they become available. We match experts to opportunities on a rolling basis.

**About Mercor projects**

Experts in our network contribute to:

- Training and evaluating AI models in Biology
    
- Creating tasks and deliverables based on real-world scenarios
    
- Providing domain-specific feedback to advance frontier AI research
    

Projects vary in scope and duration, with typical commitments ranging from 15-30 hours per week.

**What we''re looking for:**

- Professional experience in molecular & cellular biology techniques, experimental design & lab research, data analysis in life sciences
    
- Strong communication skills
    
- Ability to work independently in a remote environment
    

**How it works:**

This is not a specific job posting. By applying, you''re joining our Biologist talent network. 

- Apply once: Complete your profile by uploading your resume and confirming your work location.
    
- Get verified: We review your credentials and approve qualified experts.
    
- Stay connected: When projects need Biology expertise, we match you to opportunities based on your expertise and project needs.
    
- Start working: Be invited to interview for opportunities that align with your schedule and interests. You will earn competitive rates while working remotely on your own schedule.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Commitment: Part-Time', '["Molecular Biology", "Biologist Talent Network"]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Biologist Talent Network", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABnJ0CrCN6LLqupi9Bf6jc?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('aab2d5db-6b66-5b44-a667-0e5fc30ba369', 'Biology & Life Sciences Domain Expert', 'Mercor', 'Science', 'Remote (United States)', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$90 - $140/hr', '**Help define how frontier AI models reason about biology and the life sciences.**

## 1\. Overview

We are looking for senior biologists and life scientists to improve how frontier AI models reason about real life sciences research.

Your scientific judgment is the substance of this role. You will review the quality of life sciences reasoning tasks and model outputs, write the problem specifications and reference solutions that define what "correct" looks like, and design benchmarks that show whether a model is genuinely improving. We are looking for a practicing specialist rather than a generalist.

This role is fully remote.

## 2\. Key Responsibilities

- **Expert review:** Assess life sciences tasks and model outputs, catching mechanistic hand-waving, unsupported causal claims, flawed experimental design, and answers that read well but would not survive peer review.
- **Problem specs and reference solutions:** Write precise problem statements and rigorous reference solutions that reflect how life sciences research is actually done.
- **Benchmarks:** Design challenging, research-level problems and evaluation sets in your area of specialization.
- **Calibration:** Work with other researchers and experts in adjacent fields to turn tacit expert judgment into explicit, teachable criteria.

## 3\. Core Qualifications

- **Education:** PhD in biochemistry, molecular or cell biology, genetics, immunology, neuroscience, or a closely related life science.
- **Seniority:** A faculty appointment, principal investigator, staff or senior scientist, or an equivalent senior research role at a university, academic medical center, national laboratory, or research organization.
- **Domain depth:** Genuine specialization in at least one area, for example molecular and cell biology, biochemistry and structural biology, immunology, genetics and genomics, neuroscience, or ecology and evolution.
- **Research record:** A strong peer-reviewed publication record. Recognition such as competitive fellowships or awards is a plus.
- **AI fluency:** Hands-on use of large language models in your work, and the judgment to tell a sound argument from a plausible-sounding wrong one.
- **Communication:** Excellent written communication and the ability to give precise, well-structured feedback.
- **Location:** Based in the United States.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Commitment: Hourly
• Eligible Locations: USA', '["Biochemistry", "Molecular Biology"]', '["**Expert review:** Assess life sciences tasks and model outputs, catching mechanistic hand-waving, unsupported causal claims, flawed experimental design, and answers that read well but would not survive peer review.", "**Problem specs and reference solutions:** Write precise problem statements and rigorous reference solutions that reflect how life sciences research is actually done.", "**Benchmarks:** Design challenging, research-level problems and evaluation sets in your area of specialization.", "**Calibration:** Work with other researchers and experts in adjacent fields to turn tacit expert judgment into explicit, teachable criteria."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoYr3vuO4cXwvq0FKEZxq?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('be2dfc1f-bf04-586e-8993-9b4e2789da92', 'Biology Expert', 'Mercor', 'Science', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$70 - $105/hr', 'The research teams behind the best-known AI models come to Mercor for biology judgment they can''t generate on their own. Your standards and expertise become the rubric that frontier AI is graded against.

This is a standing listing for biologists who want AI training and evaluation work, not a specific job opening. It stays open whether or not a matching project is running this week.

New projects start on short notice, so instead of posting and pulling a listing each time, we keep one open per field and draw from it when one begins.

**What the work looks like**

We match biologists in the network to projects like:

- Writing a research problem from your own work, with the system, the data, and the controls, plus the reference answer a model''s attempt gets graded against
    
- Grading model-written experimental designs and interpretations: whether the controls rule out what they claim to, whether the statistics suit the design, whether the conclusion follows from the figure
    
- Flagging where a model gives a textbook-correct answer that would not survive at the bench, given the organism, the limits of the assay, or what the reagents can actually show
    

Past rates have run $70 to $105 an hour, set per project by scope and depth.

**What we''re looking for**

- A graduate degree in biology or a related life science, with research experience
    
- Clear written communication, since most of the work involves explaining your reasoning
    
- Comfort with ambiguous tasks, and willingness to flag unclear instructions
    

Where you trained matters less than whether you designed and ran the experiments yourself, recently enough to explain the calls you made.

**How it works**

Apply here with your resume and confirm where you work from, then take a short AI interview, about 20 minutes total.

We verify your background and add you to the biology pool.

When a project needs biology expertise, we invite matching people from the pool to that specific listing. It names the rate, the hours, and the client, and any hiring decision is made there.

**What to expect**

This listing does not accept or reject candidates, so you will not get a decision on it. We reach out when a project matches your background. Depending on what our clients are running, that can be within a week or several months.

Finishing the domain expert interview and joining every network you qualify for both improve your odds of being matched. You only need to sign up once to be eligible across all of them.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Expected Hours: 40 hrs/week
• Commitment: Part-Time', '["Molecular Biology"]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Biology Expert", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoKMjUBDgN45J6XxLf7pG?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('406304c3-772e-52ef-9f49-3cd98930eec2', 'Biotech Investment Analyst — Drug Asset & Company Assessment', 'Mercor', 'Healthcare', 'Remote — US-based or deep US-market experience', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$120 - $200/hr', 'Mercor is partnering with a biotech and pharma research team on expert human-evaluation work — creating and critiquing rubrics that analyze commercial drugs and drug-development programs. We''re seeking a biotech investment analyst (specialist-fund background) for a paid pilot, with the potential to continue as the work scales.

**Responsibilities**

- Create and critique rubrics that analyze commercial drugs and drug-development programs
    
- Provide overall company and asset assessment — mechanism, clinical data, competitive position, and value drivers
    
- Judge the quality of an investment-style thesis and flag weak, overconfident, or missing assumptions
    
- Apply your assessment across the pilot''s set of companies (~5–10)
    

**Requirements**

- US-based biotech / healthcare investment analyst with a specialist-fund background
    
