### Role Details & Eligibility
• Commitment: Part-Time', '["Chemist Talent Network"]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Chemist Talent Network", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABnJ0EyzP13xP26dJJXKpS?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('a9e7b945-485c-5554-9c68-6a71c1112a98', 'Chemistry Domain Expert', 'Mercor', 'Science', 'Remote (United States)', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$90 - $140/hr', '**Help define how frontier AI models reason about chemistry.**

## 1\. Overview

We are looking for senior chemists to improve how frontier AI models reason about real chemistry research.

Your scientific judgment is the substance of this role. You will review the quality of chemistry reasoning tasks and model outputs, write the problem specifications and reference solutions that define what "correct" looks like, and design benchmarks that show whether a model is genuinely improving. We are looking for a practicing specialist rather than a generalist.

This role is fully remote.

## 2\. Key Responsibilities

- **Expert review:** Assess chemistry tasks and model outputs, catching implausible mechanisms, infeasible reactions, stoichiometric and thermodynamic errors, misread spectra, and answers that read well but would not survive peer review.
- **Problem specs and reference solutions:** Write precise problem statements and rigorous reference solutions that reflect how research chemistry is actually done.
- **Benchmarks:** Design challenging, research-level problems and evaluation sets in your area of specialization.
- **Calibration:** Work with other researchers and experts in adjacent fields to turn tacit expert judgment into explicit, teachable criteria.

## 3\. Core Qualifications

- **Education:** PhD in chemistry, chemical engineering, or a closely related field.
- **Seniority:** A faculty appointment, principal investigator, staff or senior scientist, or an equivalent senior research role at a university, national laboratory, or research organization.
- **Domain depth:** Genuine specialization in at least one area, for example organic and synthetic chemistry, physical and computational chemistry, inorganic and materials chemistry, analytical chemistry, or chemical biology.
- **Research record:** A strong peer-reviewed publication record. Recognition such as competitive fellowships or awards is a plus.
- **AI fluency:** Hands-on use of large language models in your work, and the judgment to tell a sound argument from a plausible-sounding wrong one.
- **Communication:** Excellent written communication and the ability to give precise, well-structured feedback.
- **Location:** Based in the United States.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Commitment: Hourly
• Eligible Locations: USA', '["Molecular Biology"]', '["**Expert review:** Assess chemistry tasks and model outputs, catching implausible mechanisms, infeasible reactions, stoichiometric and thermodynamic errors, misread spectra, and answers that read well but would not survive peer review.", "**Problem specs and reference solutions:** Write precise problem statements and rigorous reference solutions that reflect how research chemistry is actually done.", "**Benchmarks:** Design challenging, research-level problems and evaluation sets in your area of specialization.", "**Calibration:** Work with other researchers and experts in adjacent fields to turn tacit expert judgment into explicit, teachable criteria."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoYr3mMPdrm41A5tHTK36?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('902aeaed-7da7-5248-9eb0-c97063e4864a', 'Chemistry Expert', 'Mercor', 'Science', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$65 - $105/hr', 'The research teams behind the best-known AI models come to Mercor for chemistry judgment they can''t generate on their own. Your standards and expertise become the rubric that frontier AI is graded against.

This is a standing listing for chemists who want AI training and evaluation work, not a specific job opening. It stays open whether or not a matching project is running this week.

New projects start on short notice, so instead of posting and pulling a listing each time, we keep one open per field and draw from it when one begins.

**What the work looks like**

We match chemists in the network to projects like:

- Writing a synthesis or characterization problem from your own work, with the substrate, the conditions, and the analytical data, plus the reference answer a model''s attempt gets graded against
    
- Grading model-proposed routes and mechanisms: whether the disconnection is sensible, whether the selectivity claim is supported, whether the spectra match the structure assigned
    
- Flagging where a model proposes something that works on paper and fails in the flask, given side reactivity, workup losses, or what the reagent tolerates
    

Past rates have run $65 to $105 an hour, set per project by scope and depth.

**What we''re looking for**

- A graduate degree in chemistry or a related field, with laboratory or computational research experience
    
- Clear written communication, since most of the work involves explaining your reasoning
    
- Comfort with ambiguous tasks, and willingness to flag unclear instructions
    

Where you trained matters less than whether you ran the reactions and interpreted the data yourself, recently enough to explain the calls you made.

**How it works**

Apply here with your resume and confirm where you work from, then take a short AI interview, about 20 minutes total.

We verify your background and add you to the chemistry pool.

When a project needs chemistry expertise, we invite matching people from the pool to that specific listing. It names the rate, the hours, and the client, and any hiring decision is made there.

**What to expect**

This listing does not accept or reject candidates, so you will not get a decision on it. We reach out when a project matches your background. Depending on what our clients are running, that can be within a week or several months.

Finishing the domain expert interview and joining every network you qualify for both improve your odds of being matched. You only need to sign up once to be eligible across all of them.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Expected Hours: 40 hrs/week
• Commitment: Part-Time', '[]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Chemistry Expert", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoKMjbmWSx1ImOhtE4p1n?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('7fa6ccc8-6c9b-51b7-9ca3-fa648c67dc81', 'Chemistry Specialist, Synthetic & Analytical Chemistry', 'Mercor', 'Science', 'Remote (London, UK / US East Coast)', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$70 - $100/hr', '**Join a leading AI lab''s cutting-edge research team to be at the core of the AI revolution, where your expertise fuels the development of the most advanced LLMs.**

# 1\. Overview

Join a leading AI lab''s cutting-edge research team and help build foundational AI models for science from the ground up. We''re seeking talented Chemistry subject-matter experts (SMEs), including synthetic, organic, medicinal, analytical and physical chemists from academia or industry, to bring deep, hands-on laboratory expertise to the design and evaluation of advanced AI models for chemistry.

This is a part-time position through Cincinnatus LLC (or an appropriate international entity), with the opportunity to be placed at a leading AI Lab as part of their extended workforce.

# 2\. Key Responsibilities

- Guide research and engineering teams to close knowledge gaps and improve AI model performance in synthetic chemistry, reaction mechanisms, structure elucidation, and physical-chemical property reasoning.
- Design challenging, non-searchable chemistry tasks, benchmarks and training data, and write accurate, well-structured solutions to problems such as multi-step route design, reaction optimization and spectroscopic characterization.
- Evaluate AI model outputs and step-by-step reasoning on chemistry tasks, diagnosing errors in chemical logic, tool usage and factual accuracy, and provide clear, written technical feedback.
- Develop specifications, grading rubrics and verification processes for chemistry data produced by external technical teams, and act as the domain authority on data quality.
- Advise on experimental design, common lab failure modes, and the chemical validity of model outputs, including molecular representations such as SMILES.
- Collaborate with other subject matter experts to ensure consistency and accuracy in training data.

# 3\. Core Qualifications

- PhD in chemistry (synthetic, organic, medicinal, analytical, physical or a closely related discipline), or equivalent research experience.
- 3+ years of hands-on chemistry experience at a recognized organization, such as a pharmaceutical, biotech, chemical or materials company, a contract research organization, or a university research group.
- Hands-on experience in small-molecule synthesis, including designing and running multi-step routes and optimizing reactions.
- Practical experience characterizing compounds with analytical techniques such as NMR, mass spectrometry, IR and HPLC / LC-MS, and interpreting the resulting data.
- Comfortable using cheminformatics and scientific AI tools (no coding required).
- Ability to engage reliably for at least 20 hours/week during weekdays.
- Strong written communication skills and the ability to explain complex technical decisions clearly.
- Nice to have: experience with cheminformatics representations (SMILES / SMARTS), writing grading rubrics, designing benchmarks, or evaluating scientific AI models or agents.

**About Cincinnatus LLC:**
Cincinnatus LLC is an enterprise staffing company that partners with leading technology companies to source and employ highly skilled professionals for contingent and contract-based opportunities. Cincinnatus, or an appropriate international entity, serves as the employer of record for these engagements, providing employment, payroll, benefits, and compliance, while placing employees directly within client teams to work on high-impact initiatives.

