• Expected Hours: 15 hrs/week
• Commitment: Part-Time', '["Clinical Medicine", "Disease", "Area Clinician", "Trial Endpoints & Prescribing"]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Disease-Area Clinician \u2014 Trial Endpoints & Prescribing", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABn9FsCZc6Mg0uj9hOSohQ?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('8f633548-c9ba-5e31-aff0-de759e2b3a6d', 'Drug Discovery Scientist', 'Mercor', 'Science', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$60 - $90/hr', '**About the role**

This is an evaluation framework for frontier AI models in drug research and development. Domain experts write realistic research problems wrapped around messy evidence worlds. The model works offline in a sandbox with open-source scientific tooling, receiving incomplete, indirect and sometimes misleading data, and must reach a defensible conclusion. The answer is present in the evidence but never stated.

Your job is to build a research problem so realistic and well-constructed that the model has to genuinely reason to solve it — it can''t pattern-match or look the answer up.

**What you''ll deliver**

Three things per task: the prompt, the data room, and the grading document.

1. **Design the challenge** — identify the hidden basin and the forcing chain that makes one conclusion inevitable.
    
2. **Build the world** — assemble a data room from real, source-grounded data. Every decisive value traces to a real source.
    
3. **Write the grader** — a grading document that scores a submitted memo on substance, not style or method.
    
4. **Validate it** — run verification and calibration before submission.
    
5. **Revise it** — you own the rework if a reviewer requests changes.
    

You are the final authority on every scientific and difficulty question in your task.

**Who we''re looking for**

- Working expertise in mechanistic enzymology, structure-guided peptide or antibody design, fragment-based discovery, or structure-based medicinal chemistry — PhD or equivalent industry track record.
    
- You can pose a problem whose answer you can defend rigorously, but which a strong solver cannot shortcut.
    
- Comfortable judging reasoning quality, not just final answers.
    

**Commitment**

Minimum 20 hours per week, up to 40.

**Tooling**

Work happens in a browser-based studio plus Claude Code. A Claude Max subscription is required and is fully reimbursed.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Expected Hours: 20 hrs/week
• Commitment: Hourly', '["Drug Discovery Scientist"]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Drug Discovery Scientist", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoFcXq-GdBUxvUuBByYMp?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
