• Eligible Locations: GBR, USA', '["Compliance", "Toxicology", "Biochemistry"]', '["Guide research and engineering teams to close knowledge gaps and improve AI model performance in mechanism of action, target and cellular pharmacology, ADME/Tox, and PK/PD.", "Design challenging, non-searchable drug discovery tasks, benchmarks and training data, and write accurate, well-structured solutions to problems such as interpreting assay readouts, identifying compound liabilities and planning optimization strategy.", "Evaluate AI model outputs and step-by-step reasoning on drug discovery tasks, diagnosing errors in scientific logic, tool usage and factual accuracy, and provide clear, written technical feedback.", "Develop specifications, grading rubrics and verification processes for drug discovery data produced by external technical teams, and act as the domain authority on data quality.", "Advise on assay design and quality control, experimental failure modes, and the biological and pharmacological validity of model outputs.", "Collaborate with other subject matter experts to ensure consistency and accuracy in training data."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoWVP2LVSRCNBUUlNs4H0?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
