INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('765ad5ad-da40-54cc-b845-cb43746bb952', 'Electrical Engineering Expert', 'Mercor', 'Finance', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$70 - $120/hr', 'The research teams behind the best-known AI models come to Mercor for electrical engineering judgment they can''t generate on their own. Your standards and expertise become the rubric that frontier AI is graded against.

This is a standing listing for electrical engineers who want AI training and evaluation work, not a specific job opening. It stays open whether or not a matching project is running this week.

New projects start on short notice, so instead of posting and pulling a listing each time, we keep one open per field and draw from it when one begins.

**What the work looks like**

We match electrical engineers in the network to projects like:

- Writing a circuit or systems problem from work you have done, with the specification, the constraints, and the operating conditions, plus the reference answer a model''s attempt gets graded against
    
- Grading model-written design and analysis: whether the topology suits the requirement, whether the noise and stability margins hold, whether the timing closes
    
- Flagging where a model''s design simulates cleanly and fails on a real board, given parasitics, tolerance stack-up, or interference
    

Past rates have run $70 to $120 an hour, set per project by scope and depth.

**What we''re looking for**

- A degree in electrical engineering, with professional design, test, or systems experience
    
- Clear written communication, since most of the work involves explaining your reasoning
    
- Comfort with ambiguous tasks, and willingness to flag unclear instructions
    

Where you trained matters less than whether you have debugged your own design on the bench and found out what the simulation missed.

**How it works**

Apply here with your resume and confirm where you work from, then take a short AI interview, about 20 minutes total.

We verify your background and add you to the electrical engineering pool.

When a project needs electrical engineering expertise, we invite matching people from the pool to that specific listing. It names the rate, the hours, and the client, and any hiring decision is made there.

**What to expect**

This listing does not accept or reject candidates, so you will not get a decision on it. We reach out when a project matches your background. Depending on what our clients are running, that can be within a week or several months.

Finishing the domain expert interview and joining every network you qualify for both improve your odds of being matched. You only need to sign up once to be eligible across all of them.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Expected Hours: 40 hrs/week
• Commitment: Part-Time', '[]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Electrical Engineering Expert", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoKMj8ATHeyLKYLFJq6Ox?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
