INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('8d798640-e41b-53b2-a71c-0120de0ec3ef', 'Investment Banking Expert', 'Mercor', 'Finance', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$100 - $130/hr', 'The research teams behind the best-known AI models come to Mercor for investment banking judgment they can''t generate on their own. Your standards and expertise become the rubric that frontier AI is graded against.

This is a standing listing for investment bankers who want AI training and evaluation work, not a specific job opening. It stays open whether or not a matching project is running this week.

New projects start on short notice, so instead of posting and pulling a listing each time, we keep one open per field and draw from it when one begins.

**What the work looks like**

We match bankers in the network to projects like:

- Building a three-statement model and an LBO from a filing set, then writing the rubric a grader uses to mark a model''s attempt wrong
- Reviewing model-generated comps and precedent transactions, and explaining where the multiple, the calendarization, or the peer set is off
- Grading model-drafted CIM and pitch material against what an MD would send, and writing the reasoning behind each deduction

Past rates have run $100 to $130 an hour, set per project by scope and depth.

**What we''re looking for**

- Professional experience in financial modeling, valuation, or deal execution
- Clear written communication, since most of the work involves explaining your reasoning
- Comfort with ambiguous tasks, and willingness to flag unclear instructions

**Where people in this pool have worked**

The most common backgrounds, though the pool is broader than this:

- Bulge bracket and elite boutique advisory: M&A, leveraged finance, restructuring, ECM/DCM
- Buy-side seats built on banking training: private equity, growth equity, private credit, distressed
- Corporate development and in-house M&A

The firm name matters less than whether you built the models and wrote the materials yourself, recently enough to explain the judgment calls behind them.

**How it works**

Apply here with your resume and confirm where you work from, then take a short AI interview, about 20 minutes total.

We verify your background and add you to the investment banking pool.

When a project needs investment banking expertise, we invite matching people from the pool to that specific listing. It names the rate, the hours, and the client, and any hiring decision is made there.

**What to expect**

This listing does not accept or reject candidates, so you will not get a decision on it. We reach out when a project matches your background. Depending on what our clients are running, that can be within a week or several months.

Finishing the domain expert interview and joining every network you qualify for both improve your odds of being matched. You only need to sign up once to be eligible across all of them.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Expected Hours: 40 hrs/week
• Commitment: Part-Time', '["Financial Analysis"]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Investment Banking Expert", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoKMhfQur1DCRx9tAD7Jq?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('e21e61d4-f86c-58d9-9d8e-0ba8810d3dee', 'Japanese Linguistic Experts', 'Mercor', 'Languages', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$50/hr', 'Mercor is seeking experienced Japanese Linguistic Experts to join a cutting-edge AI research project in partnership with a leading research lab. This role centers on evaluating how effectively a large language model (LLM) performs in Japanese-language tasks and on curating high-quality Japanese linguistic data to train and improve the model''s understanding and generation capabilities.

**Key Responsibilities:**

- Evaluate the quality and accuracy of LLM-generated Japanese text across various use cases (e.g., translation, summarization, dialogue, grammar correction).
    
- Edit, refine, or rewrite Japanese content to meet linguistic and cultural standards.
    
- Annotate Japanese text for grammatical, syntactic, and semantic features.
    
- Identify model errors and language gaps, and collaborate with AI researchers to improve LLM performance.
    
- Provide detailed linguistic feedback and analysis to guide ongoing model training efforts.
    

**You''re a strong fit if you have:**

- Native or near-native fluency in Japanese, with excellent command over grammar, syntax, and stylistics.
    
- Professional experience in translation, editing, linguistic annotation, or NLP data work in Japanese.
    
- Strong understanding of linguistic nuances, regional variations, and context-appropriate usage.
    
- Interest in AI and LLM-driven language technologies (preferred but not required).
    
- Excellent attention to detail and ability to spot subtle errors or unnatural phrasing.
    
- Clear communication skills and experience working in distributed, remote teams.
    

**Why Join**

- Contribute to cutting-edge AI research in partnership with a leading research lab.
    
- Work on high-impact projects that directly support the development of advanced AI systems.
    
- Gain hands-on exposure to state-of-the-art AI research and development.
    
- Join a fast-moving project where your expertise and judgment can have a meaningful impact.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Commitment: Part-Time', '["LLM Evaluation", "Translation"]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Japanese Linguistic Experts", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoXlytUOfloSDF6JPw4yP?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
