• Eligible Locations: USA', '["Python", "TypeScript"]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Kubernetes Task Auditor", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoEpy3lTX4ecyqy9GZ6_u?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('2a29f550-cee2-566c-aef2-0cabace2f083', 'LLM Research Scientist (Pre-training & Computer Vision & Adversarial Robustness)', 'Mercor', 'Science', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$100 - $120/hr', 'We''re looking for experienced machine learning researchers with hands-on experience training and improving deep learning models end-to-end, across vision and language. You''ll work on well-scoped empirical open-ended ML research problems.

## Responsibilities

- Train image classifiers and generative image models from scratch, and fine-tune open-weight language models.
- Get the most out of limited data, compute, and model-size budgets.
- Make models robust — to adversarial inputs and to adversarial conversations.
- Compress models to meet hard size and latency constraints without sacrificing accuracy.
- Diagnose and resolve training issues.

## Requirements

We are looking for candidates with strong expertise in one or more of the following areas:

**Adversarial Robustness**

Experience with:
- Adversarial training of image classifiers (e.g. PGD-based training, TRADES).
- Evaluating robust accuracy under standard threat models (e.g. L∞ attacks, AutoAttack) and avoiding gradient-masking pitfalls.
- Managing the robustness–accuracy trade-off and robust overfitting.

**Efficient Computer Vision**

Experience with:
- Training image classifiers end-to-end, especially for fine-grained recognition (many visually similar classes, few examples per class).
- Model compression: quantization, pruning, and knowledge distillation from large teachers into small students.
- Deploying models under hard size or latency budgets (on-device, edge, or embedded settings).

**Generative Image Modeling**

Experience with:
- Training image generative models from scratch: diffusion models, GANs, VAEs, or flow-based models.
- Iterating against sample-quality metrics such as FID.
- Training-efficiency tricks that produce good generators quickly and at small parameter counts.

**LLM Post-Training & Behavioral Robustness**

Hands-on experience with one or more of:
- Supervised fine-tuning and preference optimisation (DPO, RLHF, RLAIF) of open-weight language models, including building your own datasets via synthetic generation, noisy or weak supervision, and rejection sampling.
- Shaping conversational behaviour over multiple turns: resistance to persuasion and sycophancy, calibrated confidence, and knowing when to accept corrections.
- Alignment-style fine-tuning that changes a specific behaviour while preserving general capability.

**Multilingual Pre-training**

Experience with:
- Training multilingual or low-resource-language models from scratch.
- Tokenizer design across scripts and typologically diverse languages.
- Balancing highly unequal per-language data (sampling temperatures, cross-lingual transfer) in data-constrained regimes.

**Additional Areas of Interest**

Experience in any of the following is a plus:
- Scaling laws and training-efficiency research.
- Curriculum learning and data ordering.
- Model evaluation: benchmark construction, contamination control, statistically sound comparisons.
- Uncertainty estimation and model calibration.
- Data augmentation and synthetic data for robustness.

## General Qualifications

- 3+ years of machine learning research experience (PhD research counts toward this requirement).
- Strong experience with PyTorch, JAX, TensorFlow, or similar ML frameworks.
- Degree from a top-100 university, experience at a FAANG or comparable AI company, or an equivalent research track record through publications or impactful open-source contributions.

## Why Join

- Work on cutting-edge machine learning research.
- Collaborate with leading AI researchers on challenging, high-impact projects.
- Flexible, project-based work with competitive compensation.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Expected Hours: 40 hrs/week
• Commitment: Hourly', '["Machine Learning", "Deep Learning", "PyTorch", "LLM Evaluation", "RLHF"]', '["Train image classifiers and generative image models from scratch, and fine-tune open-weight language models.", "Get the most out of limited data, compute, and model-size budgets.", "Make models robust \u2014 to adversarial inputs and to adversarial conversations.", "Compress models to meet hard size and latency constraints without sacrificing accuracy.", "Diagnose and resolve training issues."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABn9G5kyvGTlH1jQZGvpVY?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('7d824589-e26f-5082-87ca-7fa3ab20af63', 'Language & Audio Expert', 'Mercor', 'Languages', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$35 - $50/hr', 'The research teams behind the best-known AI models come to Mercor for language and audio judgment they can''t generate on their own. Your standards and expertise become the rubric that frontier AI is graded against.

This is a standing listing for linguists, translators, and audio professionals who want AI training and evaluation work, not a specific job opening. It stays open whether or not a matching project is running this week.

New projects start on short notice, so instead of posting and pulling a listing each time, we keep one open per field and draw from it when one begins.

**What the work looks like**

We match people in this network to projects like:

- Writing prompts and reference answers in your language, with the register, idiom, and cultural context a model has to get right for the answer to read as native
- Grading model output in your language: whether a translation preserves meaning and tone, whether the grammar is idiomatic rather than merely correct, whether the register suits the speaker and the setting
- Judging voice, music, and sound work on whether it is clean, natural, and usable, and saying precisely what is wrong when it is not

Listings in this field on Mercor have posted at $35 to $50 an hour, set per project by scope, language, and depth.

**What we''re looking for**

- Native or professional fluency in at least one language, or professional experience in translation, voice, music, or audio production
- Clear written communication, since most of the work involves explaining your reasoning
- Comfort with ambiguous tasks, and willingness to flag unclear instructions

**What this covers**

This pool spans the language and audio field, including:

- Languages: Spanish, Arabic, English, Hindi, French, Portuguese, Italian, Chinese, Russian, Japanese, Korean, Polish, Tamil, Telugu, Kannada, Malayalam, Marathi, Assamese, Punjabi, Gujarati, Thai, Dutch, and Finnish
- Translation and interpretation
- Voice acting
- Music, audio engineering, and sound design

**How it works**

Apply here with your resume and confirm where you work from, then take a short AI interview, about 20 minutes total.

We verify your background and add you to the language and audio pool.

When a project needs your language or your specialty, we invite matching people from the pool to that specific listing. It names the rate, the hours, and the client, and any hiring decision is made there.

**What to expect**

This listing does not accept or reject candidates, so you will not get a decision on it. We reach out when a project matches your background. Depending on what our clients are running, that can be within a week or several months.

Finishing the domain expert interview and joining every network you qualify for both improve your odds of being matched. You only need to sign up once to be eligible across all of them.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Expected Hours: 40 hrs/week
• Commitment: Part-Time', '["Translation"]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Language & Audio Expert", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoKOPMUFnRCU8QMZBH634?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
