INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('051e8e16-d004-536e-989d-fb09b7687fa9', 'Legacy Codebase Migration Expert', 'Mercor', 'Healthcare', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$200/hr', 'Mercor is partnering with a **frontier AI research lab** to engage experienced software engineers with deep expertise in **legacy codebase migration and modernisation**. We are looking for engineers who have personally executed complex migrations across **large, production-grade systems**, particularly in **financial services, fintech/payments, insurance, healthcare, telecom, large technology companies, and other mission-critical enterprises**. Strong hands-on experience with production migrations is the primary qualification.

## What You''ll Do

- Design, implement, review, and evaluate complex **codebase migration and modernisation tasks**.
    
- Analyse legacy code, dependencies, APIs, databases, build systems, and infrastructure to determine safe migration approaches.
    
- Preserve **functionality, backwards compatibility, data integrity, security, and performance** during migrations.
    
- Develop tests and validation strategies to identify migration regressions and behavioural differences.
    
- Evaluate AI-generated migration solutions for **correctness, completeness, maintainability, and production readiness**.
    

## Relevant Migration Experience

Candidates should have deep expertise in **one or more** of the following:

- **Language/version:** Java 8 → 17/21, legacy .NET → modern .NET, Python 2 → 3, PHP 7 → 8
    
- **Language rewrites:** COBOL → Java/Python, JavaScript → TypeScript
    
- **Frameworks:** Angular, Rails, Django, Spring/Spring Boot, ASP.NET, Next.js/Astro, and other major framework upgrades/replacements
    
- **Databases & ORMs:** Oracle/MySQL → PostgreSQL, SQL → NoSQL, Hibernate → jOOQ, Sequelize → Prisma, raw SQL → ORM
    
- **Infrastructure:** VMs/bare metal → containers, Docker/Kubernetes, cloud-native architectures
    
- **CI/CD:** Jenkins/Travis → GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, or modern deployment pipelines
    
- **Build/package tooling:** Maven → Gradle, Webpack → Vite, CRA → Next.js, npm → pnpm
    
- **APIs:** REST → GraphQL, HTTP/REST → gRPC, SOAP/legacy APIs → modern interfaces
    
- **Authentication:** Legacy auth → OAuth/OIDC, SAML/SSO, modern identity and authorisation systems
    
- **Repositories:** Polyrepo → monorepo using Bazel, Nx, Turborepo, or similar
    
- **Testing:** Migration of unit, integration, browser, and E2E testing frameworks
    
- **Dependencies/SDKs:** Replacement of deprecated or EOL libraries, APIs, runtimes, and vendor SDKs
    

## Ideal Background

- **5+ years of professional software engineering experience**, ideally Senior, Staff, Principal, or equivalent.
    
- Personally owned or made substantial technical contributions to **large-scale production migrations**.
    
- Experience working with mature systems involving technical debt, complex dependencies, legacy integrations, and significant regression risk.
    
- Strong knowledge of **compatibility, testing, observability, staged rollouts, rollback strategies, and behavioural equivalence**.
    
- Ability to reason deeply about unfamiliar codebases and diagnose subtle migration failures.
    
- **Especially valuable:** engineers who have modernised **core banking, payments, trading, insurance, healthcare, telecom, or other high-reliability systems**.
    
- For **COBOL/mainframe modernisation, experience with technologies such as z/OS, CICS, JCL, DB2, VSAM, batch processing, and COBOL-to-Java/Python migrations** is particularly valuable.
    

## Why Join

- Apply your migration expertise to help shape how **frontier AI models understand and execute complex software modernisation**.
    
- Work on technically challenging problems modelled after **real-world, production-scale legacy systems**.
    
- Contribute expertise developed from large enterprise migrations without needing an open-source maintainer background.
    
- Opportunity for **ongoing work** as the research program expands.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Expected Hours: 40 hrs/week
• Commitment: Part-Time', '["Python", "JavaScript", "TypeScript", "SQL", "Docker"]', '["Design, implement, review, and evaluate complex **codebase migration and modernisation tasks**."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoCl905TW9jWTfs9Oh44S?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
