INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('27a9c93a-3162-55a2-945a-59b79d620a50', 'Mechanical Engineering Experts', 'Mercor', 'Coding', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$100 - $120/hr', '**Mercor is seeking experienced Mechanical Engineers** to support an advanced engineering and AI research initiative with a leading technology organisation. We are looking for deeply hands-on engineers who have designed, analysed, built, tested, validated, or troubleshot real-world mechanical and electromechanical systems in production environments.

Relevant backgrounds include:

- **Structural / Stress Engineering**
    
- **Thermal Engineering**
    
- **Mechanical Design Engineering**
    
- **Dynamics & Controls Engineering**
    

This role is particularly well suited for engineers who have worked directly on complex physical products and can bring practical engineering judgment to evaluating technical designs, analyses, testing workflows, failure modes, and real-world engineering problems.

### Key Responsibilities

- Apply hands-on mechanical engineering expertise to technically complex engineering tasks involving real physical systems and products.
    
- Review and evaluate mechanical designs, engineering analyses, simulation results, test methodologies, and troubleshooting approaches.
    
- Analyse engineering trade-offs involving **structures, materials, thermal performance, mechanical design, dynamics, vibration, controls, reliability, and manufacturability**.
    
- Assess the technical correctness and practical feasibility of engineering solutions generated for real-world mechanical engineering problems.
    
- Identify incorrect assumptions, unrealistic boundary conditions, design deficiencies, failure modes, and potential implementation or reliability risks.
    
- Develop or review technically rigorous engineering problems, reference solutions, evaluation criteria, and supporting technical documentation.
    
- Draw on practical experience with **design, simulation, prototyping, hardware integration, test, validation, qualification, debugging, and manufacturing**.
    
- Provide clear technical feedback grounded in real-world engineering experience and established engineering principles.
    

### You’re a Strong Fit If You Have

- **5+ years of professional mechanical engineering experience**, including at least **3 years of recent, actively hands-on experience** in hardware development, analysis, testing, validation, integration, bring-up, or troubleshooting—not solely program or people management.
    
- Demonstrated experience as the **responsible engineer for real hardware or physical systems**, owning meaningful portions of the engineering lifecycle from requirements and analysis through design, prototype development, testing, validation, qualification, and manufacturing readiness.
    
- Deep technical expertise in at least one core domain: **structural/stress analysis and FEA; thermal analysis, heat transfer, and thermal management; mechanical design and product development; or dynamics, vibration, mechanisms, and controls**.
    
- Strong practical command of **materials, loads and boundary conditions, structural margins, fatigue, thermal constraints, tolerances/GD&T, component selection, reliability, manufacturability, system integration, and engineering failure-mode analysis**.
    
- Extensive hands-on experience **analyzing, testing, debugging, and validating physical hardware**, using relevant engineering tools such as CAD/CAE, FEA, CFD/thermal simulation, dynamic or controls simulation, test instrumentation, data acquisition, and structured root-cause analysis.
    
- Proven experience developing hardware in **real-world product or manufacturing environments**, ideally across aerospace/defense, space, automotive/EV, semiconductors, consumer electronics, robotics/eVTOL, industrial/energy, or medical devices—e.g., **Lockheed Martin, RTX, Boeing, Blue Origin, Rocket Lab, Tesla, Rivian, NVIDIA, Qualcomm, Apple, Google, Meta, Skydio, Shield AI, Joby, Boston Dynamics, Siemens, GE Aerospace, ABB, Medtronic, or Intuitive Surgical**—with the ability to clearly explain technical decisions, design trade-offs, test results, and failure mechanisms.
    

### Preferred Background

Experience working for a company that **designs, builds, tests, and manufactures physical hardware products or systems** is strongly preferred. Relevant organisations may include, but are not limited to:

- **Aerospace & Defense:**
    Lockheed Martin, Northrop Grumman, RTX, Boeing, General Atomics, L3Harris, BAE Systems, General Dynamics, Honeywell Aerospace, Textron
    
- **Space:**
    Blue Origin, Rocket Lab, Relativity Space, Firefly Aerospace, Sierra Space, Astranis, Planet, Maxar, Axiom Space
    
- **Automotive & EV:**
    Tesla, Rivian, General Motors, Ford, Lucid, Waymo, Zoox, Aptiv, Bosch
    
- **Semiconductors:**
    NVIDIA, Qualcomm, Intel, Analog Devices, Texas Instruments, Broadcom, Marvell, Micron, NXP, Infineon
    
- **Consumer Electronics & Computing:**
