INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('1fb84123-7531-5c5c-bff3-103cfbf11d97', 'Nephrologist', 'Mercor', 'Healthcare', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$200/hr', 'Mercor is hiring board-certified nephrologists (MDs and DOs) to evaluate health AI models in partnership with a leading AI lab.

You will read de-identified patient charts and judge AI answers to clinical questions in nephrology.

**Key Responsibilities**

- Evaluate AI answers to nephrology questions for clinical accuracy, safety and alignment with current standards of care
- Check each answer against the patient chart and decide which of two responses is stronger
- Write structured rationales on clinical rigor, completeness and clarity
- Flag errors that could compromise patient safety

**Required Qualifications**

- **MD or DO** from an accredited medical school
- Board certified in **ABIM Nephrology** through an ABMS member board or the AOA
- Active, unrestricted US medical license
- Residency complete, plus fellowship where your specialty requires one
- **Currently practicing** and seeing patients in the US, with at least 1 year of independent practice after training
- 3+ years of post-training experience strongly preferred
- Clear written communication and close attention to detail

**Project Details**

- Remote and hourly, with flexible part-time hours
- Start date: immediate

**Application & Onboarding**

- Upload your resume
- Complete a 25-minute conversational interview on your background, experience and motivations
- Credential verification: license status, board certification, training and current practice setting
- Receive next steps and onboarding details within a few days

Apply today and put your clinical expertise to work shaping the health models clinicians and patients will rely on.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Expected Hours: 20 hrs/week
• Commitment: Hourly', '["Clinical Medicine", "Nephrologist"]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Nephrologist", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoWtwOLHV8_xCHd5M26Cl?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('81773dde-dad4-5508-be67-b79fece0b6a2', 'Network Engineer - Talent Network (Data for Autonomous Systems)', 'Mercor', 'Coding', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$50 - $70/hr', 'Are you a hands-on enterprise network engineer — Level 3 / Tier 3 support, network operations, or the person your team escalates to — interested in data science and autonomous infrastructure? Our client is building vertically integrated networking systems and using the data they generate to power the next generation of AI-driven infrastructure. They''re looking for engineers experienced in troubleshooting, escalations, packet analysis and RCA workflows to help label, annotate, and structure networking data from real production systems.

This is a hands-on role that blends your troubleshooting and incident-response experience with a growing understanding of how data pipelines are built and used in AI systems.

**About this talent network**

This is an ongoing talent network rather than a single open vacancy. Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis, and interview rounds run periodically as the client opens new headcount. Completing the technical practicum now means your profile is ready to be put forward as soon as the next round opens — there''s no need to reapply later.

**In this role, you''ll:**

- Review real-world data from deployed networks: logs, configs, telemetry, event streams

- Label and classify network behaviors, issues, anomalies, and incident patterns

- Help define schemas and structure for large-scale data pipelines that downstream ML models will train on

**Must have:**

- Hands-on experience operating enterprise production networks — switches, access points and firewalls — in end-customer environments such as retail, healthcare, financial, manufacturing, university or hospitality

- At least 5 years of experience in network engineering, network operations or network support roles

- Currently, or most recently, working in a hands-on network engineering, network operations or network support role

**Strongly preferred:**

- Experience as an escalation point for network incidents — Tier 3, final escalations, on-call rotation, RCAs, troubleshooting outages

- Hands-on enterprise Wi-Fi — WLAN controllers (Cisco WLC/9800, Aruba, or Meraki), 802.1X / RADIUS, and wireless troubleshooting

- Packet-level troubleshooting you do yourself — Wireshark, tcpdump, SPAN captures

- Exposure to a wide variety of network environments, vendors and customer types — whether through an MSP, VAR or systems integrator, or a single enterprise with a genuinely diverse estate

- Networks operated across multiple sites or a large campus environment

- Curiosity about how raw infrastructure data becomes machine learning input

This is a **maintainer** role — likely not the right fit if your current work is mainly network design/architecture, cloud/SRE, security/SOC, or IT helpdesk.

Your work will directly feed into the pipelines that power client''s AI models, and help shape how intelligent systems reason about networks in the real world.

**Here are more details about the role:**

- You will interface directly with the client team.

- You are expected to work 30-40 hours/week, with your hours overlapping the Pacific (PT) business day.

- This is an individual 1099 contract paid to a personal account — no corp-to-corp or agency billing.

- You must be authorized to work in the US or Canada without sponsorship. Please note this project cannot accommodate F-1 STEM OPT, as Mercor is unable to sign Form I-983. Standard F-1 OPT is fine.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Commitment: Part-Time
• Eligible Locations: CAN, USA
• Client Partner: Meter', '["Machine Learning", "Network Engineer", "Talent Network", "Data For Autonomous Systems"]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Network Engineer - Talent Network (Data for Autonomous Systems)", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoAA0CcB7r_IpsvtENYja?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
