INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('19541a1c-1e78-5270-b08c-b2ee575894ee', 'Office & Productivity Software Expert', 'Mercor', 'Finance', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$60 - $70/hr', 'The research teams behind the best-known AI models come to Mercor for judgment about how office and productivity software is actually used. Your standards and expertise become the rubric that frontier AI is graded against.

This is a standing listing for people who work in these tools all day and who want AI training and evaluation work, not a specific job opening. It stays open whether or not a matching project is running this week.

New projects start on short notice, so instead of posting and pulling a listing each time, we keep one open per field and draw from it when one begins.

**What the work looks like**

We match people in this network to projects like:

- Writing a realistic task from your own work, a document, a model, or a deck, with the starting material and the constraint, plus the reference answer a model''s attempt gets graded against
- Grading model-generated documents, spreadsheets, and slides: whether the formula is correct and robust, whether the formatting survives editing, whether the deck actually makes its argument
- Flagging where a model''s output opens cleanly and would break in real use, given file conversion, version compatibility, or what happens once someone else edits it

Listings in this field on Mercor have posted at $60 to $70 an hour, set per project by scope and depth.

**What we''re looking for**

- Professional experience working at a high level in office and productivity tools
- Clear written communication, since most of the work involves explaining your reasoning
- Comfort with ambiguous tasks, and willingness to flag unclear instructions

**What this covers**

This pool spans office and productivity software, including:

- Documents and word processing
- Spreadsheets and modeling
- Presentations and slides
- PDF and document conversion
- Email and collaboration tools
- Office scripting and add-ins

Depth in one tool matters more than passing familiarity with all of them.

**How it works**

Apply here with your resume and confirm where you work from, then take a short AI interview, about 20 minutes total.

We verify your background and add you to the office and productivity software pool.

When a project needs your tool or specialty, we invite matching people from the pool to that specific listing. It names the rate, the hours, and the client, and any hiring decision is made there.

**What to expect**

This listing does not accept or reject candidates, so you will not get a decision on it. We reach out when a project matches your background. Depending on what our clients are running, that can be within a week or several months.

Finishing the domain expert interview and joining every network you qualify for both improve your odds of being matched. You only need to sign up once to be eligible across all of them.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Expected Hours: 40 hrs/week
• Commitment: Part-Time', '[]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Office & Productivity Software Expert", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoKOQsxXSV5vKwxhGnL5Z?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('9ace69d3-5e67-5003-868a-208944402f14', 'Oncologist', 'Mercor', 'Healthcare', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$350 - $450/hr', '**1\. Role Overview**

Mercor is collaborating with a leading AI research lab on a project to advance frontier medical problem-solving in oncology. We are looking for oncologists based in the United States with hands-on clinical practice experience. The goal of this project is to identify gaps in AI model reasoning around real-world oncology cases, particularly in clinical trial design, patient eligibility, and treatment decision-making, and to support the training of cutting-edge AI models.

This is a short-term, high-impact, remote opportunity for oncologists excited about applying their clinical expertise to frontier AI research, with the possibility of extension based on performance.

**2\. Key Responsibilities**

- Create realistic, nuanced oncology tasks and scenarios, particularly around clinical trials, that expose weaknesses in frontier AI model responses
    
- Evaluate AI-generated clinical reasoning for accuracy, completeness, and alignment with current standard-of-care guidelines
    
- Identify flawed logic, missed diagnoses, incomplete treatment rationale, or unsafe recommendations in model outputs
    
- Provide clear, well-structured expert responses and chain-of-thought reasoning that reflect real clinical decision-making
    

**3\. Qualifications**

You are a **strong** fit for this project if you meet most or all of the following:

- MD or DO who is currently pursuing or has completed a fellowship in medical oncology or hematology/oncology
    
- Currently practicing in the United States and seeing oncology patients, or has done so within the past three years (3+ years of post-residency experience strongly preferred)
    
- Ability to articulate clinical reasoning clearly and precisely in written form


