INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('8719ef06-602b-5536-9569-437e4d09bbe1', 'Physics Domain Expert', 'Mercor', 'Science', 'Remote (United States)', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$90 - $140/hr', '**Help define how frontier AI models reason about physics.**

## 1\. Overview

We are looking for senior physicists to improve how frontier AI models reason about real physics research.

Your scientific judgment is the substance of this role. You will review the quality of physics reasoning tasks and model outputs, write the problem specifications and reference solutions that define what "correct" looks like, and design benchmarks that show whether a model is genuinely improving. We are looking for a practicing specialist rather than a generalist.

This role is fully remote.

## 2\. Key Responsibilities

- **Expert review:** Assess physics tasks and model outputs, catching flawed derivations, unjustified approximations, dimensional and limit errors, and answers that read well but would not survive peer review.
- **Problem specs and reference solutions:** Write precise problem statements and rigorous reference solutions that reflect how research physics is actually done.
- **Benchmarks:** Design challenging, research-level problems and evaluation sets in your area of specialization.
- **Calibration:** Work with other researchers and experts in adjacent fields to turn tacit expert judgment into explicit, teachable criteria.

## 3\. Core Qualifications

- **Education:** PhD in physics, astrophysics, applied physics, or a closely related field.
- **Seniority:** A faculty appointment, principal investigator, staff or senior scientist, or an equivalent senior research role at a university, national laboratory, or research organization.
- **Domain depth:** Genuine specialization in at least one area, for example condensed matter, high-energy or particle physics, astrophysics and cosmology, atomic, molecular, optical and quantum physics, or statistical and computational physics.
- **Research record:** A strong peer-reviewed publication record. Recognition such as competitive fellowships or awards is a plus.
- **AI fluency:** Hands-on use of large language models in your work, and the judgment to tell a sound argument from a plausible-sounding wrong one.
- **Communication:** Excellent written communication and the ability to give precise, well-structured feedback.
- **Location:** Based in the United States.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Commitment: Hourly
• Eligible Locations: USA', '[]', '["**Expert review:** Assess physics tasks and model outputs, catching flawed derivations, unjustified approximations, dimensional and limit errors, and answers that read well but would not survive peer review.", "**Problem specs and reference solutions:** Write precise problem statements and rigorous reference solutions that reflect how research physics is actually done.", "**Benchmarks:** Design challenging, research-level problems and evaluation sets in your area of specialization.", "**Calibration:** Work with other researchers and experts in adjacent fields to turn tacit expert judgment into explicit, teachable criteria."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoYr3SG3-4yi5ct9Bgp3k?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('7f14431b-c33e-541c-a43a-69454559f273', 'Physics Expert', 'Mercor', 'Science', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$70 - $100/hr', 'The research teams behind the best-known AI models come to Mercor for physics judgment they can''t generate on their own. Your standards and expertise become the rubric that frontier AI is graded against.

This is a standing listing for physicists who want AI training and evaluation work, not a specific job opening. It stays open whether or not a matching project is running this week.

New projects start on short notice, so instead of posting and pulling a listing each time, we keep one open per field and draw from it when one begins.

**What the work looks like**

We match physicists in the network to projects like:

- Writing a problem from your own area, with the system, the assumptions, and the regime, plus the reference answer a model''s attempt gets graded against
    
- Grading model-written derivations and numerical work: whether the approximation is valid in the regime claimed, whether the limiting cases check out, whether the units and scaling survive scrutiny
    
- Flagging where a model reaches the right final expression through reasoning that would not hold if the assumptions changed
    

Past rates have run $70 to $100 an hour, set per project by scope and depth.

**What we''re looking for**

- A graduate degree in physics or a related field, with research experience
    
- Clear written communication, since most of the work involves explaining your reasoning
    
- Comfort with ambiguous tasks, and willingness to flag unclear instructions
    

Where you trained matters less than whether you did the derivations and the analysis yourself, recently enough to explain the calls you made.

**How it works**

Apply here with your resume and confirm where you work from, then take a short AI interview, about 20 minutes total.

We verify your background and add you to the physics pool.

When a project needs physics expertise, we invite matching people from the pool to that specific listing. It names the rate, the hours, and the client, and any hiring decision is made there.

**What to expect**

This listing does not accept or reject candidates, so you will not get a decision on it. We reach out when a project matches your background. Depending on what our clients are running, that can be within a week or several months.

Finishing the domain expert interview and joining every network you qualify for both improve your odds of being matched. You only need to sign up once to be eligible across all of them.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Expected Hours: 40 hrs/week
• Commitment: Part-Time', '[]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Physics Expert", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoKMjqUMNbxdYam1EnL82?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('9ea56a97-5039-52d6-8a4e-1ee0add6a1da', 'Portuguese Linguistic Experts', 'Mercor', 'Languages', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$50/hr', 'Mercor is seeking experienced Portuguese Linguistic Experts to join a cutting-edge AI research project in partnership with a leading research lab. This role centers on evaluating how effectively a large language model (LLM) performs in Portuguese-language tasks and on curating high-quality Portuguese linguistic data to train and improve the model''s understanding and generation capabilities.

**Key Responsibilities:**

