INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('854abe6a-16d4-5756-ac6b-eebd7dd8e884', 'Software Engineering Expert', 'Mercor', 'Finance', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$70 - $150/hr', 'The research teams behind the best-known AI models come to Mercor for software engineering judgment they can''t generate on their own. Your standards and expertise become the rubric that frontier AI is graded against.

This is a standing listing for engineers who want AI training and evaluation work, not a specific job opening. It stays open whether or not a matching project is running this week.

New projects start on short notice, so instead of posting and pulling a listing each time, we keep one open per field and draw from it when one begins.

**What the work looks like**

We match engineers in the network to projects like:

- Writing an engineering problem from a system you have shipped, with the requirements, the constraints, and the failure modes, plus the reference answer a model''s attempt gets graded against
- Grading model-written code and design: whether it handles the edge cases, whether the complexity is justified, whether the test actually exercises the behaviour it claims to
- Flagging where a model''s code passes review and would fail in production, given concurrency, scale, error handling, or what it costs to operate

Software engineering listings on Mercor have posted at $70 to $150 an hour, set per project by scope and depth.

**What we''re looking for**

- Professional experience building and shipping software
- Clear written communication, since most of the work involves explaining your reasoning
- Comfort with ambiguous tasks, and willingness to flag unclear instructions

**What this covers**

This pool spans software engineering, including:

- Frontend (React, TypeScript, Next.js); backend (Java, Go, Node.js); full-stack
- Mobile (Android, iOS); embedded and IoT
- DevOps and platform engineering; systems and performance engineering
- QA and automation; security engineering

Where you trained matters less than whether you have owned code in production and dealt with what it did there.

**How it works**

Apply here with your resume and confirm where you work from, then take a short AI interview, about 20 minutes total.

We verify your background and add you to the software engineering pool.

When a project needs your stack or specialty, we invite matching people from the pool to that specific listing. It names the rate, the hours, and the client, and any hiring decision is made there.

**What to expect**

This listing does not accept or reject candidates, so you will not get a decision on it. We reach out when a project matches your background. Depending on what our clients are running, that can be within a week or several months.

Finishing the domain expert interview and joining every network you qualify for both improve your odds of being matched. You only need to sign up once to be eligible across all of them.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Expected Hours: 40 hrs/week
• Commitment: Part-Time', '["TypeScript", "React", "Node.js"]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Software Engineering Expert", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoKOP6g9ZUjU9LdNBCqS7?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('f838c3d4-bb2b-537d-8909-597fffcc1868', 'Source Security Specialist', 'Mercor', 'Science', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$75/hr', '## About the work

Mercor is assembling a panel of radiological safety experts to red-team frontier AI models. The goal is to test whether a model can correctly judge the misuse potential of a technical request — answering legitimate questions fully while refusing genuinely dangerous ones.

You will:

- Write challenging single-turn prompts in your domain, labelled across three levels: benign, dual-use, and adversarial.
- Evaluate the responses that come back against a defined policy standard, and judge whether each was handled correctly.
- Write the reference answer — what a correct response looks like, and the technical reasoning for why.

This domain lives on the dual-use line more than most. The same isotope underpins cancer therapy and industrial radiography; the same shielding calculation protects a worker and conceals a source. A model that refuses a routine dose question is failing as badly as one that answers a question it shouldn''t. Drawing that line reliably is why we need practitioners rather than generalists.

## Background we''re looking for

We''re looking for people who have assessed how Category 1 and 2 sources actually get stolen, shielded or moved — the security and vulnerability side of a licensed programme, not just its paperwork. What matters most is being able to tell a routine professional question from one that''s fishing for something else: the same shielding calculation protects a worker and conceals a source. You will be writing prompts that sit exactly on that line, then judging whether the model held it.

Examples of relevant backgrounds (ideally with red-teaming experience):

- Security or vulnerability assessment of licensed facilities holding Category 1 and 2 sources
- Physical protection design and review — detect, delay, assess and respond; insider threat considerations
- Source recovery, consolidation or security-upgrade programmes for disused and orphan sources
- Regulatory security inspection and compliance — 10 CFR 37 or national equivalents
- Transport security for radioactive material — routing, escort, tracking and chain of custody

## What this role demands beyond technical depth

This is writing-intensive work. Every judgment you make needs a written rationale that a non-specialist can follow. Prior technical writing, published research, or expert witness experience is a strong signal; please include a sample or link. You will also be reading and writing about misuse scenarios in your field for sustained periods. We brief experts on this in advance, and you can pause or step away at any point without penalty.

## Before you apply

Your work here will not involve, and must not draw on, classified or export-controlled information, or anything covered by an NDA or prepublication review obligation. If you hold such obligations you may still be a good fit; tell us in your application and we will scope the work accordingly.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Commitment: Task-Based
• Client Partner: Neon', '["Cybersecurity", "Compliance"]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Source Security Specialist", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoKHZlukvTP7GqdNK4phe?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
