INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('fbdf3de8-625d-557c-8936-ea0a28e39bd6', 'Specialty Materials Chemist — Pyrotechnics or Propulsion', 'Mercor', 'Science', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$75/hr', '## About the work

Mercor is assembling a panel of energetic materials and propulsion experts to red-team frontier AI models. The goal is to test whether a model can correctly judge the misuse potential of a technical request — answering legitimate questions fully while refusing genuinely dangerous ones.

You will:

- Write challenging single-turn prompts in your domain, labelled across three levels: benign, dual-use, and adversarial.
- Evaluate the responses that come back against a defined policy standard, and judge whether each was handled correctly.
- Write the reference answer — what a correct response looks like, and the technical reasoning for why.

This domain lives on the dual-use line more than most. The same formulation work that qualifies a propellant or a display composition sits next to something nobody should be helped with; the same sensitivity data that protects a production line reads as a specification from the other side. A model that refuses a routine thermal-stability question is failing as badly as one that answers a question it shouldn''t. Drawing that line reliably is why we need practitioners rather than generalists.

## Background we''re looking for

This is the chemistry half of the domain: we''re looking for people who have formulated, synthesised and tested specialty energetic materials in a licensed or government facility, not modelled them from a distance. What matters most is being able to tell a routine professional question from one that''s fishing for something else: the same sensitivity result that sets a safe handling limit is what someone else would want to design around. You will be writing prompts that sit exactly on that line, then judging whether the model held it.

Examples of relevant backgrounds (ideally with red-teaming experience):

- Formulation chemist for pyrotechnics, propellants or specialty energetic materials
- Synthesis and characterisation of energetic compounds in a licensed or government facility
- Performance and sensitivity testing — calorimetry, thermal stability, small-scale safety testing
- Scale-up and process safety for energetic material production
- Solid or liquid rocket propellant development — binders, oxidisers, burn-rate modifiers

## What this role demands beyond technical depth

This is writing-intensive work. Every judgment you make needs a written rationale that a non-specialist can follow. Prior technical writing, published research, or expert witness experience is a strong signal; please include a sample or link. You will also be reading and writing about misuse scenarios in your field for sustained periods. We brief experts on this in advance, and you can pause or step away at any point without penalty.

## Before you apply

Your work here will not involve, and must not draw on, classified or export-controlled information, or anything covered by an NDA or prepublication review obligation. If you hold such obligations you may still be a good fit; tell us in your application and we will scope the work accordingly.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Commitment: Task-Based
• Client Partner: Neon', '["Specialty Materials Chemist", "Pyrotechnics Or Propulsion"]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Specialty Materials Chemist \u2014 Pyrotechnics or Propulsion", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoKHb4faM2SbEMuFOMK3h?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('11455129-542c-53dc-b6d1-aaa95deda99d', 'Stanford Youth Study — US Parents & Kids (Age 9–13)', 'Mercor', 'Data Annotation & RLHF', 'Remote (United States)', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$110/hr', 'Mercor is recruiting participants for the **Youth Well-being Project**, a research study led by **Stanford University** in collaboration with **Bocconi University**, focused on how smartphones and digital tools affect children and families.

**📋 Applications are open now.** We''re accepting applications at this stage to **finalize and confirm participants for the upcoming batch, which begins in January.** Apply now to lock in your spot — selected applicants will have their place confirmed ahead of the January start.

## ✅ Who can take part — please read carefully

- You are a **parent/guardian based in the United States**
- You have a **child aged 9–13**
- **Your child has their own smartphone with an active SIM card** (a working phone number). This is **required** — the study involves installing an app on the child''s phone, so a tablet, Wi‑Fi‑only device, or a phone without a SIM will not qualify.
- You and your child are **willing to take part together**

*You can pick one child to take part with you — one child per household.*

## What you''ll be asked to do

- Complete a few short online surveys plus occasional text-message check-ins across the study
- Install a parental-control app on your child''s phone and keep it installed for the study period
- Your child completes two short online surveys and a few text-message check-ins

## Engagement details

- **Start:** January (applications are being finalized now)
- **Format:** Remote — online surveys + short text-message check-ins
- **Time commitment:** The study runs over **~8 weeks**. Active time is light — the surveys are short and the app simply stays installed on your child''s phone during that period, with a few quick check-ins along the way
- **Compensation:** A flat fee of $110, paid once on completion
- **Participation:** One child per household

## Why participate

- Contribute to Stanford + Bocconi research on children''s well-being in the digital age
- Help parents make more informed decisions about technology
- Flexible, remote participation


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Commitment: Part-Time
• Eligible Locations: USA
• Client Partner: Stanford Research', '["Age 9"]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Stanford Youth Study \u2014 US Parents & Kids (Age 9\u201313)", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABn6i483EoSNpFPh1PSKFO?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('211db14b-a284-59d6-97dc-a2698f3d6abb', 'Survey Research & Consumer Insights Expert', 'Mercor', 'Data Annotation & RLHF', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$120/hr', 'Mercor is partnering with a leading AI research organisation to engage experienced professionals in survey research, market research, consumer insights, and behavioural science for a project focused on evaluating and improving sophisticated survey-based research. We are looking for individuals who have **professionally designed, fielded, managed, or evaluated surveys** and understand what separates a rigorous, decision-useful survey from one that produces noisy, biased, or misleading results. This opportunity is intentionally open to professionals from a range of research backgrounds. Candidates do **not** need to be academic survey methodologists; strong practitioners from market research agencies, consumer insights teams, behavioural science organisations, polling/research firms, or in-house research functions are highly encouraged to apply.

## What You’ll Do

- Review and evaluate surveys for methodological quality, clarity, and fitness for purpose.
    
- Assess survey questions for issues such as **leading language, ambiguity, double-barreled questions, response-option problems, ordering effects, and respondent burden**.
    
- Evaluate screeners, eligibility criteria, survey flows, skip/display logic, scales, and questionnaire structure.
    
- Identify potential sources of **sampling, measurement, response, and selection bias**.
    
- Assess whether surveys are likely to generate reliable and interpretable data from the intended respondent population.
    
- Review approaches to survey fielding, respondent recruitment, quotas, sample composition, and data-quality controls.
    
- Apply practical research judgment to ambiguous survey-design problems where there may not be a single objectively correct answer.
    
- Provide clear, structured rationales explaining methodological issues and recommended improvements.
    
- Help evaluate AI-generated survey content and research reasoning against professional research standards.
    

## What We’re Looking For

We are open to candidates from several backgrounds, including:

- **Market Research / Consumer Insights:** Professionals who have designed and fielded quantitative surveys at market research firms, insights consultancies, research agencies, or internal consumer/customer insights teams.
    
- **Survey Methodology:** Survey researchers or methodologists with deep expertise in questionnaire design, sampling, measurement, fieldwork, or survey statistics.
    
- **Behavioural Science: Researchers who have used surveys, experiments, or structured questionnaires as a meaningful part of applied behaviou**ral research.
    
- **UX / Customer Research:** Quantitative or mixed-methods researchers with substantial hands-on survey design and fielding experience.
    
- **Polling / Social Research:** Professionals experienced in public opinion, political, social, policy, or population-based survey research.
    

## Ideal Qualifications

- 3+ years of professional experience in **survey research, market research, consumer insights, behavioural science, UX research, or a closely related field**.
    
- Meaningful hands-on experience **designing and/or fielding surveys professionally**.
    
- Strong understanding of questionnaire design and common sources of survey error and bias.
    
- Experience working with respondent panels, sampling strategies, screeners, quotas, or survey fieldwork is highly valuable.
    
- Ability to critically evaluate survey methodology rather than execute a predefined questionnaire.
    
- Strong written communication skills and the ability to explain _why_ a survey design decision is methodologically strong or weak.
    
- High attention to detail and comfort making nuanced judgments with incomplete or ambiguous information.
    
- Experience with platforms such as **Qualtrics, SurveyMonkey, Alchemer, Decipher/Forsta, QuestionPro, or similar research tools** is helpful but not required.
    

## Particularly Strong Profiles

Strong candidates may include **Senior Research Managers, Consumer Insights Managers, Market Research Managers, Survey Researchers, Survey Methodologists, Quantitative Researchers, Behavioural Scientists, Insights Consultants, Research Directors, UX Researchers, or Research Scientists**. Experience at established market research and insights organisations, research-intensive technology or consumer companies, academic survey centres, behavioural science organisations, or polling/social research institutions is especially relevant.

## Why Join

- Apply professional research expertise to cutting-edge AI research.
    
- Work on problems that require genuine methodological judgment rather than routine survey administration.
    
- Help improve how advanced AI systems understand **survey design, research methodology, respondent behaviour, and evidence quality**.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Expected Hours: 40 hrs/week
• Commitment: Hourly', '["Market Research"]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Survey Research & Consumer Insights Expert", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoGvWRUT2estOlP9J4o1I?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('948fcea2-59c5-5399-9552-309ffdead4ec', 'Synthetic / Process Chemist', 'Mercor', 'Science', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$75/hr', '## About the work

Mercor is assembling a panel of chemistry and chemical safety experts to red-team frontier AI models. The goal is to test whether a model can correctly judge the misuse potential of a technical request — answering legitimate questions fully while refusing genuinely dangerous ones.

You will:

- Write challenging single-turn prompts in your domain, labelled across three levels: benign, dual-use, and adversarial.
- Evaluate the responses that come back against a defined policy standard, and judge whether each was handled correctly.
- Write the reference answer — what a correct response looks like, and the technical reasoning for why.

This domain lives on the dual-use line more than most. The same route design that scales a medicine underpins a controlled compound; the same impurity profile that proves a clean process identifies how something was made. A model that refuses a routine scale-up or kinetics question is failing as badly as one that answers a question it shouldn''t. Drawing that line reliably is why we need practitioners rather than generalists.

## Background we''re looking for

We''re looking for chemists who have actually run routes and scaled them — bench to pilot to plant — and who know which requests are ordinary process chemistry and which are asking for something else. What matters most is being able to tell a routine professional question from one that''s fishing for something else: the same route knowledge that shortens a synthesis serves whoever is shortening it. You will be writing prompts that sit exactly on that line, then judging whether the model held it.

Examples of relevant backgrounds (ideally with red-teaming experience):

- Synthetic route design and development in pharmaceutical, agrochemical or fine chemicals
- Process chemistry and reaction engineering — optimisation, kinetics, impurity control
- Scale-up from bench to pilot to plant, with the safety review that goes with it
- Precursor sourcing, controlled-substance registration or regulatory chemistry
- Method development and troubleshooting in a GMP or equivalent quality environment

## What this role demands beyond technical depth

This is writing-intensive work. Every judgment you make needs a written rationale that a non-specialist can follow. Prior technical writing, published research, or expert witness experience is a strong signal; please include a sample or link. You will also be reading and writing about misuse scenarios in your field for sustained periods. We brief experts on this in advance, and you can pause or step away at any point without penalty.

## Before you apply

Your work here will not involve, and must not draw on, classified or export-controlled information, or anything covered by an NDA or prepublication review obligation. If you hold such obligations you may still be a good fit; tell us in your application and we will scope the work accordingly.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Commitment: Task-Based
• Client Partner: Neon', '["Chemical Safety", "Clinical Medicine"]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Synthetic / Process Chemist", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoKHdHDCST78SsOhLs7Pk?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('f80554cd-1b55-5f85-8654-de869cd870e5', 'Systems & Integration Engineering Experts', 'Mercor', 'Coding', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$100 - $120/hr', '**Mercor is seeking experienced Systems & Integration Engineers** to support an advanced engineering and AI research initiative with a leading technology organization. We are looking for deeply hands-on engineers who have integrated, tested, validated, debugged, qualified, or analyzed complex real-world hardware and electromechanical systems in production environments.

Relevant backgrounds include:

- **Systems Engineering**
    
- **Integration & Test Engineering**
    
- **Reliability / Failure Analysis Engineering**
    
- **Manufacturing Test Engineering**
    

This role is particularly well suited for engineers who have worked directly on complex physical products and can bring practical engineering judgment to system integration, verification and validation, reliability, root-cause analysis, manufacturing test, and cross-functional hardware troubleshooting.

### Key Responsibilities

- Apply hands-on systems, integration, reliability, and test engineering expertise to technically complex problems involving real physical products and hardware systems.
    
- Review and evaluate **system requirements, interfaces, integration plans, verification strategies, test procedures, qualification approaches, reliability analyses, and manufacturing test workflows**.
    
- Analyze system-level interactions across **electrical, mechanical, firmware/software, thermal, controls, and manufacturing domains**.
    
- Assess the technical correctness and practical feasibility of engineering solutions, test strategies, troubleshooting approaches, and system-level decisions.
    
- Diagnose integration failures and identify **root causes, interface issues, design deficiencies, reliability risks, manufacturing defects, and test coverage gaps**.
    
- Develop or review technically rigorous engineering problems, reference solutions, test cases, verification criteria, failure analyses, and technical documentation.
    
- Draw on practical experience with **prototype integration, bring-up, verification and validation, qualification, environmental testing, reliability testing, production test, and field failure investigation**.
    
- Provide clear technical feedback grounded in real-world hardware development, testing, and production experience.
    

### You’re a Strong Fit If You Have

- **5+ years of professional systems, integration, reliability, or test engineering experience**, including at least **3 years of recent, actively hands-on experience** with hardware integration, test, validation, qualification, failure analysis, manufacturing test, or troubleshooting—not solely program or people management.
    
- Demonstrated experience as the **responsible engineer for complex physical systems or hardware products**, owning meaningful portions of the lifecycle from requirements and interface definition through integration, verification, qualification, production readiness, and field support.
    
- Deep technical expertise in at least one core domain: **systems engineering and requirements/V&V; hardware integration and test; reliability engineering and failure analysis; or manufacturing/production test engineering**.
    
- Strong practical command of **requirements traceability, interface management, verification and validation, test planning, FMEA/FMECA, fault isolation, root-cause analysis, reliability, qualification, environmental testing, design-for-test, manufacturing yield, and system-level failure modes**, as applicable to the candidate''s specialization.
    
- Extensive hands-on experience **integrating, instrumenting, testing, debugging, and characterizing physical hardware**, using relevant laboratory equipment, data-acquisition systems, automated test infrastructure, environmental test equipment, diagnostic tools, and structured failure-analysis methodologies.
    
- Proven experience developing and validating hardware in **real-world product or manufacturing environments**, ideally across aerospace/defense, space, automotive/EV, semiconductors, consumer electronics, robotics/eVTOL, industrial/energy, or medical devices—e.g., **Lockheed Martin, RTX, Boeing, Blue Origin, Rocket Lab, Tesla, Rivian, NVIDIA, Qualcomm, Intel, Apple, Google, Meta, Skydio, Shield AI, Joby, Boston Dynamics, Siemens, GE Aerospace, ABB, Medtronic, or Intuitive Surgical**—with the ability to clearly explain system decisions, integration trade-offs, test results, root causes, and failure mechanisms.
    

### Preferred Background

Experience working for a company that **designs, builds, integrates, tests, and manufactures complex physical hardware systems** is strongly preferred. Relevant organizations may include, but are not limited to:

- **Aerospace & Defense:**
    Lockheed Martin, Northrop Grumman, RTX, Boeing, General Atomics, L3Harris, BAE Systems, General Dynamics, Honeywell Aerospace, Textron
    
- **Space:**
    Blue Origin, Rocket Lab, Relativity Space, Firefly Aerospace, Sierra Space, Astranis, Planet, Maxar, Axiom Space
    
- **Automotive & EV:**
    Tesla, Rivian, General Motors, Ford, Lucid, Waymo, Zoox, Aptiv, Bosch
    
- **Semiconductors:**
    NVIDIA, Qualcomm, Intel, Analog Devices, Texas Instruments, Broadcom, Marvell, Micron, NXP, Infineon
    
- **Consumer Electronics & Computing:**
    Apple, Google Hardware, Meta Reality Labs, Microsoft Devices, Amazon, Samsung, Garmin, Sonos
    
- **Drones, eVTOL & Robotics:**
    Skydio, Shield AI, Zipline, Joby Aviation, Archer Aviation, Boston Dynamics, Figure, Agility Robotics, Wing
    
- **Industrial, Energy & Medical Devices:**
    Siemens, GE Aerospace, GE Vernova, ABB, Schneider Electric, Rockwell Automation, Enphase, Medtronic, Intuitive Surgical
    

Candidates from comparable hardware-focused organizations are equally encouraged to apply.

### Why Join

- Apply your systems and integration expertise to technically challenging problems at the intersection of **advanced hardware engineering and AI research**.
    
- Work on projects where practical experience with **real hardware integration, verification, reliability, failure analysis, and production testing** is highly valued.
    
- Help improve how advanced AI systems reason about **complex systems, interfaces, verification and validation, troubleshooting, reliability, manufacturing, and hardware failures**.
    
- Contribute remotely with flexible engagement structures alongside experienced engineers and researchers.
    
- Work on problems requiring genuine engineering judgment and hands-on industry experience rather than purely theoretical systems knowledge.


