INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('fb5456d0-3501-5aa6-8930-77aa97e349fd', 'VFX & Compositing Supervisor', 'Mercor', 'Data Annotation & RLHF', 'Remote (United States)', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$70 - $110/hr', '**Join a leading AI lab''s cutting-edge GenAI team to be at the core of the AI revolution, where your expertise fuels the development of the most advanced AI models.**

# 1\. Overview

A leading AI lab is building generative video models that aim for feature-quality visual effects and preproduction: micro detail, physically plausible simulation, clean multi-layer integration, previs and concept art, carried into a new output. We''re looking for experienced VFX and compositing supervisors, FX and CG specialists, previs supervisors and concept artists to help define what excellent VFX work looks like, and to judge where the models get it right or wrong. This is a full-time role of approximately 40 hours per week.

This is a W-2 employment position with Cincinnatus LLC, with the opportunity to be placed at a leading AI Lab as part of their extended workforce.

# 2\. Key Responsibilities

- **Set the quality bar:** Define clear standards and an artifact taxonomy for micro detail, multi-layer integration, physics, previs and concept art, and critique current evaluations.
- **Curate benchmarks:** Identify, generate and curate strong examples of excellent and genuinely hard VFX, simulation, previs and concept work, and test early model capabilities against them.
- **Critique model outputs:** Review generated footage frame by frame and write precise, actionable notes on temporal instability, compositing seams, spill, physics and fine detail.
- **Shape the reviewer pool and captions:** Help define how human reviewers are vetted and calibrated, and review captioning guidelines so VFX, physics and preproduction detail is described accurately.
- **Collaborate with other experts** to keep evaluations consistent and accurate.

# 3\. Core Qualifications

- 7+ years of professional experience in feature VFX, animation or virtual production.
- Credits on 2+ professional films.
- A background in at least one of: VFX Supervisor, Compositing Supervisor or Lead Nuke or Flame Compositor; FX Technical Director or CG Supervisor (fluids, pyro, cloth, hair); Previs or Postvis Supervisor; or Senior Concept Artist, Matte Painter or Visual Development Artist.
- A meticulous eye for temporal instability, compositing seams, spill, physics and micro detail.
- Hands-on use of generative tools to create concept art, previs and test samples for comparison.
- Nice to have: reliable access to a 4K display for pixel-level review.
- Ability to engage reliably for approximately 40 hours/week during weekdays.
- Strong written communication and the ability to turn VFX, physics and preproduction detail into precise language for captions and evaluation templates.

**About Cincinnatus LLC:**
Cincinnatus LLC is an enterprise staffing company that partners with leading technology companies to source and employ highly skilled professionals for contingent and contract-based opportunities. Cincinnatus serves as the employer of record for these engagements, providing W-2 employment, payroll, benefits, and compliance, while placing employees directly within client teams to work on high-impact initiatives.

**Equal Employment Opportunity:**
Cincinnatus is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, reproductive health decisions, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, genetic information, political views or activity, or any other legally protected characteristic.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Expected Hours: 40 hrs/week
• Commitment: Full-Time
• Eligible Locations: USA', '["LLM Evaluation", "Compliance"]', '["**Set the quality bar:** Define clear standards and an artifact taxonomy for micro detail, multi-layer integration, physics, previs and concept art, and critique current evaluations.", "**Curate benchmarks:** Identify, generate and curate strong examples of excellent and genuinely hard VFX, simulation, previs and concept work, and test early model capabilities against them.", "**Critique model outputs:** Review generated footage frame by frame and write precise, actionable notes on temporal instability, compositing seams, spill, physics and fine detail.", "**Shape the reviewer pool and captions:** Help define how human reviewers are vetted and calibrated, and review captioning guidelines so VFX, physics and preproduction detail is described accurately.", "**Collaborate with other experts** to keep evaluations consistent and accurate."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoWTgSJZkV8di89dEJ5Z3?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('a2785ecd-6be3-584d-84d1-c22e46595faf', 'Vietnamese Linguistic Experts', 'Mercor', 'Languages', 'Remote', 'Contract', 'Specialist / SME', '$30/hr', 'Mercor is seeking experienced Vietnamese Linguistic Experts to join a cutting-edge AI research project in partnership with a leading research lab. This role centers on evaluating how effectively a large language model (LLM) performs in Vietnamese-language tasks and on curating high-quality Vietnamese linguistic data to train and improve the model''s understanding and generation capabilities.

**Key Responsibilities:**

- Evaluate the quality and accuracy of LLM-generated Vietnamese text across various use cases (e.g., translation, summarization, dialogue, grammar correction).
    
- Edit, refine, or rewrite Vietnamese content to meet linguistic and cultural standards.
    
- Annotate Vietnamese text for grammatical, syntactic, and semantic features.
    
- Identify model errors and language gaps, and collaborate with AI researchers to improve LLM performance.
    
- Provide detailed linguistic feedback and analysis to guide ongoing model training efforts.
    

**You''re a strong fit if you have:**

- Native or near-native fluency in Vietnamese, with excellent command over grammar, syntax, and stylistics.
    
- Professional experience in translation, editing, linguistic annotation, or NLP data work in Vietnamese.
    
- Strong understanding of linguistic nuances, regional variations, and context-appropriate usage.
    
- Interest in AI and LLM-driven language technologies (preferred but not required).
    
- Excellent attention to detail and ability to spot subtle errors or unnatural phrasing.
    
- Clear communication skills and experience working in distributed, remote teams.
    

**Why Join**

- Contribute to cutting-edge AI research in partnership with a leading research lab.
    
- Work on high-impact projects that directly support the development of advanced AI systems.
    
- Gain hands-on exposure to state-of-the-art AI research and development.
    
- Join a fast-moving project where your expertise and judgment can have a meaningful impact.


### Role Details & Eligibility
• Commitment: Part-Time', '["LLM Evaluation", "Translation"]', '["Contribute specialized domain expertise in Vietnamese Linguistic Experts", "Collaborate with leading frontier AI research teams to evaluate and improve model reasoning", "Ensure strict adherence to quality benchmarks and high-accuracy reference guidelines"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:48:50.407678Z', '2026-11-04T21:49:28.123610Z', 'https://work.mercor.com/jobs/list_AAABoXlzElsOghL6D6NMkrR1?referralCode=2a6bc3e0-a5f7-40ad-95f3-1609d00a73a8');
