INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('fc778864-9bfa-4750-95da-4859df2e8caf', ' Godot Game Developer', 'micro1', 'Coding', 'Remote', 'Contract', '2+ years professional experience', '$20 - $60/hr', 'Role Title: Godot Game Developer

Role Type: Contractor

Location: Remote

micro1 is engaging Godot Game Developers to participate in a dynamic project for a valued customer, focusing on crafting engaging interactive experiences using the Godot engine. In this role, you''ll apply your expertise to help train next-generation AI systems. Your work will shape how models learn, reason, and perform through high-quality, real-world input. This is an exciting opportunity for seasoned professionals who take pride in clear written and verbal communication, and who are ready to apply their Godot skills to real-world deliverables.

Scope of Work

Design and implement advanced gameplay systems, mechanics, and features using Godot engine.
Collaborate on scene creation, visual scripting, and asset integration to ensure interactive and visually appealing content.
Provide in-depth documentation and regular written feedback on game development processes and delivered components.
Deliver comprehensive code reviews and mentorship to enhance the project’s overall code quality and maintainability.
Identify, analyze, and resolve technical challenges, optimizing performance and user experience.
Participate in iterative development cycles, contributing insights to improve playability and engagement.
Support the adaptation of project assets and logic to meet evolving scope requirements.

Preferred Qualifications

Demonstrated experience in game development, whether in AAA, indie, solo, or serious hobby contexts.
