Clear written English.

How the selection process worksApply with your resume and a short profile.
Complete the curation interview. It is a short conversation about your experience with exhibitions, collections and attribution. You don’t need to prepare, look at anything or write anything. Finishing it is what moves your application forward.
Review. We check your experience against what the project needs.
Onboarding and first task. If selected, you get the guidelines and start with an initial task, which is reviewed before you continue.', '["Curator", "Collections specialist", "attention to detail", "print processes", "selecting works"]', '["Judge attribution, date, medium, edition and print type (for example, vintage vs. later print) from what is shown and described.", "Flag provenance gaps, doubtful attributions and condition or display risks.", "Check that titles, labels and descriptions are accurate and fair to the work.", "Flag rights, consent or ownership issues.", "Write a short explanation for each decision so a reviewer can follow your reasoning.", "What we\u2019re looking forProfessional work as a curator, assistant curator, collections or exhibitions specialist, gallery director, auction house specialist, art or photo archivist, or registrar.", "Experience with real decisions: selecting works, attributing them, planning displays or handling loans and acquisitions.", "For photography: familiarity with prints, editions and photographic processes."]', 'open', '2026-11-04 01:09:48', '2026-11-05T00:36:27.000Z', 'https://jobs.micro1.ai/post/4cb20660-d3e5-409a-9417-071a88777a60?referralCode=a462a1ef-5825-41db-8422-83628df889fc&utm_source=referral&utm_medium=share&utm_campaign=job_referral');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('b1316606-46fb-4c3d-a4f9-5a2368e88d70', 'Associate Forward Deployed Engineer (aFDE)', 'micro1', 'Coding', 'Remote', 'Contract', '2+ years professional experience', '$40 - $60/hr', 'Job Title: Associate Forward Deployed Engineer (aFDE)

Job Type: Full-time

Location: Remote

Work Arrangement: Hourly, with expected weekly hours agreed upfront

The Role

We’re hiring junior engineers to help scale data ingestion and customer data workflows.

You’ll work alongside core FDEs to prepare and transfer data, troubleshoot issues, build scripts and automations, and keep customers informed. You’ll start with clearly scoped responsibilities and receive guidance as you take on more technical ownership.

The initial work will combine hands-on engineering with operational execution, with the opportunity to grow into a full FDE role over time.

What You’ll Do

Help customers bring their data into the platform, from initial preparation through successful transfer and validation.
Build and improve scripts, integrations, and automations that make data ingestion faster and more reliable.
Investigate and resolve technical issues across APIs, data formats, and transfer workflows, with support from core FDEs.
Monitor active workflows, identify gaps, and verify that customer data arrives complete and accurate.
Work directly with customers and internal teams to communicate progress and move past blockers.
Turn recurring issues into better tooling, documentation, and reusable workflows.
Take on increasingly complex technical work as your experience and ownership grow.

What We’re Looking For

Foundational programming skills, including the ability to write and debug basic scripts in Python or a similar language.
Familiarity with APIs and comfort using command-line tools and Git.
A methodical approach to troubleshooting and willingness to ask for help when needed.
Strong ownership, reliability, and attention to detail.
Clear written communication with customers and internal teams.
Ability to follow runbooks, recognize their limitations, and suggest improvements.
Sound judgment around sensitive data and production systems.
Curiosity, initiative, and a desire to take on increasing engineering responsibility.

Nice to Have

Experience with SQL, data pipelines, or large datasets.
Familiarity with cloud storage and data-transfer workflows.
Experience working in Linux environments.
Familiarity with formats such as JSON, CSV, or Parquet.
Experience using AI coding tools to build and debug, with careful review of their output.
Experience in a startup or customer-facing technical role.', '["Python", "SQL", "Data Workflows"]', '["The initial work will combine hands-on engineering with operational execution, with the opportunity to grow into a full FDE role over time.", "What You\u2019ll Do", "Help customers bring their data into the platform, from initial preparation through successful transfer and validation.", "Build and improve scripts, integrations, and automations that make data ingestion faster and more reliable.", "Investigate and resolve technical issues across APIs, data formats, and transfer workflows, with support from core FDEs.", "Monitor active workflows, identify gaps, and verify that customer data arrives complete and accurate.", "Work directly with customers and internal teams to communicate progress and move past blockers.", "Turn recurring issues into better tooling, documentation, and reusable workflows."]', 'open', '2026-09-14 22:52:42', '2026-11-05T00:36:27.000Z', 'https://jobs.micro1.ai/post/b1316606-46fb-4c3d-a4f9-5a2368e88d70?referralCode=a462a1ef-5825-41db-8422-83628df889fc&utm_source=referral&utm_medium=share&utm_campaign=job_referral');
