Expertise in candidate sourcing, recruitment pipeline management, and talent acquisition best practices.
Exceptional organizational skills with the ability to self-manage and deliver results in a remote work setting.
Strong stakeholder communication, collaboration, and relationship-building abilities.
Deep familiarity with the San Francisco talent market and local recruiting channels.
Adaptability and resilience to thrive amidst shifting priorities and fast-paced demands.
Demonstrated commitment to attending and actively participating in in-person career events in San Francisco.

Preferred Qualifications:

Experience recruiting for high-growth startups or hyper-growth environments.
Established network within the San Francisco technology ecosystem.
Familiarity with modern applicant tracking systems and recruiting analytics tools.', '["Sourcing", "Recruitment pipeline", "Remote work self-management", "Stakeholder communication"]', '["Source and engage top-tier candidates through various channels, including headhunting, networking, and digital platforms.", "Manage the end-to-end recruitment pipeline, ensuring a seamless candidate experience from initial outreach to onboarding.", "Act as a trusted advisor to hiring managers and stakeholders, providing insights and recommendations on talent strategy.", "Maintain and update accurate records in the applicant tracking system, reporting key recruitment metrics and progress.", "Self-manage priorities and deliverables while working remotely, demonstrating high autonomy and accountability.", "Represent our customer''s team at San Francisco-based career fairs and industry events on a bi-weekly basis to enhance employer brand and connect with prospective talent.", "Continuously refine sourcing strategies to adapt to the evolving needs of a fast-paced startup environment."]', 'open', '2026-10-13 15:22:43', '2026-11-05T00:36:27.000Z', 'https://jobs.micro1.ai/post/30cdcad1-c75b-412d-94b6-2af95f118549?referralCode=a462a1ef-5825-41db-8422-83628df889fc&utm_source=referral&utm_medium=share&utm_campaign=job_referral');
