Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with emphasis on descriptive and technical visual vocabulary.
Demonstrated ability to detect subtle differences and accurately identify artifacts unique to AI-generated images.
Basic understanding of AI image generation processes and knowledge of typical failure points (e.g., Midjourney, Stable Diffusion, Firefly, Flux experience is a plus).
Experience in image evaluation, data annotation, or quality assurance in creative or technical projects is advantageous.', '["image evaluation", "Comparative ranking", "attention to visual detail", "written communication", "verbal comunication", "digital photography", "Artifact detection", "constructive feedback", "collaboration"]', '["Upload your own original digital images or photographs in line with provided project specifications.", "Conduct side-by-side evaluations of your artwork against AI-generated counterparts, documenting every visible difference and deviation.", "Identify and articulate issues related to anatomy, color, lighting, perspective, texture, and fine detail.", "Detect and describe common AI artifacts, including warped anatomy, smeared or broken textures, inconsistent shadows, and irregular reflections or text.", "Compose concise, visually precise written feedback using industry-standard terminology to describe each flaw, referencing specific locations within images.", "Deliver thorough, methodical reviews, prioritizing accuracy and visual detail over speed to maintain consistent quality across all assignments.", "Collaborate with project coordinators and other contributors to ensure comprehensive image assessment and feedback alignment."]', 'open', '2026-11-02 22:09:31', '2026-11-05T00:36:27.000Z', 'https://jobs.micro1.ai/post/0ea4c32b-a608-4db4-ba77-f54fafda5d02?referralCode=a462a1ef-5825-41db-8422-83628df889fc&utm_source=referral&utm_medium=share&utm_campaign=job_referral');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('c476c74d-96cc-4254-ab50-282849e9de5b', 'Domain Contributor - Evaluation Specialist ', 'micro1', 'Finance', 'Remote', 'Contract', '2+ years professional experience', '$30 - $60/hr', 'Role Title: Domain Contributor - Evaluation Specialist

Role Type: Contractor (~15 hrs/week)

Location: Remote

micro1 is engaging Domain Contributor - Evaluation Specialists to support an internal project evaluating and improving advanced AI models. In this role, you''ll apply your expertise to help train next-generation AI systems. Your work will shape how models learn, reason, and perform through high-quality, real-world input. Flexible, pay-per-task work across history, law, finance, journalism, and tech, for experts with prior AI training experience.

Scope of Work

Design nuanced, domain-specific tasks that probe AI model limits and surface reasoning flaws.
Author questions and scenarios demanding deep subject knowledge, beyond general understanding.
Assess AI-generated outputs, validating accuracy against authoritative, primary sources in your area of expertise.
Document clear rationales for model shortcomings, specifying missed reasoning, source errors, or nuances.
Apply detailed task guidelines and evaluation rubrics consistently to each submission.
Submit completed deliverables independently on a rolling basis, meeting project requirements for written and verbal clarity.

Preferred Qualifications

Proven hands-on experience with AI model training, annotation, RLHF, or evaluation.
Deep expertise in a core domain: history, archival or library science, law (paralegal, legal academic, compliance), finance (equity research, PE/VC, forensic accounting), journalism, or technology/industry history.
Advanced research skills with a track record of verifying complex claims against authoritative sources.
Exceptional written and verbal communication skills to articulate findings and feedback.
Demonstrated ability to precisely follow detailed instructions and evaluation frameworks.
Background in adversarial or “stomp the model” task design is advantageous.
Graduate-level research, experience at a Fortune 100 company, or professional fluency in a non-English language a plus.

Compensation Structure

Compensation is output-based; experts are paid per task that meets the project specifications. The time required to complete work may vary depending on the expert’s experience and workflow. Minimum submission requirements apply. Experts must submit a minimum of tasks per week.

Start Timeline & Availability

We typically fill roles within 48 hours and are looking for experts ready to jump in right away. If selected, we expect you to start your first tasks within 24–48 hours of completing onboarding.', '["Domain depth", "Source verification", "Reasoning clarity", "Evaluation expertise"]', '["Design nuanced, domain-specific tasks that probe AI model limits and surface reasoning flaws.", "Author questions and scenarios demanding deep subject knowledge, beyond general understanding.", "Assess AI-generated outputs, validating accuracy against authoritative, primary sources in your area of expertise.", "Document clear rationales for model shortcomings, specifying missed reasoning, source errors, or nuances.", "Apply detailed task guidelines and evaluation rubrics consistently to each submission."]', 'open', '2026-10-21 10:43:59', '2026-11-05T00:36:27.000Z', 'https://jobs.micro1.ai/post/c476c74d-96cc-4254-ab50-282849e9de5b?referralCode=a462a1ef-5825-41db-8422-83628df889fc&utm_source=referral&utm_medium=share&utm_campaign=job_referral');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('d2321880-8435-45d5-98c6-c8340aae8c9f', 'Domain Researcher, Finance', 'micro1', 'Finance', 'Remote', 'Contract', '2+ years professional experience', '$6 - $8/hr', 'Job Title: Domain Researcher, Finance

Job Type: Full-time

Location: Remote

The Role

Join our research team as a Domain Researcher (DR), Finance, where you''ll help define the frontier of AI-powered financial reasoning. This role sits at the intersection of large language models, agentic systems, and enterprise finance, with a focus on building rigorous evaluation frameworks that measure, benchmark, and advance AI performance across complex financial workflows.

You will conduct applied research, develop novel methodologies for assessing financial intelligence in AI systems, and partner closely with researchers, engineers, and product teams to shape the next generation of enterprise AI.

What You''ll Be Doing

Design, own, and evolve evaluation frameworks for AI agents operating in financial domains, including benchmark suites, scoring methodologies, quality rubrics, and research-grade evaluation protocols.
Conduct original research on financial reasoning, decision-making, and workflow automation, translating findings into measurable improvements in AI system performance.
