INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('ab7c2d1d-bee1-4e0d-9735-e9f86f054fde', 'Engineering PhD ', 'micro1', 'Coding', 'Remote', 'Contract', '2+ years professional experience', '$80 - $95/hr', 'Role: Engineering PhD 

Opportunity Snapshot

Pay: $80–95/hour

Duration: Short-term pilot — approximately 2–3 weeks

Project kickoff: Ideally end of week( November 8th)

Location: Fully remote

You’ll need: PhD or PhD candidate in electrical, mechanical, chemical, industrial, or aerospace engineering

Your tasks: Build technical problems from real engineering workflows and define what makes an answer correct

This is a short pilot, roughly 2–3 weeks, focused on real engineering workflows: the problems you’d actually encounter in your research or practice, not textbook exercises. You’ll build those problems, provide the correct analysis, and define what separates a right answer from one that only looks right.

What you’ll do

Design technical problems drawn from real engineering work in your field, with realistic constraints and supporting data.
Provide the correct solution and walk through the reasoning that gets there.
Define objective criteria for correctness, so another engineer reviewing the work would reach the same verdict.
Review problems built by other contributors for technical accuracy and soundness of method.
Flag problems that turn out to be ambiguous or ungradable rather than submitting them.
What we’re looking for

PhD, or PhD candidate, in electrical, mechanical, chemical, industrial, or aerospace engineering.
Degree from a strong research institution is preferred.
Hands-on research or practice experience — problems you worked on yourself, not ones you read about.
Able to explain why an answer is correct clearly enough that another engineer could verify it.
Publications or a record of technical contribution is a plus.
AI or LLM evaluation experience is a plus, but not required.

How the selection process works

Apply and complete the screening questions
Complete the AI interview for this role — it’s how your expertise gets in front of the client
Profile review
Onboarding — our Talent Ops team will get you set up

Start Timeline & AvailabilityWe typically fill roles within 48 hours and are looking for experts who are ready to begin immediately. If selected, you will be expected to start your first task within 24–48 hours of completing onboarding.', '["PhD", "Mechanichal Engineering", "Electrical Engineer", "Chemical Engineer"]', '["Apply verified knowledge in PhD, Mechanichal Engineering, Electrical Engineer to benchmark AI solutions", "Audit generative model outputs for technical and factual correctness", "Synthesize domain feedback and evaluation signals to improve model performance", "Collaborate with project coordinators to maintain high rubric adherence"]', 'open', '2026-11-03 23:37:58', '2026-11-05T00:36:27.000Z', 'https://jobs.micro1.ai/post/ab7c2d1d-bee1-4e0d-9735-e9f86f054fde?referralCode=a462a1ef-5825-41db-8422-83628df889fc&utm_source=referral&utm_medium=share&utm_campaign=job_referral');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('7cb06da3-8e02-4bd1-8a53-46a573e92907', 'English Teacher', 'micro1', 'Data Annotation & RLHF', 'Remote', 'Contract', '2+ years professional experience', '$15 - $40/hr', 'Role Title: English Teacher

Role Type: Contractor, Remote

Location: United States only

micro1 is engaging English Teachers to collaborate on a customer-driven project that improves AI assistant quality through real-world task evaluation. In this role, you''ll draw on your academic background and classroom experience, including managing student and parent communication, schedules, and coordination, to help train and evaluate next-generation AI assistants. Your expertise in language, literature, writing, and precise instruction following will shape how AI models handle the everyday tasks people delegate.

Key Responsibilities:

Complete realistic teaching-related digital tasks (emailing parents and students, scheduling conferences, booking field trips to theaters or author events, coordinating with colleagues) using AI assistant tools under standardized, repeatable conditions.
Read detailed task instructions and grading guidelines closely and follow them precisely and consistently, including multi-step requirements and fine details.
Give an AI assistant clear instructions for real-world tasks, then review its work for accuracy, tone, grammar, completeness, and whether it followed the instructions given.
Apply detailed grading guidelines to evaluate, rank, and annotate assistant responses, with a focus on language quality, literary and stylistic appropriateness, clarity, and tone.
Draw on your knowledge of literature, rhetoric, and composition to judge whether AI-written text is well-constructed, audience-appropriate, and faithful to the request.
Use AI training tools and platforms to record findings and submit evaluation data in line with project standards and milestones.

Required Skills and Qualifications:

Based in the US, with an iPhone with iMessage and a Facebook and/or Instagram account.
Bachelor''s degree in English, literature, creative writing, linguistics, comparative literature, education, or a related humanities field.
Strong instruction-following skills: the ability to read detailed, multi-step guidelines carefully and apply every requirement accurately, without skipping or reinterpreting steps.
Experience teaching English or literature (for example, language arts, literature, composition, creative writing, or ESL) at the K-12, college, or adult education level.
Solid knowledge of literary analysis, writing conventions, and grammar, with the ability to evaluate text for style, tone, and clarity.
Daily, hands-on use of Google Classroom to run your classes: posting assignments and announcements, giving feedback on student work, managing due dates, and communicating with students and parents, alongside regular use of Gmail and Google Calendar.
Experience using AI tools for real, practical tasks, with comfort giving an AI assistant instructions and checking its work.
Exceptional attention to detail in grammar, tone, and accuracy when reviewing AI-generated writing.

Preferred Qualifications:

Master''s degree or advanced coursework in English, literature, or a related field.
Prior experience with AI evaluation, data labeling, user testing, or similar feedback-driven projects.
Familiarity with prompt writing and a practical understanding of AI assistant behaviors and limitations.
Experience grading or reviewing writing or AI outputs for accuracy, helpfulness, and appropriateness.
Experience writing rubrics or giving structured feedback on student writing or literary analysis.', '["English", "Attention to Detail", "AI Usage", "Google Classroom", "Literature"]', '["Complete realistic teaching-related digital tasks (emailing parents and students, scheduling conferences, booking field trips to theaters or author events, coordinating with colleagues) using AI assistant tools under standardized, repeatable conditions."]', 'open', '2026-10-06 14:01:51', '2026-11-05T00:36:27.000Z', 'https://jobs.micro1.ai/post/7cb06da3-8e02-4bd1-8a53-46a573e92907?referralCode=a462a1ef-5825-41db-8422-83628df889fc&utm_source=referral&utm_medium=share&utm_campaign=job_referral');
