INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('7c577ab9-89b0-4104-b22e-89b1408187d6', 'HR & People Operations Expert', 'micro1', 'Data Annotation & RLHF', 'Remote', 'Contract', '2+ years professional experience', '$45 - $90/hr', 'Role Title: HR & People Operations Expert 

Role Type: Contractor

Location: Remote, global

Opportunity SnapshotPay: Up to $90/hour equivalent

Time per task: ~10 hours per task

Location: Fully remote — no geographic restrictions. Strong English required (B2 minimum, C1 preferred)

Next step: Complete the role-specific AI interview — it’s how your expertise gets in front of the client

Your tasks: Design realistic, multi-step HR and people operations tasks with objective criteria for grading the output

micro1 is engaging experienced HR and people operations practitioners to design the tasks that measure what AI systems can actually do. Your domain knowledge is what matters here — no prior AI experience required.

The work is to turn real HR workflows into benchmark tasks: realistic, difficult, and gradable against objective criteria. If you’ve written a policy, built a payroll checklist, or trained someone to handle employee cases against a standard, that’s the instinct this needs.

Scope of Work

Design multi-step tasks drawn from real HR work — payroll operations, workforce planning, policy application, employee lifecycle processes — with realistic reference files and clear instructions.
Define objective grading criteria so two qualified reviewers would reach the same verdict on the same output.
Build tasks that require judgment rather than lookup: ones where the right answer depends on reading the materials correctly.
Create or source the supporting materials each task needs: policy documents, payroll reports, headcount data, employment agreements.
Flag tasks that turn out to be ambiguous or ungradable instead of submitting them anyway.
Deliver approved tasks on schedule and at the required quality level.

Preferred Qualifications

5+ years of hands-on responsibility in payroll, workforce planning, HR policy, or employee lifecycle operations — direct ownership of the work, not supervisory-only or adjacent exposure.
Experience creating or applying structured standards: HR policies, payroll checklists, process documentation, compliance frameworks, or training assessments.
Comfortable working across spreadsheets, reports, and policy documents at the same time.
HR certification (SHRM, CIPD, PHR or equivalent) is a plus, but not required.
Strong English, written and spoken — B2 minimum, C1 preferred.
AI or LLM evaluation experience is a plus, but not required.

How the selection process works

Apply and complete the screening questions
Complete the AI interview for this role — even if you’ve interviewed with us before, a role-specific interview is how we showcase your domain expertise to the client, and it gives you the strongest shot at being selected
Profile review
Onboarding — our Talent Ops team will get you set up', '["Payroll and Lifecycle Operations", "Objective Grading Criteria", "Turning Real HR Work Into a Defined Task", "Policy Application in Edge Cases", "Working Across Documents"]', '["Design multi-step tasks drawn from real HR work \u2014 payroll operations, workforce planning, policy application, employee lifecycle processes \u2014 with realistic reference files and clear instructions.", "Define objective grading criteria so two qualified reviewers would reach the same verdict on the same output.", "Build tasks that require judgment rather than lookup: ones where the right answer depends on reading the materials correctly.", "Create or source the supporting materials each task needs: policy documents, payroll reports, headcount data, employment agreements.", "Flag tasks that turn out to be ambiguous or ungradable instead of submitting them anyway.", "Deliver approved tasks on schedule and at the required quality level."]', 'open', '2026-10-24 16:39:24', '2026-11-05T00:36:27.000Z', 'https://jobs.micro1.ai/post/7c577ab9-89b0-4104-b22e-89b1408187d6?referralCode=a462a1ef-5825-41db-8422-83628df889fc&utm_source=referral&utm_medium=share&utm_campaign=job_referral');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('aa1993c5-2079-40ac-ad0a-09ebfd77960d', 'Hardware Expert (MSc. or PhD)', 'micro1', 'Science', 'Remote', 'Contract', '2+ years professional experience', '$60 - $120/hr', 'Hardware Expert (MSc. or PhD)Pay: $60–$120/hour

Location: Global, fully remote

Job Type: Contractor (~15 hours per week)

Schedule: Flexible—you choose the hours and days you work, including weekends if desired

micro1 is engaging experienced Hardware Engineers to contribute to AI training projects built around complex, real-world engineering problems. In this role, you will use your technical expertise to create, solve, and evaluate engineering challenges that require sound judgment, quantitative reasoning, and reproducible answers.

We are looking for engineers who have personally owned meaningful technical work—such as taking a hardware system into production, validating a model against test data, developing a rigorous verification approach, or diagnosing a difficult failure. We value engineers who can connect first-principles reasoning with practical constraints and produce work that can be independently verified.

Scope of WorkCreate technically rigorous, self-contained hardware engineering problems based on realistic industry or research scenarios.
Develop clear reference solutions using engineering calculations, simulations, scripts, experimental reasoning, or other appropriate methods.
Use tools such as Python, MATLAB, Simulink, SPICE, Julia, C/C++, test automation platforms, or equivalent engineering software to validate results when relevant.

Preferred QualificationsBachelor’s, Master’s, or PhD degree in Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Mechatronics, Aerospace Engineering, Systems Engineering, Applied Physics, or a closely related field.
Significant professional or research experience in hardware engineering, product development, systems integration, testing, validation, reliability, or failure analysis.
Demonstrated ownership of a substantial engineering problem—for example, a product or subsystem that reached production, a model validated against physical testing, a test system you developed, or a difficult failure you diagnosed.
Experience working with Coding Agents is a must

ProcessApply to the role and complete the screening questions.
Complete an AI interview of approximately 30 minutes.
Complete the hiring manager review.

Compensation Structure

Compensation is output-based. Experts are paid per task that meets the project specifications. The time required to complete each task may vary depending on the expert’s experience and workflow.

Minimum submission requirements apply..

Start Timeline & Availability

We typically fill roles within 48 hours and are looking for experts who are ready to begin immediately. If selected, you will be expected to start your first task within 24–48 hours of completing onboarding.', '["RTL", "Hardware"]', '["Develop clear reference solutions using engineering calculations, simulations, scripts, experimental reasoning, or other appropriate methods.", "Use tools such as Python, MATLAB, Simulink, SPICE, Julia, C/C++, test automation platforms, or equivalent engineering software to validate results when relevant."]', 'open', '2026-10-16 18:13:05', '2026-11-05T00:36:27.000Z', 'https://jobs.micro1.ai/post/aa1993c5-2079-40ac-ad0a-09ebfd77960d?referralCode=a462a1ef-5825-41db-8422-83628df889fc&utm_source=referral&utm_medium=share&utm_campaign=job_referral');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('cf33e75a-c1e5-4255-a96c-81f2b7a52947', 'Head of Communications', 'micro1', 'Data Annotation & RLHF', 'Remote', 'Contract', '2+ years professional experience', '$7 - $8/hr', 'Job Title: Head of Communications

Job Type: Full-time

Location: Remote

The Role

We''re looking for a strategic communicator to lead our external communications and shape how our work is understood across media, customers, and the AI ecosystem. You''ll own our communications strategy—from product launches and company announcements to executive thought leadership and media relations, helping build trust, credibility, and visibility for the company.

What You''ll Do

Own and execute the company''s external communications and PR strategy.
Build relationships with journalists, creators, analysts, and industry influencers.
Secure earned media across digital, print, broadcast, podcasts, and social channels.
Develop messaging for product launches, partnerships, company announcements, and executive communications.
Position company leaders through interviews, speaking engagements, bylines, and media opportunities.
Prepare executives with messaging, briefing materials, and media coaching.
Manage external PR agencies and communications partners.
Lead crisis and rapid-response communications when needed.

What We''re Looking For

Significant experience leading communications or PR for high-growth technology companies.
Exceptional writing, storytelling, and verbal communication skills.
Proven success securing top-tier media coverage and building lasting press relationships.
Experience leading communications for product launches and major company announcements.
Strong strategic judgment with the ability to translate complex technical topics into clear, compelling narratives.
Experience managing multiple priorities in a fast-paced, remote environment.

Preferred

Experience in AI, developer tools, enterprise software, or B2B SaaS.
Familiarity with AI and emerging technologies.
Experience working with distributed teams.
Crisis communications experience.

Compensation & Benefits Notice

The national pay range for this full-time position is base salary of $150,000 –$200,000. All employees are eligible for equity compensation, and employees may also receive performance-based bonuses, dependent on role and subject to company policies. micro1 provides a comprehensive benefits package, including up to 100% reimbursement for health-insurance premiums, paid time off, a 401(K) plan with a company match, and additional benefits designed to support a high-performing, remote-first workforce.

micro1 is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, or gender identity), national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable local laws, regulations and ordinances. If you need assistance and/or a reasonable accommodation during the application process, reach out to support@micro1.ai.

Our hiring process utilizes artificial intelligence tools to assist in candidate screening and assessment. Our AI tools are designed to complement, not replace, human decision-making.

Disclaimer

The information contained in this job posting, including but not limited to role responsibilities, qualifications, compensation, and benefits, is provided for informational purposes only and does not constitute a binding offer of employment. micro1 reserves the right to amend, modify, or withdraw any portion of this posting at its sole discretion and without prior notice. All employment decisions are made in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.', '["PR", "Vendor Management", "Partnerships", "Communications Strategy"]', '["Own and execute the company''s external communications and PR strategy.", "Build relationships with journalists, creators, analysts, and industry influencers.", "Secure earned media across digital, print, broadcast, podcasts, and social channels.", "Develop messaging for product launches, partnerships, company announcements, and executive communications.", "Position company leaders through interviews, speaking engagements, bylines, and media opportunities.", "Prepare executives with messaging, briefing materials, and media coaching.", "Manage external PR agencies and communications partners.", "Lead crisis and rapid-response communications when needed."]', 'open', '2026-10-05 05:05:18', '2026-11-05T00:36:27.000Z', 'https://jobs.micro1.ai/post/cf33e75a-c1e5-4255-a96c-81f2b7a52947?referralCode=a462a1ef-5825-41db-8422-83628df889fc&utm_source=referral&utm_medium=share&utm_campaign=job_referral');
