Review sample questions about signing up for Medicare and flag any that don’t sound like what real people ask.
Write rubrics that define a correct, complete answer on initial enrollment, special enrollment periods, and Part B late penalties, including how enrollment ties to Social Security benefits.
Cover Medigap vs. Medicare Advantage and Part D in your rubrics, with a focus on scenarios involving employer or retiree coverage.
Cover how employer coverage interacts with Medicare, including employer size, primary vs. secondary coverage, COBRA, and creditable coverage.
Evaluate AI-generated answers against your rubrics, flagging errors, omissions, and common misconceptions.
Share clear written feedback with the project team, working asynchronously.

Required Qualifications

Former SSA Medicare enrollment experience, or employer benefits/HR experience advising employees on Medicare
1+ years advising on initial enrollment, special enrollment periods, Part B late penalties, Medigap vs. Medicare Advantage, and Part D
Working knowledge of Social Security and employer coverage coordination, including creditable coverage
US-based
Able to start quickly and commit 20-30 hours/week
Clear, precise writing

Nice to Have

Experience with premium adjustments (such as IRMAA), working while enrolled, or HSA rules alongside Medicare
Experience creating guides, counseling scripts, or training materials
Experience helping a diverse range of beneficiaries, including rural and non-English-speaking clients', '["Medicare", "Enrollment", "Coordination", "Coverage", "COBRA"]', '["Review sample questions about signing up for Medicare and flag any that don\u2019t sound like what real people ask."]', 'open', '2026-10-12 19:58:51', '2026-11-05T00:36:27.000Z', 'https://jobs.micro1.ai/post/a6091fe2-e1e0-4460-b9db-6a513ceead46?referralCode=a462a1ef-5825-41db-8422-83628df889fc&utm_source=referral&utm_medium=share&utm_campaign=job_referral');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('cf2d7fe9-2077-4932-87bb-e8f98977518a', 'Member of Technical Staff, Coding Research', 'micro1', 'Coding', 'Remote', 'Contract', '2+ years professional experience', '$8 - $9/hr', 'Job Title: Member of Technical Staff, Coding Research

Job Type: Full-time

Location: Remote

The Role

We are seeking a Member of Technical Staff to help advance the evaluation and development of frontier coding agents. Sitting at the intersection of AI research, software engineering, and model evaluation, you will design the benchmarks, methodologies, and data systems that shape how next-generation coding models are measured and improved.

What You''ll Do

Design and own evaluation frameworks for coding agents, including benchmark specifications, scoring methodologies, rubrics, and quality standards.
Lead end-to-end research initiatives focused on measuring and improving coding model performance across diverse software engineering tasks.
Develop high-quality datasets, golden examples, and evaluation protocols that enable reliable assessment of frontier coding systems.
Analyze model behavior and failure modes, identifying systematic weaknesses and translating findings into actionable improvements for training and evaluation.
Build tooling and infrastructure that support large-scale experimentation, data generation, review workflows, and evaluation pipelines.
Establish best practices for coding-agent assessment, ensuring methodological rigor, reproducibility, and measurement quality.
Partner closely with researchers, engineers, and applied AI teams to design experiments and evaluate emerging model capabilities.
Contribute to technical reports, benchmark studies, and client-facing research initiatives that communicate model performance and insights.

What We''re Looking For

Strong software engineering background with expertise in Python, C++, or comparable programming languages.
3+ years of experience in software engineering, machine learning, AI research, evaluation, or related technical disciplines.
Experience designing, reviewing, or validating technical assessments, benchmarks, coding tasks, or evaluation methodologies.
Familiarity with large language models, coding agents, reinforcement learning, model evaluation, or related AI systems.
Proven ability to build tooling, automate workflows, and improve technical processes through systematic experimentation.
Strong analytical skills with the ability to investigate model behavior and derive insights from complex technical systems.
Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to clearly articulate technical findings to diverse audiences.
Comfortable operating in fast-moving research environments with significant ambiguity and evolving priorities.

Preferred

Experience working on frontier AI systems, coding agents, or model evaluation research.
Deep interest in understanding how data, evaluations, and feedback mechanisms influence model capabilities.
Track record of independently driving ambiguous technical or research projects from conception to execution.
Experience designing benchmarks or datasets for machine learning systems at scale.
Familiarity with agentic workflows, tool use, reinforcement learning, or post-training methodologies.
Publications, open-source contributions, or demonstrated technical leadership in AI, machine learning, or software engineering.

Compensation & Benefits Notice

The national pay range for this full-time position is base salary of $200,000 –$260,000 USD. All employees are eligible for equity compensation, and employees may also receive performance-based bonuses, dependent on role and subject to company policies. micro1 provides a comprehensive benefits package, including up to 100% reimbursement for health-insurance premiums, paid time off, a 401(K) plan with a company match, and additional benefits designed to support a high-performing, remote-first workforce.

micro1 is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, or gender identity), national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable local laws, regulations and ordinances. If you need assistance and/or a reasonable accommodation during the application process, reach out to support@micro1.ai.

Our hiring process utilizes artificial intelligence tools to assist in candidate screening and assessment. Our AI tools are designed to complement, not replace, human decision-making.', '["LLMs", "Coding Evaluation", "AI Evaluation", "ML Systems"]', '["Design and own evaluation frameworks for coding agents, including benchmark specifications, scoring methodologies, rubrics, and quality standards.", "Lead end-to-end research initiatives focused on measuring and improving coding model performance across diverse software engineering tasks.", "Develop high-quality datasets, golden examples, and evaluation protocols that enable reliable assessment of frontier coding systems.", "Analyze model behavior and failure modes, identifying systematic weaknesses and translating findings into actionable improvements for training and evaluation.", "Build tooling and infrastructure that support large-scale experimentation, data generation, review workflows, and evaluation pipelines.", "Establish best practices for coding-agent assessment, ensuring methodological rigor, reproducibility, and measurement quality.", "Partner closely with researchers, engineers, and applied AI teams to design experiments and evaluate emerging model capabilities.", "Contribute to technical reports, benchmark studies, and client-facing research initiatives that communicate model performance and insights."]', 'open', '2026-09-14 21:19:43', '2026-11-05T00:36:27.000Z', 'https://jobs.micro1.ai/post/cf2d7fe9-2077-4932-87bb-e8f98977518a?referralCode=a462a1ef-5825-41db-8422-83628df889fc&utm_source=referral&utm_medium=share&utm_campaign=job_referral');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('0e5cfd61-fe27-4955-ad5c-952e6e5d8198', 'Member of Technical Staff, Data Engineering', 'micro1', 'Coding', 'Remote', 'Contract', '2+ years professional experience', '$7 - $8/hr', 'Job Title: Member of Technical Staff, Data Engineering

Job Type: Full-time

Location: Remote

The Role

This is a Staff-level, hands-on engineering role for someone who has built data infrastructure from zero to production and knows how to turn fragmented operational data into reliable, accessible, and actionable systems.

You''ll own the architecture and implementation of our data warehouse, ingestion pipelines, transformations, and product analytics foundations.

We''re building an AI-native organization where both humans and autonomous agents need access to trustworthy, well-structured data. You''ll design the systems that make this possible, enabling self-service analytics, automated decision-making, and increasingly intelligent workflows across the company.

What You''ll Do

Build our data platform from zero: Architect and implement our internal data warehouse, ingestion infrastructure, ETL/ELT pipelines, and core data models.
Create agent-ready data foundations: Design reliable, well-documented datasets and interfaces that AI agents can safely discover, query, and use.
Turn messy data into trusted systems: Transform fragmented operational and product data into consistent, high-quality sources of truth.
Enable self-service analytics: Build the infrastructure that allows engineering, product, and business teams to answer questions independently without relying on manual data requests.
Own product analytics infrastructure: Establish the event tracking, instrumentation, data models, and reporting foundations needed to understand product usage and performance.
Automate data operations: Leverage AI coding agents and intelligent automation to accelerate pipeline development, data validation, documentation, monitoring, and troubleshooting.
Build for reliability and scale: Establish data quality standards, observability, governance, and scalable architectural patterns from the beginning.
Raise the engineering bar: Mentor engineers, establish strong data engineering practices, and lead architectural decisions through hands-on execution.

What We''re Looking For

Staff-level engineering expertise with extensive hands-on experience building and operating production data platforms.
Proven greenfield experience: You''ve personally led the design and implementation of a data platform from scratch, rather than exclusively maintaining or extending existing infrastructure.
