Recognition at the field level—such as major prizes, society fellowships, or plenary/invited talks at top scholarly events.
A consistent publication record in leading venues within your domain, with recent results published in the past year.
Demonstrated success resolving named open problems or introducing influential concepts adopted by peers.
Deep, hands-on experience with computational research methods: simulation, numerical analysis, algorithmic implementation, and/or high-performance computing environments.
Proven ability to rigorously examine technical work outside your immediate area of expertise.
Experience on program committees, editorial boards, or with formal research tools (e.g., Lean, Coq, SAT/SMT solvers) is a strong plus, as is a public record of outlining open problems or showcasing research with advanced AI systems.', '["Novelty judgment", "Research direction", "Computational rigor", "Complex problem solving - Research"]', '["Identify, frame, and articulate foundational open problems, theoretical bounds, or simulation challenges where verifiable progress can be demonstrated.", "Guide AI models and agents in multi-step research processes\u2014ranging from proofs and algorithms to numerical experiments and high-performance simulations.", "Critically assess and validate results, utilizing proof checks, computational reproduction, and formal methods to pinpoint the limits of model-generated reasoning.", "Evaluate and document the novelty, correctness, and significance of research outputs relative to current literature and established results.", "Produce clear, concise research memos detailing research attempts, partial solutions, and observed model limitations or failure patterns.", "Advise on research directions, recommending promising subfields and open problems suitable for advancement via AI models and computational tools."]', 'open', '2026-10-13 15:52:12', '2026-11-05T00:36:27.000Z', 'https://jobs.micro1.ai/post/83ed9d66-130e-4c8f-8e9f-b1d18acdcf98?referralCode=a462a1ef-5825-41db-8422-83628df889fc&utm_source=referral&utm_medium=share&utm_campaign=job_referral');
