This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your AWS expertise directly helps improve the world’s premier AI models by teaching them how real users complete cloud setup, configuration, monitoring, and troubleshooting tasks.


### Responsibilities
• Create realistic AWS tasks: Come up with realistic and challenging tasks that can be executed on the computer using AWS, then document the task clearly in SuperAnnotate.
• Prepare the work environment: Ensure your setup supports the task, including having AWS access, permissions, test resources, sample files, and any required references ready before recording.
• Record task execution: Record yourself executing the AWS task on your computer while following project instructions and ensuring the workflow is clear, complete, realistic, and safe.
• Document task context: Provide enough task context, steps, goals, resource details, files, and notes so reviewers can understand what the task is and how it was completed.
• Demonstrate practical software use: Complete workflows involving AWS Console navigation, S3, IAM, EC2, Lambda, CloudWatch, billing views, security groups, deployment, or troubleshooting where relevant.
• Maintain submission quality: Review your recording and documentation before submission to ensure the task is complete, understandable, realistic, safe, and aligned with project guidelines.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Hands-on experience using AWS for cloud setup, configuration, monitoring, storage, compute, permissions, deployment, or troubleshooting workflows.
• English proficiency at B2 level or higher to understand project instructions, document tasks clearly, and communicate with the project team.
• Comfortable using a computer, browser-based tools, cloud consoles, documentation, terminals where needed, and recording workflows.
• Ability to come up with realistic and challenging AWS tasks that reflect actual cloud, DevOps, backend, admin, data, or infrastructure use cases.
• Strong understanding of AWS basics such as IAM, S3, EC2, Lambda, CloudWatch, security groups, regions, billing awareness, and resource configuration.
• Ability to ensure your setup supports the task, including having AWS access, permissions, sample resources, safe test environments, and any required references ready before recording.
• High attention to detail when preparing the task, executing the workflow, and checking that the recording is complete, safe, and understandable.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Additional professional skills are appreciated, including cloud engineering, DevOps, backend development, cybersecurity, data engineering, coding, admin, operations, or other computer-based workflows.


### Eligible Countries (3)
Bangladesh, India, Pakistan', '["S3", "DevOps", "IAM", "Screen Recording", "Lambda", "EC2", "English", "Cloud Computing", "AWS", "AWS Console"]', '["Create realistic AWS tasks: Come up with realistic and challenging tasks that can be executed on the computer using AWS, then document the task clearly in SuperAnnotate.", "Prepare the work environment: Ensure your setup supports the task, including having AWS access, permissions, test resources, sample files, and any required references ready before recording.", "Record task execution: Record yourself executing the AWS task on your computer while following project instructions and ensuring the workflow is clear, complete, realistic, and safe.", "Document task context: Provide enough task context, steps, goals, resource details, files, and notes so reviewers can understand what the task is and how it was completed.", "Demonstrate practical software use: Complete workflows involving AWS Console navigation, S3, IAM, EC2, Lambda, CloudWatch, billing views, security groups, deployment, or troubleshooting where relevant.", "Maintain submission quality: Review your recording and documentation before submission to ensure the task is complete, understandable, realistic, safe, and aligned with project guidelines."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=81db3818-48a3-4dba-b761-bacd57f12ffe&jobPostingId=AWS-26-129');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('b70fa49f-e0c9-5d36-ad48-1560d731d513', 'Accountant', 'sme.careers', 'Finance', 'Remote (39 Countries: Austria, Bangladesh, Belgium…)', 'Contract', 'Mid Senior Level', '$65/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as an Accounting Subject Matter Expert (SME) to review AI-generated accounting and finance responses and/or create expert accounting content, evaluating reasoning quality and step-by-step problem-solving while providing precise written feedback. You will assess solutions for accuracy, clarity, completeness, and adherence to the prompt; identify errors in bookkeeping logic, journal entries, accruals, reconciliations, financial statement presentation, and controls; fact-check technical accounting claims; write high-quality explanations and model solutions that demonstrate correct methods; and rate and compare multiple responses based on correctness and reasoning quality. This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs.

Important:
There is no immediate project for this role; however, if qualified, you will be among the first experts we reach out to when relevant opportunities arise. This will also provide you with access to future projects available through our expert network.


### Responsibilities
• Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts and gold-standard accounting outputs (journal entries, explanations, close checklists, reconciliations logic, scenario analyses).
• Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to improve correctness, clarity, and adherence to GAAP/IFRS and best practices.
• Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI outputs for inaccuracies, misleading guidance, unsafe assumptions, and bias; validate reliability across business scenarios.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree (or higher) in Accounting, Finance, or a related field; CPA/ACCA/CMA (or local equivalent) is a strong plus.
• 5+ years of professional experience in accounting (public accounting, industry, shared services, or advisory).
• Strong command of core accounting areas: revenue/expense recognition, accruals, prepaid/deferred items, fixed assets, inventory basics, payroll basics, and taxes awareness.
• Proven ability to prepare and review journal entries, account reconciliations, and month-end close deliverables with attention to auditability.
• Solid understanding of financial statements (P&L, balance sheet, cash flow) and common classification/presentation issues.
• Familiarity with internal controls concepts (segregation of duties, approvals, documentation standards) and audit readiness.
• Comfortable evaluating answers for internal consistency (sign conventions, debits/credits, timing, cut-off, supporting schedules) and business realism.
• Minimum C1 English proficiency with the ability to write clear, structured explanations and follow detailed guidelines.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Prior experience with AI data training/annotation, accounting QA, audit review, or technical accounting writing is strongly preferred.


