• Prepare the work environment: Ensure your setup supports the task, including having AutoCAD installed, files available, drawings/templates prepared, and any necessary references ready before recording.
• Record task execution: Record yourself executing the AutoCAD task on your computer while following project instructions and ensuring the workflow is clear, complete, and realistic.
• Document task context: Provide enough task context, steps, goals, files, and notes so reviewers can understand what the task is and how it was completed.
• Demonstrate practical software use: Complete workflows involving drafting, layers, dimensions, blocks, layouts, plotting, annotations, xrefs, or drawing cleanup where relevant.
• Maintain submission quality: Review your recording and documentation before submission to ensure the task is complete, understandable, realistic, and aligned with project guidelines.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Hands-on experience using AutoCAD for drafting, technical drawings, layouts, annotation, dimensions, plotting, or related CAD workflows.
• English proficiency at B2 level or higher to understand project instructions, document tasks clearly, and communicate with the project team.
• Comfortable using a computer, managing files, installing/opening required programs, navigating software interfaces, and recording workflows.
• Ability to come up with realistic and challenging AutoCAD tasks that reflect actual drafting, design, documentation, engineering, architecture, or technical drawing use cases.
• Strong understanding of AutoCAD basics such as model space, paper space, layers, lineweights, blocks, dimensions, annotations, layouts, viewports, and plotting.
• Ability to ensure your setup supports the task, including having AutoCAD installed, files available, templates/assets prepared, and any required references ready before recording.
• High attention to detail when preparing the task, executing the workflow, and checking that the recording is complete and understandable.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Additional professional skills are appreciated, including architecture, engineering, drafting, construction documentation, design, sales, administration, coding, operations, or other computer-based workflows.


### Eligible Countries (7)
Bangladesh, Brazil, India, Indonesia, Nepal, Pakistan, The United States', '["AutoCAD", "Layers", "Blocks", "Screen Recording", "CAD Drafting", "Dimensioning", "English", "Layouts", "2D Drafting", "Technical Drawing"]', '["Create realistic AutoCAD tasks: Come up with realistic and challenging tasks that can be executed on the computer using AutoCAD, then document the task clearly in SuperAnnotate.", "Prepare the work environment: Ensure your setup supports the task, including having AutoCAD installed, files available, drawings/templates prepared, and any necessary references ready before recording.", "Record task execution: Record yourself executing the AutoCAD task on your computer while following project instructions and ensuring the workflow is clear, complete, and realistic.", "Document task context: Provide enough task context, steps, goals, files, and notes so reviewers can understand what the task is and how it was completed.", "Demonstrate practical software use: Complete workflows involving drafting, layers, dimensions, blocks, layouts, plotting, annotations, xrefs, or drawing cleanup where relevant.", "Maintain submission quality: Review your recording and documentation before submission to ensure the task is complete, understandable, realistic, and aligned with project guidelines."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=688165c8-21d0-4d5b-8d69-8189adb38fdd&jobPostingId=AutoCAD-26-201');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('9b1fcb81-a877-5018-a785-c385af2652fd', 'Bash Team Lead', 'sme.careers', 'Finance', 'Remote (The United States)', 'Contract', 'Mid Senior Level', '$65/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Bash Quality Assurance Lead (QAL) to oversee quality, consistency, and trainer performance across Bash/shell scripting AI training projects. You will review AI-generated Bash code and trainer/QA work, evaluate output quality against project guidelines, provide precise written feedback, and ensure that contributors follow expected quality standards.

You will assess work for script correctness, command safety, portability, debugging accuracy, error handling, security awareness, readability, maintainability, formatting, instruction-following, and adherence to project-specific rubrics. You will spot recurring quality issues, communicate updates to trainers and QAs, support onboarding, maintain documentation, and help activate contributors who are not working consistently.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your Bash quality leadership will directly help improve the world’s premier AI models by ensuring that shell-scripting training data is accurate, executable, safe, clearly explained, and aligned with client expectations.

Selection process involves an AI interview, a domain-specific task, and an interview with a recruiter.

Important:
There is no immediate project for this role; however, if qualified, you will be among the first experts we reach out to when relevant opportunities arise. This will also provide you with access to future projects available through our expert network.


### Responsibilities
• Quality monitoring: Spot-check Bash items, identify quality issues, provide feedback through DMs, and escalate recurring or critical issues.
• Code review: Evaluate AI-generated shell scripts, CLI workflows, automation snippets, debugging responses, and explanations for correctness and safety.
• Trainer/QA communication: Update contributors on Discord about new guidelines, workflow changes, and Bash-specific review expectations.
• Question handling: Respond to questions around quoting, portability, Linux commands, destructive operations, permissions, pipelines, and rubric interpretation.
• Activation management: DM inactive contributors, encourage activation, track follow-ups, and flag availability issues.
• Documentation: Create and maintain Bash style guides, trackers, FAQs, examples, honeypots, calibration tasks, and onboarding materials.
• Onboarding: Run onboarding/training calls explaining workflows, rubrics, safety expectations, and Bash-specific review rules.
• Safety review: Flag unsafe scripts, destructive commands, credential exposure, injection risks, or misleading production guidance.
• Process improvement: Identify recurring gaps and build scalable QA processes.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, IT, Systems Administration, or equivalent professional experience.
• Strong grasp of English to follow guidelines and provide clear technical feedback.
• 3+ years of experience with Bash/shell scripting, Linux/Unix systems, automation, DevOps, systems administration, CI/CD, or technical support workflows.
• Strong understanding of Bash fundamentals: variables, quoting, conditionals, loops, functions, pipes, redirection, exit codes, signals, process management, file permissions, and POSIX portability.
• Ability to identify issues such as unsafe commands, poor quoting, non-portable syntax, missing error handling, incorrect assumptions, hallucinated flags, and destructive operations.
• Familiarity with tools such as grep, awk, sed, find, xargs, curl, jq, cron, SSH, Git, Docker, CI/CD pipelines, and Linux package managers is preferred.
• Experience leading or supporting remote teams of trainers, reviewers, engineers, or QAs is strongly preferred.
