• Trainer and QA communication: Update trainers and QAs on Discord about new item guidelines, project changes, workflow updates, quality expectations, and biomedical-engineering-specific review standards.
• Question handling: Respond to trainer/QA questions clearly and promptly, especially around engineering assumptions, units, formulas, biological context, device safety, regulatory considerations, standards references, and rubric interpretation.
• Trainer/QA activation management: DM contributors who are inactive or not working, encourage activation, track follow-ups, and flag availability issues when needed.
• Documentation: Create and maintain biomedical engineering project documentation, including style guides, trackers, FAQs, quality notes, examples, honeypots, calibration tasks, and onboarding materials.
• Onboarding and training: Schedule and run onboarding/training calls with trainers and QAs to explain project expectations, workflows, rubrics, quality standards, and biomedical-engineering-specific review requirements.
• Quality alignment: Ensure all trainers and QAs apply biomedical engineering guidelines consistently and understand updates as projects evolve.
• Risk and safety review: Flag unsafe, misleading, or overconfident biomedical engineering recommendations, especially where medical devices, patient safety, clinical workflows, biological systems, diagnostics, imaging, rehabilitation tools, or regulatory claims may be affected.
• Process improvement: Identify recurring quality gaps, propose workflow improvements, and help build scalable QA processes for biomedical engineering AI training projects.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Biomedical Engineering, Bioengineering, Medical Engineering, Biomechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering with biomedical focus, Mechanical Engineering with biomedical focus, or a closely related field.
• Strong grasp of the English language to follow project guidelines, communicate with teams, and provide clear technical feedback in English.
• 3+ years of professional experience in biomedical engineering, medical devices, biomechanics, biomaterials, bioinstrumentation, clinical engineering, R&D, regulatory documentation, technical review, engineering education, or related workflows.
• Strong understanding of core biomedical engineering topics such as biomechanics, biomaterials, medical devices, bioinstrumentation, biosignals, imaging systems, physiological systems, tissue engineering, rehabilitation engineering, and biomedical data analysis.
• Ability to evaluate biomedical engineering content against detailed rubrics and identify issues such as incorrect assumptions, flawed calculations, missing units, unsafe recommendations, weak biological/clinical reasoning, hallucinated standards, regulatory overclaims, or incomplete explanations.
• Familiarity with common biomedical engineering tools or workflows such as MATLAB, Python, LabVIEW, SolidWorks, CAD/CAE tools, signal processing workflows, medical device documentation, ISO/FDA-related documentation, clinical engineering workflows, or biomedical data analysis tools is preferred.
• Experience leading or supporting remote teams of trainers, annotators, reviewers, engineers, technical writers, or QAs is strongly preferred.
• Comfortable working in fast-moving remote environments using tools such as Discord, Google Sheets, Google Docs, trackers, dashboards, and project management systems.
• Highly detail-oriented and organized, with the ability to maintain style guides, FAQs, trackers, onboarding materials, honeypots, calibration tasks, and other quality documentation.
• Experience with AI training, data annotation, large language models, prompt/response evaluation, technical content QA, biomedical content QA, or rubric-based LLM evaluation is a strong plus.', '["LLM Evaluation", "Medical Devices", "Engineering QA", "Technical Review", "Biomechanics", "Biomedical Engineering", "AI Training", "Documentation", "Biomaterials", "Trainer Feedback"]', '["Quality monitoring: Spot-check biomedical engineering items, identify quality issues, provide ongoing feedback through DMs, and escalate recurring or critical issues.", "Technical review: Evaluate AI-generated biomedical engineering explanations, medical-device reasoning, biomechanics calculations, biomaterials discussions, bioinstrumentation workflows, biosignal explanations, diagrams/descriptions, and problem-solving steps for correctness and clarity.", "Trainer and QA communication: Update trainers and QAs on Discord about new item guidelines, project changes, workflow updates, quality expectations, and biomedical-engineering-specific review standards.", "Question handling: Respond to trainer/QA questions clearly and promptly, especially around engineering assumptions, units, formulas, biological context, device safety, regulatory considerations, standards references, and rubric interpretation.", "Trainer/QA activation management: DM contributors who are inactive or not working, encourage activation, track follow-ups, and flag availability issues when needed.", "Documentation: Create and maintain biomedical engineering project documentation, including style guides, trackers, FAQs, quality notes, examples, honeypots, calibration tasks, and onboarding materials.", "Onboarding and training: Schedule and run onboarding/training calls with trainers and QAs to explain project expectations, workflows, rubrics, quality standards, and biomedical-engineering-specific review requirements.", "Quality alignment: Ensure all trainers and QAs apply biomedical engineering guidelines consistently and understand updates as projects evolve.", "Risk and safety review: Flag unsafe, misleading, or overconfident biomedical engineering recommendations, especially where medical devices, patient safety, clinical workflows, biological systems, diagnostics, imaging, rehabilitation tools, or regulatory claims may be affected.", "Process improvement: Identify recurring quality gaps, propose workflow improvements, and help build scalable QA processes for biomedical engineering AI training projects."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=d67b09a2-081c-41d6-b26d-96715896aeb6&jobPostingId=BiomedEngineerQAL-26-133');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('02704e40-c825-5639-ace9-e70c33a9ddf2', 'Blender Specialist', 'sme.careers', 'Coding', 'Remote (31 Countries: Australia, Bangladesh, Bhutan…)', 'Contract', 'Not Applicable', '$30/hr', '## About SME Careers
As AI systems become more sophisticated, they rely on human knowledge to better understand context and the world. At SME Careers, we partner with leading AI labs to improve how the next generation of intelligent systems learn, reason, and act. SME Careers is a fast-growing AI data services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate that provides AI training data to many of the world''s top AI companies and foundation model labs. Your expertise as a Blender 3D artist will directly help improve the world''s premier AI models.

## About the role
The current generation of AI agents can read a screen, but they still fail badly at doing real professional work inside real desktop software — and Blender is one of the hardest cases there is. Dense modal interfaces, keyboard-driven operators, a 3D viewport where the correct next click depends on the state of the mesh: agents that handle a web form competently fall apart on a modifier stack.

In this remote, hourly contract role you will help fix that. You will design realistic, challenging Blender tasks, then record yourself completing them on your own computer using recording tools we provide. Each recording captures the full picture of how expert work actually gets done — the sequence of actions, the interface state at every step, and the files before and after — and becomes both a demonstration the model learns from and a benchmark it is measured against.

Because a model can only learn from work that can be scored, an equally important part of the job is defining what "done correctly" means. Alongside each task you will write the objective and the steps you took, and specify how the result should be verified — what the finished scene, mesh, or render has to satisfy for the outcome to count as correct, and which intermediate checkpoints a partially-successful attempt would hit. This is the reward side of the work: in reinforcement learning, an agent improves only when success can be judged consistently, so expert-authored tasks with expert-defined success criteria are the actual bottleneck in training capable agents. Your judgment about what a competent Blender artist would do, and what a plausible-looking-but-wrong result looks like, is the contribution.

This position is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI data services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate that provides AI training data to many of the world''s top AI companies and foundation model labs. Your work will directly help improve the world''s premier AI models.

## Why Join Us
- Paid, flexible remote work where your Blender expertise directly shapes how AI agents learn to use professional creative software.
- Work on frontier agent training rather than generic labeling — your demonstrations and success criteria become both training data and benchmarks.
Clear guidelines and structured review focused on practical 3D correctness, not generic ratings.
Progression paths into QA and QA lead roles, and ongoing batches as performance and availability align.


### Responsibilities
• - Author production-realistic Blender tasks: Write task briefs that reflect work a studio or client would actually ask for — a low-poly prop to spec, a retopology and UV pass, a shader and lighting setup, a scene assembled to a camera brief — scoped tightly enough that the outcome can be objectively verified.
• Record expert demonstrations: Set up your own environment for the task (files staged, add-ons and reference assets in place) and record yourself executing it end to end with the provided capture tooling, producing a complete trace of actions, interface state, and file changes.
• Document the workflow step by step: Log the steps you took in a form another expert could follow and reproduce, in clear professional English.
• Define verification and success criteria: Specify what the finished result must satisfy, which intermediate milestones mark real progress, and which common wrong paths should not be credited — the rubric a grader uses to score an agent''s attempt.
• Cover the range of difficulty: Produce tasks from single-tool operations up to long, multi-step workflows that cross applications (reference gathered in a browser, assets from a file manager, delivery into a target format).
• Review and quality-check others'' work: For those who move into QA, audit submitted traces for task realism, recording completeness, step-to-action mapping, and whether the stated success criteria genuinely hold for the result produced.
• Work to project quality standards: Keep recordings free of personal information, use only approved applications, and complete all work using your own expertise — the use of closed-source AI assistants is contractually prohibited on this project.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• 2–5 years of professional experience as a Blender-focused 3D artist (contract, studio, or freelance), or equivalent demonstrable practical experience.
• Proven proficiency in Blender for production work: modeling and clean topology, modifiers, UV unwrapping, materials and shading, lighting, and rendering in Cycles and/or EEVEE.
• Strong troubleshooting instincts — you can recognize and explain bad topology, shading and normals problems, scale inconsistencies, and non-manifold geometry, not just avoid them.
• A computer you can install our recording tools on and work in daily: Windows 11, Ubuntu (X11), or macOS. Batches are assigned by operating system, and hardware capable of running Blender comfortably alongside a screen recorder is required.
• English proficiency: minimum B2, with the written clarity to document a workflow another expert can reproduce.
• Ability to apply detailed rubrics consistently and make repeatable quality judgments across many similar tasks.
• Highly detail-oriented and self-directed, with strong asynchronous work habits for remote, flexible-hour contract work.
• Previous experience with AI data training, annotation, evaluation, or benchmark work.


### Eligible Countries (31)
Australia, Bangladesh, Bhutan, Brazil, Cambodia, China, Fiji, Hong Kong, India, Indonesia, Japan, Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan, Macau, Malaysia, Mongolia, Nauru, Nepal, New Zealand, Pakistan, Singapore, South Korea, Sri Lanka, Taiwan, Tajikistan, Thailand, The Philippines, The United States, Timor Leste, Uzbekistan, Vietnam', '["Python", "3D Modelling", "Blender 3D"]', '["- Author production-realistic Blender tasks: Write task briefs that reflect work a studio or client would actually ask for \u2014 a low-poly prop to spec, a retopology and UV pass, a shader and lighting setup, a scene assembled to a camera brief \u2014 scoped tightly enough that the outcome can be objectively verified.", "Record expert demonstrations: Set up your own environment for the task (files staged, add-ons and reference assets in place) and record yourself executing it end to end with the provided capture tooling, producing a complete trace of actions, interface state, and file changes.", "Document the workflow step by step: Log the steps you took in a form another expert could follow and reproduce, in clear professional English.", "Define verification and success criteria: Specify what the finished result must satisfy, which intermediate milestones mark real progress, and which common wrong paths should not be credited \u2014 the rubric a grader uses to score an agent''s attempt.", "Cover the range of difficulty: Produce tasks from single-tool operations up to long, multi-step workflows that cross applications (reference gathered in a browser, assets from a file manager, delivery into a target format).", "Review and quality-check others'' work: For those who move into QA, audit submitted traces for task realism, recording completeness, step-to-action mapping, and whether the stated success criteria genuinely hold for the result produced.", "Work to project quality standards: Keep recordings free of personal information, use only approved applications, and complete all work using your own expertise \u2014 the use of closed-source AI assistants is contractually prohibited on this project."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=75c3ba66-f87e-4b4b-89f9-e918edb029af&jobPostingId=BLENDER-26-123');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('85885b8f-d6ee-56f8-849a-cd34fcaa16ff', 'Brand & Strategy Expert', 'sme.careers', 'Data Annotation & RLHF', 'Remote (17 Countries: Bangladesh, Bhutan, Brazil…)', 'Contract', 'Mid Senior Level', '$85/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Brand & Strategy Subject Matter Expert (SME) to review AI-generated brand strategy, positioning, and go-to-market outputs and/or create expert brand and strategy content, evaluating reasoning quality and step-by-step strategic thinking while providing precise written feedback. You will assess solutions for accuracy, clarity, brand fit, and adherence to the prompt; identify issues in customer insight, segmentation, messaging hierarchy, positioning logic, differentiation, competitive analysis, and go-to-market planning; fact-check claims where needed; write high-quality explanations and model deliverables (e.g., positioning statements, messaging frameworks, briefs) that demonstrate correct strategic reasoning; and rate and compare multiple responses based on correctness, usefulness, and reasoning quality.
This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your brand and strategy expertise directly helps improve the world’s premier AI models by making their strategic marketing outputs more rigorous, on-brand, actionable, and clearly explained.

Important:
There is no immediate project for this role; however, if qualified, you will be among the first experts we reach out to when relevant opportunities arise. This will also provide you with access to future projects available through our expert network.


### Responsibilities
• Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts and gold-standard brand/strategy outputs (briefs, frameworks, messaging, GTM plans) to guide AI learning.
• Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to improve strategic rigor, clarity, brand alignment, and practical usefulness.
• Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI outputs for inaccuracies, hallucinated claims, bias, and brand-risk issues; validate reliability across industries and audiences.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree (or higher) in Marketing, Business, Communications, Psychology, or a related field (or equivalent professional experience).
• 5+ years of professional experience in brand strategy, product marketing, strategy consulting, or integrated marketing strategy (agency or in-house).
• Strong command of positioning and messaging (value prop, proof points, objections, narrative, and tone adaptation).
• Demonstrated ability to develop customer insights (qual/quant research interpretation, personas/JTBD, segmentation).
• Strong strategic reasoning: translating ambiguous goals into clear strategy, prioritization, and measurable choices.
• Ability to evaluate and improve deliverables such as brand briefs, messaging hierarchies, campaign concepts, creative strategy, and GTM plans.
• Exceptional attention to detail when spotting weak logic, unsupported claims, misaligned tone, or risky assertions; minimum C1 English proficiency.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Previous experience with AI data training/annotation, editorial QA, strategy ops, or content review workflows is strongly preferred.


### Eligible Countries (17)
Bangladesh, Bhutan, Brazil, Cambodia, Germany, India, Indonesia, Malaysia, Nepal, Pakistan, Singapore, Sri Lanka, Thailand, The Philippines, The United States, Timor Leste, Vietnam', '["Value Proposition", "Differentiation", "Messaging Frameworks", "Brand Voice", "Positioning", "GTM", "Strategic Briefing", "Voice", "English", "Audience Segmentation", "Competitive Analysis", "Brand Tone", "Brand Strategy"]', '["Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts and gold-standard brand/strategy outputs (briefs, frameworks, messaging, GTM plans) to guide AI learning.", "Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to improve strategic rigor, clarity, brand alignment, and practical usefulness.", "Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI outputs for inaccuracies, hallucinated claims, bias, and brand-risk issues; validate reliability across industries and audiences."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=82ab2ef0-70aa-44e0-bee9-1761b3a4e735&jobPostingId=BrandandStrategy-26-112');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('8fc48796-6ab2-596c-8cdf-259ace75c736', 'Bulgarian Language Expert', 'sme.careers', 'Languages', 'Remote (Bulgaria)', 'Contract', 'Not Applicable', '$20/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Bulgarian Language Expert (SME) to review AI-generated Bulgarian content and/or create high-quality Bulgarian reference content, evaluating language quality and step-by-step reasoning while providing precise written feedback. You will assess outputs for accuracy, fluency, grammar, spelling, tone, cultural appropriateness, and adherence to the prompt; identify errors in meaning, mistranslation, register, ambiguity, unnatural phrasing, terminology, and logical consistency; fact-check claims when needed; write high-quality rewrites and model answers that demonstrate best practices in Bulgarian writing; and rate and compare multiple AI responses based on correctness and overall quality.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your Bulgarian expertise directly helps improve the world’s premier AI models by making their Bulgarian language output more natural, reliable, culturally accurate, and clearly written.


### Responsibilities
• Develop AI Training Content: Create prompts and gold-standard Bulgarian answers across multiple domains, including general knowledge, customer support, education, conversational writing, translation, localization, and culturally sensitive content.
• Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI outputs to improve fluency, correctness, tone match, register consistency, meaning preservation, terminology quality, and cultural appropriateness.
• Ensure Model Integrity: Detect unsafe or misleading content, factual hallucinations, bias, mistranslations, ambiguity, policy-risk language, and culturally inappropriate phrasing; validate reliability across use cases.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree or higher in Linguistics, Bulgarian Language, Bulgarian Literature, English Literature, Communications, Journalism, Translation, or a related field, or equivalent professional experience.
• Native or near-native Bulgarian proficiency, with strong reading and writing skills required.
• Strong professional proficiency in English, minimum C1, to follow guidelines and provide detailed feedback in English.
• 3+ years of professional experience in writing, editing, localization, translation, content QA, journalism, education, or related language-focused work.
• Deep understanding of Bulgarian grammar, spelling conventions, punctuation, Cyrillic script, definite articles, verb aspect, verb tense, mood, word order, tone, and style—able to explain why something is wrong and how to fix it.
• Comfortable handling multiple registers, including formal, neutral, conversational, professional, educational, and public-facing Bulgarian, depending on audience and project requirements.
• High attention to detail when spotting subtle meaning shifts, awkward literal translations, incorrect article usage, verb-aspect errors, hallucinated claims, Russian- or English-influenced phrasing, or culturally mismatched wording.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Prior experience with AI data training/annotation, translation QA, editorial QA, localization QA, or rubric-based evaluation is strongly preferred.', '["Style", "Copyediting", "Translation Quality Review", "Bulgarian", "Localization", "Fact-Checking", "Tone & Register", "English", "Proofreading", "Cultural Context", "Grammar"]', '["Develop AI Training Content: Create prompts and gold-standard Bulgarian answers across multiple domains, including general knowledge, customer support, education, conversational writing, translation, localization, and culturally sensitive content.", "Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI outputs to improve fluency, correctness, tone match, register consistency, meaning preservation, terminology quality, and cultural appropriateness.", "Ensure Model Integrity: Detect unsafe or misleading content, factual hallucinations, bias, mistranslations, ambiguity, policy-risk language, and culturally inappropriate phrasing; validate reliability across use cases."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=45e38c7c-7c2e-480a-8a3c-ef8fdd2f447c&jobPostingId=Bulgarian-26-193');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('03e2ae50-dc9e-561c-bf5e-f662eaff4c73', 'Bulgarian Team Lead', 'sme.careers', 'Languages', 'Remote (Bulgaria)', 'Contract', 'Mid Senior Level', '$25/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Bulgarian Quality Assurance Lead (QAL) to oversee quality, consistency, and trainer performance across Bulgarian AI training projects. You will review AI-generated Bulgarian content and trainer/QA work, evaluate output quality against project guidelines, provide precise written feedback, and ensure that all contributors follow the expected quality standards.

You will assess work for accuracy, fluency, grammar, spelling, tone, cultural appropriateness, meaning preservation, instruction-following, formatting, and adherence to project-specific rubrics. You will spot recurring quality issues, communicate updates to trainers and QAs, support onboarding, maintain documentation, and help activate contributors who are not working consistently. This role requires strong Bulgarian and English skills, excellent attention to detail, structured communication, and the ability to manage quality workflows across remote teams.

