INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('9edf737b-6e9d-5fc0-b5b4-75ffa3c4f91a', 'CBRN Specialist', 'sme.careers', 'Science', 'Remote (31 Countries: Australia, Austria, Belgium…)', 'Contract', 'Not Applicable', '$0 - $100/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a CBRN Specialist (SME) to review AI-generated content related to chemical, biological, radiological, and nuclear safety topics and/or create high-quality reference content that supports safe, accurate, policy-aligned AI behavior. You will evaluate technical accuracy, safety framing, terminology, risk awareness, and reasoning quality while providing precise written feedback.

You will assess outputs for correctness, clarity, responsible handling of hazardous topics, appropriate refusal/redirection where needed, and adherence to project guidelines. You will identify errors in CBRN terminology, hazard classification, emergency preparedness, exposure risk, protective measures, public-safety communication, regulatory framing, and scientific interpretation. You will also flag unsafe, operationally enabling, misleading, or overconfident content and help ensure that model responses remain useful without providing dangerous instructions.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your CBRN expertise directly helps improve the world’s premier AI models by making their responses safer, more accurate, more responsible, and better aligned with public-safety expectations.


### Responsibilities
• Review CBRN-related AI content: Evaluate AI-generated responses involving chemical, biological, radiological, nuclear, hazardous-material, emergency-preparedness, and public-safety topics for accuracy, safety, and guideline alignment.
• Identify unsafe or enabling content: Flag outputs that provide dangerous procedural detail, acquisition guidance, weaponization support, evasion tactics, unsafe lab guidance, harmful exposure advice, or other misuse-enabling content.
• Develop safe reference content: Create gold-standard examples that answer benign CBRN questions responsibly while avoiding operationally dangerous instructions.
• Optimize AI safety behavior: Evaluate and rank model outputs based on safe handling, correct risk framing, appropriate refusals, helpful redirection, scientific accuracy, and clarity.
• Ensure model integrity: Detect hallucinated claims, incorrect hazard classifications, misleading risk statements, overconfident conclusions, poor escalation guidance, or unsafe recommendations.
• Support policy-aligned review: Apply project rubrics consistently and provide clear written feedback explaining why content is safe, unsafe, incomplete, or technically incorrect.
• Maintain technical quality: Ensure CBRN-related content uses precise terminology, avoids exaggeration or minimization of risks, and communicates safety information in a responsible, user-appropriate way.
• Escalate sensitive cases: Flag ambiguous, high-risk, or potentially harmful content for additional review according to project guidelines.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree or higher in Chemistry, Biology, Microbiology, Public Health, Toxicology, Nuclear Engineering, Radiation Science, Emergency Management, Environmental Health & Safety, Biosecurity, Security Studies, or a related field, or equivalent professional experience.
• Strong professional proficiency in English, minimum C1, to follow guidelines and provide detailed written feedback in English.
• 3+ years of professional experience in CBRN safety, emergency preparedness, hazardous materials, biosafety, radiation safety, public health, environmental health and safety, defense/security analysis, technical review, or related work.
• Strong understanding of chemical, biological, radiological, and nuclear hazard categories, including safe high-level risk assessment, exposure pathways, protective concepts, emergency communication, and public-safety principles.
• Ability to evaluate CBRN-related AI outputs for accuracy, safety, completeness, policy alignment, and potential misuse risk.
• Comfortable identifying unsafe instructions, operationally enabling details, inappropriate specificity, misleading hazard claims, inaccurate emergency advice, or unsupported technical conclusions.
• Familiarity with safety frameworks, emergency-response concepts, biosafety levels, hazardous-material communication, radiation protection principles, decontamination concepts, incident reporting, and public-health guidance is preferred.
• High attention to detail when reviewing terminology, units, exposure concepts, risk levels, safety disclaimers, escalation guidance, and sensitive technical boundaries.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Prior experience with AI safety, data annotation, technical QA, policy review, risk assessment, red-team review, scientific review, or rubric-based evaluation is strongly preferred.


### Eligible Countries (31)
Australia, Austria, Belgium, Bulgaria, Canada, Croatia, Cyprus, Denmark, Estonia, Finland, France, Germany, Hungary, Ireland, Italy, Latvia, Lithuania, Luxembourg, Malta, New Zealand, Poland, Portugal, Romania, Slovakia, Slovenia, Spain, Sweden, The Czech Republic, The United Kingdom, The United States, the Netherlands', '["CBRN", "Radiological Safety", "Chemical Safety", "Hazard Communication", "AI Safety", "Risk Review", "Nuclear Safety", "Biological Safety", "Emergency Preparedness", "English"]', '["Review CBRN-related AI content: Evaluate AI-generated responses involving chemical, biological, radiological, nuclear, hazardous-material, emergency-preparedness, and public-safety topics for accuracy, safety, and guideline alignment.", "Identify unsafe or enabling content: Flag outputs that provide dangerous procedural detail, acquisition guidance, weaponization support, evasion tactics, unsafe lab guidance, harmful exposure advice, or other misuse-enabling content.", "Develop safe reference content: Create gold-standard examples that answer benign CBRN questions responsibly while avoiding operationally dangerous instructions.", "Optimize AI safety behavior: Evaluate and rank model outputs based on safe handling, correct risk framing, appropriate refusals, helpful redirection, scientific accuracy, and clarity.", "Ensure model integrity: Detect hallucinated claims, incorrect hazard classifications, misleading risk statements, overconfident conclusions, poor escalation guidance, or unsafe recommendations.", "Support policy-aligned review: Apply project rubrics consistently and provide clear written feedback explaining why content is safe, unsafe, incomplete, or technically incorrect.", "Maintain technical quality: Ensure CBRN-related content uses precise terminology, avoids exaggeration or minimization of risks, and communicates safety information in a responsible, user-appropriate way.", "Escalate sensitive cases: Flag ambiguous, high-risk, or potentially harmful content for additional review according to project guidelines."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=92fc5ff8-9636-434a-9e73-dfa8eaa26608&jobPostingId=CBRN-26-508');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('cdcada14-2726-5e3b-b452-45bcf73400b4', 'Cantonese Quality Assurance Lead (QAL)', 'sme.careers', 'Languages', 'Remote (Hong Kong)', 'Contract', 'Mid Senior Level', '$40/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Chinese (Traditional) Hong Kong / Cantonese Quality Assurance Lead (QAL) to oversee quality, consistency, and trainer performance across Traditional Chinese AI training projects for the Hong Kong market. You will review AI-generated Traditional Chinese Hong Kong / Cantonese-influenced content and trainer/QA work, evaluate output quality against project guidelines, provide precise written feedback, and ensure that all contributors follow the expected quality standards.

You will assess work for accuracy, fluency, grammar, spelling, punctuation, tone, cultural appropriateness, meaning preservation, instruction-following, formatting, and adherence to project-specific rubrics. You will spot recurring quality issues, communicate updates to trainers and QAs, support onboarding, maintain documentation, and help activate contributors who are not working consistently. This role requires strong Traditional Chinese Hong Kong writing skills, Cantonese language judgment, and English communication skills, as well as excellent attention to detail, structured communication, and the ability to manage quality workflows across remote teams.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your Traditional Chinese Hong Kong / Cantonese quality leadership will directly help improve the world’s premier AI models by ensuring that training data for Hong Kong users is natural, accurate, culturally appropriate, well-documented, and aligned with client expectations.

Selection process involves an AI interview, a domain-specific task, and an interview with a recruiter.

Important:
There is no immediate project for this role; however, if qualified, you will be among the first experts we reach out to when relevant opportunities arise. This will also provide you with access to future projects available through our expert network.


### Responsibilities
• Quality monitoring: Spot-check Traditional Chinese Hong Kong / Cantonese items, identify quality issues, provide ongoing feedback through DMs, and escalate recurring or critical issues.
• Trainer and QA communication: Update trainers and QAs on Discord about new item guidelines, project changes, workflow updates, and quality expectations.
• Question handling: Respond to trainer/QA questions clearly and promptly, especially around Cantonese-influenced wording, Hong Kong Traditional Chinese writing conventions, register, punctuation, translation fidelity, cultural context, localization terminology, English code-switching, and edge cases.
• Trainer/QA activation management: DM contributors who are inactive or not working, encourage activation, track follow-ups, and flag availability issues when needed.
• Documentation: Create and maintain Traditional Chinese Hong Kong / Cantonese project documentation, including style guides, trackers, FAQs, quality notes, examples, honeypots, and onboarding materials.
• Onboarding and training: Schedule and run onboarding/training calls with trainers and QAs to explain project expectations, workflows, rubrics, quality standards, and Hong Kong-specific Traditional Chinese / Cantonese style requirements.
• Quality alignment: Ensure all trainers and QAs apply Traditional Chinese Hong Kong / Cantonese guidelines consistently and understand updates as projects evolve.
• Process improvement: Identify recurring quality gaps, propose workflow improvements, and help build scalable QA processes for Traditional Chinese Hong Kong / Cantonese projects.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Chinese, Traditional Chinese, Cantonese, Linguistics, Translation, Communications, Journalism, English, Education, Quality Assurance, or a relevant domain/related field.
• Native or near-native Traditional Chinese proficiency for Hong Kong, with strong reading and writing skills.
• Strong understanding of Cantonese and Hong Kong Traditional Chinese usage, including Cantonese-influenced written Chinese, Hong Kong terminology, tone, register, punctuation, formatting conventions, and cultural context.
• Strong grasp of the English language to follow project guidelines, communicate with teams, and provide clear feedback in English.
• 3+ years of professional experience in Traditional Chinese writing, Cantonese/Hong Kong Chinese editing, translation, localization, content QA, AI training, education, annotation, or related language-review workflows.
• Comfortable handling Hong Kong-specific usage, including Cantonese-influenced phrasing when required, formal written Chinese, local vocabulary, product/UI localization norms, English code-switching where appropriate, and audience adaptation for Hong Kong users.
• Ability to evaluate Traditional Chinese Hong Kong / Cantonese content against detailed rubrics and identify issues such as Simplified Chinese leakage, Taiwan terminology mismatch, mainland Mandarin terminology, unnatural Cantonese-influenced phrasing, mistranslation, literal phrasing, unnatural tone, hallucinated claims, ambiguity, or inconsistent terminology.
• Experience leading or supporting remote teams of trainers, annotators, reviewers, editors, or QAs is strongly preferred.
• Comfortable working in fast-moving remote environments using tools such as Discord, Google Sheets, Google Docs, trackers, dashboards, and project management systems.
• Highly detail-oriented and organized, with the ability to maintain style guides, FAQs, trackers, onboarding materials, honeypots, and other quality documentation.
• Experience with AI training, data annotation, large language models, prompt/response evaluation, or rubric-based LLM QA is a strong plus.', '["LLM Evaluation", "Hong Kong Chinese", "Translation Quality Review", "Cantonese", "Traditional Chinese", "Style Guides", "Chinese Quality Assurance", "AI Training", "English", "Localization QA"]', '["Quality monitoring: Spot-check Traditional Chinese Hong Kong / Cantonese items, identify quality issues, provide ongoing feedback through DMs, and escalate recurring or critical issues.", "Trainer and QA communication: Update trainers and QAs on Discord about new item guidelines, project changes, workflow updates, and quality expectations.", "Question handling: Respond to trainer/QA questions clearly and promptly, especially around Cantonese-influenced wording, Hong Kong Traditional Chinese writing conventions, register, punctuation, translation fidelity, cultural context, localization terminology, English code-switching, and edge cases.", "Trainer/QA activation management: DM contributors who are inactive or not working, encourage activation, track follow-ups, and flag availability issues when needed.", "Documentation: Create and maintain Traditional Chinese Hong Kong / Cantonese project documentation, including style guides, trackers, FAQs, quality notes, examples, honeypots, and onboarding materials.", "Onboarding and training: Schedule and run onboarding/training calls with trainers and QAs to explain project expectations, workflows, rubrics, quality standards, and Hong Kong-specific Traditional Chinese / Cantonese style requirements.", "Quality alignment: Ensure all trainers and QAs apply Traditional Chinese Hong Kong / Cantonese guidelines consistently and understand updates as projects evolve.", "Process improvement: Identify recurring quality gaps, propose workflow improvements, and help build scalable QA processes for Traditional Chinese Hong Kong / Cantonese projects."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=3c12692f-5c7b-4c02-9144-36ffc1bf7553&jobPostingId=CantoneseQAL-26-186');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('91002f27-47d1-52ae-95d4-73da32730d53', 'Canva Specialist', 'sme.careers', 'Data Annotation & RLHF', 'Remote (3 Countries: Bangladesh, India, Pakistan…)', 'Contract', 'Not Applicable', '$0 - $15/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Canva Specialist (SME) to create realistic, challenging computer-based tasks using Canva and related design workflows. You will design practical Canva tasks, document them clearly in SuperAnnotate, ensure your setup supports the task, and record yourself executing the task on your computer.

Tasks may include creating social media posts, presentations, flyers, posters, brand assets, templates, infographics, resumes, marketing graphics, image editing, layout adjustments, export workflows, or collaborative design tasks. Your work will help train advanced AI models to better understand how real users complete visual design tasks in browser-based tools.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your Canva expertise directly helps improve the world’s premier AI models by teaching them how real users complete practical design, marketing, presentation, and layout workflows.


### Responsibilities
• Create realistic Canva tasks: Come up with realistic and challenging tasks that can be executed on the computer using Canva, then document the task clearly in SuperAnnotate.
• Prepare the work environment: Ensure your setup supports the task, including having Canva access, files available, images/assets prepared, brand details ready, and any required references prepared before recording.
• Record task execution: Record yourself executing the Canva task on your computer while following project instructions and ensuring the workflow is clear, complete, and realistic.
• Document task context: Provide enough task context, steps, goals, files, assets, and notes so reviewers can understand what the task is and how it was completed.
• Demonstrate practical software use: Complete workflows involving templates, text editing, layout changes, image placement, branding, presentations, social posts, flyers, infographics, exports, or sharing where relevant.
• Maintain submission quality: Review your recording and documentation before submission to ensure the task is complete, understandable, realistic, and aligned with project guidelines.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Hands-on experience using Canva for social media graphics, presentations, flyers, posters, templates, brand kits, infographics, or marketing/design workflows.
• English proficiency at B2 level or higher to understand project instructions, document tasks clearly, and communicate with the project team.
• Comfortable using a computer, browser-based tools, files, uploads, downloads, exports, and recording workflows.
• Ability to come up with realistic and challenging Canva tasks that reflect actual design, marketing, admin, sales, education, or content-creation use cases.
• Strong understanding of Canva basics such as templates, elements, text styles, images, layers, alignment, brand kits, colors, spacing, exports, and sharing.
• Ability to ensure your setup supports the task, including having Canva access, files/assets available, images prepared, and any required references ready before recording.
• High attention to detail when preparing the task, executing the workflow, and checking that the recording is complete and understandable.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Additional professional skills are appreciated, including design, marketing, social media, sales, administration, education, branding, content creation, or other computer-based workflows.


### Eligible Countries (3)
Bangladesh, India, Pakistan', '["Social Media Design", "Presentations", "Marketing Design", "Templates", "Canva", "Screen Recording", "Computer Use", "Graphic Design", "Layout Design", "English"]', '["Create realistic Canva tasks: Come up with realistic and challenging tasks that can be executed on the computer using Canva, then document the task clearly in SuperAnnotate.", "Prepare the work environment: Ensure your setup supports the task, including having Canva access, files available, images/assets prepared, brand details ready, and any required references prepared before recording.", "Record task execution: Record yourself executing the Canva task on your computer while following project instructions and ensuring the workflow is clear, complete, and realistic.", "Document task context: Provide enough task context, steps, goals, files, assets, and notes so reviewers can understand what the task is and how it was completed.", "Demonstrate practical software use: Complete workflows involving templates, text editing, layout changes, image placement, branding, presentations, social posts, flyers, infographics, exports, or sharing where relevant.", "Maintain submission quality: Review your recording and documentation before submission to ensure the task is complete, understandable, realistic, and aligned with project guidelines."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=67eb3e5b-efe0-46a7-b84f-dc7bb88cea62&jobPostingId=Canva-26-127');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('015c695b-de04-58c5-a261-4cf2bca4e172', 'Catalan Language Expert', 'sme.careers', 'Languages', 'Remote (Spain)', 'Contract', 'Not Applicable', '$26/hr', 'About SME Careers
As AI systems become more sophisticated, they rely on human knowledge to better understand context and the world. At SME Careers, we partner with leading AI labs to improve how the next generation of intelligent systems learn, reason, and communicate. SME Careers is a fast-growing AI data services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate that provides AI training data to many of the world''s top AI companies and foundation model labs. Your expertise as an Catalan Language Expert will directly help improve the world''s premier AI models. Your expertise will play an important role in shaping the future of AI.

About the Role
As a Catalan Language Expert, you will review AI-generated responses and content in Catalan and English, evaluate reasoning quality and step-by-step problem-solving, and provide expert feedback that helps models produce accurate, logical, and clearly explained answers. You will assess solutions for accuracy, clarity, and adherence to the prompt; identify errors in methodology or conceptual understanding; fact-check information; write high-quality explanations and model solutions; and rate and compare multiple AI responses. This is a remote, hourly-paid contract role with flexible scheduling. SME Careers is a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate that provides AI training data for many of the world''s largest AI companies and foundation model labs. Your work in this role directly helps improve the world''s premier AI models.

What You''ll Do
- Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts in various topics and responses to guide AI learning, ensuring the models reflect a comprehensive understanding of diverse subjects.
- Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to enhance the model''s accuracy, fluency, and contextual relevance.
- Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI models for potential inaccuracies or biases, validating their reliability across use cases.
- Document review decisions and escalation notes in clear, professional English (C1+) so others can reproduce your judgments.
- Perform linguistic quality assurance on Catalan text (grammar, orthography, punctuation, register) using a consistent error taxonomy and rubric-based scoring.
- Fact-check Catalan-language responses against reliable references and flag unverifiable, misleading, or internally inconsistent claims.
- Enforce Catalan locale, register, and style-guide consistency (e.g., Central vs Valencian conventions, formal vs informal address) within each task or project guideline.

What You Bring
- 1–5 years of relevant professional experience in Catalan language work (editing, translation, localization, linguistic QA, content review, or similar).
- Native or near-native written Catalan (C2) with strong command of normative grammar, orthography, punctuation, and register.
- Minimum Bachelor''s degree
- English proficiency: Minimum C1 level.
- Fact-checking capability: ability to verify claims using reputable sources, resolve ambiguities, and document evidence succinctly.
- Linguistic quality assurance experience: applying rubrics/rating scales, consistency checks, and structured error categorization for language quality.
- Previous experience with AI data training, annotation, or evaluating AI-generated content is strongly preferred.
- Able to work independently as a remote contractor: detail-oriented, self-directed, dependable turnaround, and careful handling of confidential project content.

Application & Onboarding Process
1. Apply with your resume/CV highlighting Catalan language work (editing, translation, QA, localization, or content review).
2. Complete a Catalan language screening focused on grammar, usage, and quality judgment.
3. Complete a short fact-checking and linguistic QA exercise to calibrate how you apply guidelines.
4. Sign a contractor agreement and complete identity/payment setup.
5. Attend paid onboarding for project-specific rubrics and begin hourly tasks based on availability.

Job Details
- Company: SME Careers (subsidiary of SuperAnnotate)
- Role: Catalan Language Expert (Mid)
- Employment type: Contract (hourly)
- Location: Remote (Spain)
- Schedule: Flexible hours; task availability varies by project
- Compensation: $22.23–$31.12 USD/hour (based on skills, performance, and task complexity)

Why Join Us
- Flexible, remote contract work that fits around other commitments.
- Work focused on Catalan language accuracy, clarity, and factual reliability.
- Clear rubrics and structured feedback that make quality expectations explicit.
- Exposure to a steady stream of real-world Catalan language edge cases (terminology, register, dialect choices, and fact-checking).


### Responsibilities
• Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts in various topics and responses to guide AI learning, ensuring the models reflect a comprehensive understanding of diverse subjects.
• Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to enhance the model''s accuracy, fluency, and contextual relevance.
• Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI models for potential inaccuracies or biases, validating their reliability across use cases.
• Document review decisions and escalation notes in clear, professional English (C1+) so others can reproduce your judgments.
• Perform linguistic quality assurance on Catalan text (grammar, orthography, punctuation, register) using a consistent error taxonomy and rubric-based scoring.
• Fact-check Catalan-language responses against reliable references and flag unverifiable, misleading, or internally inconsistent claims.
• Enforce Catalan locale, register, and style-guide consistency (e.g., Central vs Valencian conventions, formal vs informal address) within each task or project guideline.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• 1–5 years of relevant professional experience in Catalan language work (editing, translation, localization, linguistic QA, content review, or similar).
• Native or near-native written Catalan (C2) with strong command of normative grammar, orthography, punctuation, and register.
• Minimum Bachelor''s degree in Linguistics, Translation and Interpreting, Catalan Philology, Journalism, or equivalent practical experience.
• English proficiency: Minimum C1 level.
• Fact-checking capability: ability to verify claims using reputable sources, resolve ambiguities, and document evidence succinctly.
• Linguistic quality assurance experience: applying rubrics/rating scales, consistency checks, and structured error categorization for language quality.
• Previous experience with AI data training, annotation, or evaluating AI-generated content is strongly preferred.
• Able to work independently as a remote contractor: detail-oriented, self-directed, dependable turnaround, and careful handling of confidential project content.', '["Catalan", "Fact-Checking", "English", "Linguistic Quality Assurance"]', '["Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts in various topics and responses to guide AI learning, ensuring the models reflect a comprehensive understanding of diverse subjects.", "Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to enhance the model''s accuracy, fluency, and contextual relevance.", "Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI models for potential inaccuracies or biases, validating their reliability across use cases.", "Document review decisions and escalation notes in clear, professional English (C1+) so others can reproduce your judgments.", "Perform linguistic quality assurance on Catalan text (grammar, orthography, punctuation, register) using a consistent error taxonomy and rubric-based scoring.", "Fact-check Catalan-language responses against reliable references and flag unverifiable, misleading, or internally inconsistent claims.", "Enforce Catalan locale, register, and style-guide consistency (e.g., Central vs Valencian conventions, formal vs informal address) within each task or project guideline."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=842ac888-8e53-40c5-a471-861f5f7a7720&jobPostingId=Catalan-17389');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('9c0ce441-d030-5ac6-b67d-55d0bbbba484', 'Catalan Team Lead', 'sme.careers', 'Data Annotation & RLHF', 'Remote (2 Countries: France, Spain…)', 'Contract', 'Not Applicable', '$36/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Catalan Quality Assurance Lead (QAL) to oversee quality, consistency, and trainer performance across Catalan AI training projects. You will review AI-generated Catalan content and trainer/QA work, evaluate output quality against project guidelines, provide precise written feedback, and ensure that all contributors follow the expected quality standards.

You will assess work for accuracy, fluency, grammar, spelling, tone, cultural appropriateness, meaning preservation, instruction-following, formatting, and adherence to project-specific rubrics. You will spot recurring quality issues, communicate updates to trainers and QAs, support onboarding, maintain documentation, and help activate contributors who are not working consistently. This role requires strong Catalan and English skills, excellent attention to detail, structured communication, and the ability to manage quality workflows across remote teams.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world''s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your Catalan quality leadership will directly help improve the world''s premier AI models by ensuring that Catalan training data is natural, accurate, culturally appropriate, well-documented, and aligned with client expectations.

Selection process involves an AI interview, a domain-specific task, and an interview with a recruiter.


### Responsibilities
• Quality monitoring: Spot-check Catalan items, identify quality issues, provide ongoing feedback through DMs, and escalate recurring or critical issues.
• Trainer and QA communication: Update trainers and QAs on Discord about new item guidelines, project changes, workflow updates, and quality expectations.
• Question handling: Respond to trainer/QA questions clearly and promptly, especially around Catalan wording, accentuation, weak pronouns, register, translation fidelity, Central/Valencian/Balearic variation, castellanismes, cultural context, and edge cases.
• Trainer/QA activation management: DM contributors who are inactive or not working, encourage activation, track follow-ups, and flag availability issues when needed.
• Documentation: Create and maintain Catalan project documentation, including style guides, trackers, FAQs, quality notes, examples, honeypots, and onboarding materials.
• Onboarding and training: Schedule and run onboarding/training calls with trainers and QAs to explain project expectations, workflows, rubrics, quality standards, and Catalan-specific style requirements.
• Quality alignment: Ensure all trainers and QAs apply Catalan language guidelines consistently and understand updates as projects evolve.
• Process improvement: Identify recurring quality gaps, propose workflow improvements, and help build scalable QA processes for Catalan-language projects.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor''s or Master''s degree in Catalan, Linguistics, Translation, Communications, Journalism, English, Education, Quality Assurance, or a relevant domain/related field.
• Native or near-native Catalan proficiency with strong reading and writing skills.
• Strong grasp of the English language to follow project guidelines, communicate with teams, and provide clear feedback in English.
• 1+ years of professional experience in Catalan writing, editing, translation, localization, content QA, AI training, education, annotation, or related language-review workflows.
• Strong understanding of Catalan grammar, spelling conventions, punctuation, accentuation (accent agut vs. greu, dièresi), the geminated l·l (punt volat), apostrophation, weak pronouns (pronoms febles), gender and number agreement, tone, register, and cultural context.
• Comfortable distinguishing Catalan variants where relevant — Central Catalan, Valencian, and Balearic — including vocabulary, spelling, terminology, and localization expectations, and able to apply the appropriate standard (IEC/AVL).
• Ability to evaluate Catalan content against detailed rubrics and identify issues such as mistranslation, literal phrasing, unnatural tone, castellanismes (Spanish interference), missing or incorrect diacritics, incorrect pronoun usage, hallucinated claims, ambiguity, or inconsistent terminology.
• Experience supporting remote teams of trainers, annotators, reviewers, editors, or QAs is strongly preferred.
• Highly detail-oriented and organized, with the ability to maintain style guides, FAQs, trackers, onboarding materials, honeypots, and other quality documentation.
• Experience with AI training, data annotation, large language models, prompt/response evaluation, or rubric-based LLM QA is a strong plus.


### Eligible Countries (2)
France, Spain', '["Catalan", "AI Training", "Documentation"]', '["Quality monitoring: Spot-check Catalan items, identify quality issues, provide ongoing feedback through DMs, and escalate recurring or critical issues.", "Trainer and QA communication: Update trainers and QAs on Discord about new item guidelines, project changes, workflow updates, and quality expectations.", "Question handling: Respond to trainer/QA questions clearly and promptly, especially around Catalan wording, accentuation, weak pronouns, register, translation fidelity, Central/Valencian/Balearic variation, castellanismes, cultural context, and edge cases.", "Trainer/QA activation management: DM contributors who are inactive or not working, encourage activation, track follow-ups, and flag availability issues when needed.", "Documentation: Create and maintain Catalan project documentation, including style guides, trackers, FAQs, quality notes, examples, honeypots, and onboarding materials.", "Onboarding and training: Schedule and run onboarding/training calls with trainers and QAs to explain project expectations, workflows, rubrics, quality standards, and Catalan-specific style requirements.", "Quality alignment: Ensure all trainers and QAs apply Catalan language guidelines consistently and understand updates as projects evolve.", "Process improvement: Identify recurring quality gaps, propose workflow improvements, and help build scalable QA processes for Catalan-language projects."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=c55ae792-d310-4ea4-a6ca-446d0e8d4e2d&jobPostingId=CatalanQAL-26-199');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('2b65f9ba-1fa1-56a2-9eaa-6613dd350a5c', 'Chemical Engineer', 'sme.careers', 'Science', 'Remote (21 Countries: Australia, Bangladesh, Bhutan…)', 'Contract', 'Associate', '$100/hr', 'If you are a chemical engineer who thrives on technical precision, applied problem-solving, and real-world process reasoning, this is a unique opportunity to contribute directly to how the next generation of AI systems understand and communicate complex chemical engineering concepts. We are looking for chemical engineering specialists who can evaluate, challenge, and refine advanced language models on domain-specific topics. Your expertise as a Chemical Engineer will directly help improve the world’s premier AI models, and will play an important role in shaping the future of AI. This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs.


### Responsibilities
• Evaluate AI-generated responses for technical accuracy, logical soundness, completeness, and clarity across chemical engineering topics.
• Challenge advanced language models with realistic chemical engineering scenarios, calculations, and process-informed reasoning tasks.
• Review and refine AI-generated prompts, model responses, explanations, and step-by-step engineering solutions.
• Provide structured feedback that identifies factual errors, flawed assumptions, missing constraints, unsafe recommendations, unit/consistency mistakes, or incomplete reasoning.
• Assess model performance on topics such as: Material & energy balances, phase behavior, and thermodynamic property use, Unit operations and sizing logic, Distillation/separations design logic and feasibility checks, Process control reasoning, Process safety, Scale-up/manufacturability, operability, and troubleshooting of plant scenarios
• Help shape AI communication standards for technical chemical engineering content, including how models explain assumptions, limitations, calculations, and professional judgment.
• Ensure AI-generated content reflects sound engineering principles, appropriate safety considerations, and responsible technical communication (including “when to escalate to a licensed engineer/site expert”).


### Requirements & Qualifications
• 4+ years of professional chemical engineering experience, with meaningful hands-on work in process design, plant/operations engineering, process safety, scale-up, manufacturing, utilities, EHS, quality, R&D, controls/automation interfaces, or a closely related chemical engineering specialty.
• Deep knowledge of chemical engineering fundamentals, including material & energy balances, thermodynamics, fluid mechanics, heat & mass transfer, reaction engineering, separations (distillation, absorption, extraction, membranes), unit operations, and process control concepts.
• Strong comfort with engineering calculations, assumptions, constraints, and defensible reasoning (including uncertainty, safety factors, and limitations).
• Bachelor’s degree in Chemical Engineering (or closely related) required; Master’s/PhD, PE/Chartered credentials, or advanced professional certifications strongly preferred.
• Previous experience with AI data training, annotation, red-teaming, or evaluating AI-generated technical content is a strong plus.
• Familiarity with tools and artifacts such as PFDs/P&IDs, Aspen Plus/HYSYS, CHEMCAD, process datasheets, PSM documentation, HAZOP/LOPA, or SOPs is a plus.


### Eligible Countries (21)
Australia, Bangladesh, Bhutan, Brazil, Cambodia, Canada, Germany, India, Indonesia, Malaysia, Nepal, New Zealand, Pakistan, Singapore, Sri Lanka, Thailand, The Philippines, The United Kingdom, The United States, Timor Leste, Vietnam', '[]', '["Evaluate AI-generated responses for technical accuracy, logical soundness, completeness, and clarity across chemical engineering topics.", "Challenge advanced language models with realistic chemical engineering scenarios, calculations, and process-informed reasoning tasks.", "Review and refine AI-generated prompts, model responses, explanations, and step-by-step engineering solutions.", "Provide structured feedback that identifies factual errors, flawed assumptions, missing constraints, unsafe recommendations, unit/consistency mistakes, or incomplete reasoning.", "Assess model performance on topics such as: Material & energy balances, phase behavior, and thermodynamic property use, Unit operations and sizing logic, Distillation/separations design logic and feasibility checks, Process control reasoning, Process safety, Scale-up/manufacturability, operability, and troubleshooting of plant scenarios", "Help shape AI communication standards for technical chemical engineering content, including how models explain assumptions, limitations, calculations, and professional judgment.", "Ensure AI-generated content reflects sound engineering principles, appropriate safety considerations, and responsible technical communication (including \u201cwhen to escalate to a licensed engineer/site expert\u201d)."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=e2f655c6-9bca-45e8-abe3-4e7fee3ed879&jobPostingId=ChemEngineer-26-132');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('b391cc6b-0086-515f-911d-c68583f45cc7', 'Chemical Engineer Quality Assurance Lead (QAL)', 'sme.careers', 'Science', 'Remote (The United States)', 'Contract', 'Mid Senior Level', '$105/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Chemical Engineering Quality Assurance Lead (QAL) to oversee quality, consistency, and trainer performance across chemical engineering AI training projects. You will review AI-generated chemical engineering content and trainer/QA work, evaluate output quality against project guidelines, provide precise written feedback, and ensure that all contributors follow the expected quality standards.

You will assess work for technical accuracy, engineering reasoning, calculation correctness, unit consistency, process safety awareness, standards awareness, clarity, formatting, instruction-following, and adherence to project-specific rubrics. You will spot recurring quality issues, communicate updates to trainers and QAs, support onboarding, maintain documentation, and help activate contributors who are not working consistently. This role requires strong chemical engineering expertise, strong English communication skills, excellent attention to detail, structured communication, and the ability to manage quality workflows across remote technical teams.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your chemical engineering quality leadership will directly help improve the world’s premier AI models by ensuring that engineering training data is accurate, logically sound, clearly explained, well-documented, and aligned with client expectations.

Selection process involves an AI interview, a domain-specific task, and an interview with a recruiter.


### Responsibilities
• Quality monitoring: Spot-check chemical engineering items, identify quality issues, provide ongoing feedback through DMs, and escalate recurring or critical issues.
• Technical review: Evaluate AI-generated engineering explanations, process calculations, mass/energy balances, reaction engineering solutions, separation process reasoning, process-control explanations, diagrams/descriptions, and problem-solving workflows for correctness and clarity.
