• Record task execution: Record yourself executing the ClickUp task on your computer while following project instructions and ensuring the workflow is clear, complete, and realistic.
• Document task context: Provide enough task context, steps, goals, workspace/project details, and notes so reviewers can understand what the task is and how it was completed.
• Demonstrate practical software use: Complete workflows involving task creation, custom fields, views, dashboards, docs, statuses, assignments, deadlines, automations, or project updates where relevant.
• Maintain submission quality: Review your recording and documentation before submission to ensure the task is complete, understandable, realistic, and aligned with project guidelines.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Hands-on experience using ClickUp for task management, project tracking, dashboards, docs, automations, team collaboration, or operations workflows.
• English proficiency at B2 level or higher to understand project instructions, document tasks clearly, and communicate with the project team.
• Comfortable using a computer, browser-based tools, workspaces, files, permissions, and recording workflows.
• Ability to come up with realistic and challenging ClickUp tasks that reflect actual admin, operations, project management, sales, marketing, support, HR, or team-collaboration use cases.
• Strong understanding of ClickUp basics such as workspaces, spaces, folders, lists, tasks, statuses, assignees, due dates, custom fields, views, dashboards, docs, and automations.
• Ability to ensure your setup supports the task, including having ClickUp access, sample workspace data, tasks/projects prepared, and any required references ready before recording.
• High attention to detail when preparing the task, executing the workflow, and checking that the recording is complete and understandable.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Additional professional skills are appreciated, including project management, admin, operations, sales, marketing, HR, customer support, documentation, or other computer-based workflows.


### Eligible Countries (3)
Bangladesh, India, Pakistan', '["Project Management", "Automations", "Admin", "Dashboards", "Screen Recording", "Computer Use", "ClickUp", "English", "Task Management", "Workflows"]', '["Create realistic ClickUp tasks: Come up with realistic and challenging tasks that can be executed on the computer using ClickUp, then document the task clearly in SuperAnnotate.", "Prepare the work environment: Ensure your setup supports the task, including having ClickUp access, workspace/projects prepared, sample tasks available, permissions ready, and references prepared before recording.", "Record task execution: Record yourself executing the ClickUp task on your computer while following project instructions and ensuring the workflow is clear, complete, and realistic.", "Document task context: Provide enough task context, steps, goals, workspace/project details, and notes so reviewers can understand what the task is and how it was completed.", "Demonstrate practical software use: Complete workflows involving task creation, custom fields, views, dashboards, docs, statuses, assignments, deadlines, automations, or project updates where relevant.", "Maintain submission quality: Review your recording and documentation before submission to ensure the task is complete, understandable, realistic, and aligned with project guidelines."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=168d3ac4-0649-47ee-9598-34b42640f200&jobPostingId=ClickUp-26-204');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('396ba28d-92d0-520a-92e4-d2a96203962f', 'Clinical Researcher', 'sme.careers', 'Healthcare', 'Remote (17 Countries: Bangladesh, Bhutan, Brazil…)', 'Contract', 'Mid Senior Level', '$0 - $70/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Clinical Researcher Subject Matter Expert (SME) to review AI-generated clinical research and biomedical content and/or create expert research content, evaluating reasoning quality and step-by-step scientific problem-solving while providing precise written feedback. You will assess solutions for accuracy, clarity, safety, and adherence to the prompt; identify errors in study design, statistics, endpoint selection, bias/confounding, clinical trial methodology, and evidence interpretation; fact-check medical and scientific claims; write high-quality explanations and model solutions that demonstrate correct research reasoning; and rate and compare multiple responses based on correctness and reasoning quality. This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your clinical research expertise directly helps improve the world’s premier AI models by making their evidence appraisal, trial interpretation, and research communication more accurate, reliable, and clearly explained.

Important:
There is no immediate project for this role; however, if qualified, you will be among the first experts we reach out to when relevant opportunities arise. This will also provide you with access to future projects available through our expert network.


### Responsibilities
• Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts and gold-standard answers across clinical research methodology, interpretation, and scientific communication.
• Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to improve correctness, rigor, clarity, and contextual relevance.
• Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI outputs for inaccuracies, misleading evidence interpretation, unsafe recommendations, and bias; validate reliability across use cases.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree (or higher) in a relevant field (e.g., Public Health/MPH, Epidemiology, Biostatistics, Clinical Research, Biomedical Sciences, PharmD, MD/DO, RN, or related).
• 5+ years of professional experience in clinical research (academia, hospitals, CROs, biopharma, public health research, or similar).
• Strong command of clinical research fundamentals: study design, endpoints, inclusion/exclusion criteria, power/sample size intuition, and interpretation of results.
• Comfortable evaluating statistical reasoning (effect sizes, confidence intervals, p-values, multiple comparisons, missing data, sensitivity analyses).
• Deep understanding of bias, confounding, and causality (randomization, blinding, selection bias, measurement bias, survivorship, collider bias).
• Familiarity with clinical trial operations concepts (protocols, deviations, AE/SAE logic, data quality, monitoring) and/or GCP principles is a plus.
• Exceptional attention to detail when fact-checking; minimum C1 English proficiency with strong scientific writing.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Prior experience with AI data training/annotation, medical/scientific editorial QA, systematic reviews, or guideline work is strongly preferred.


### Eligible Countries (17)
Bangladesh, Bhutan, Brazil, Cambodia, Germany, India, Indonesia, Malaysia, Nepal, Pakistan, Singapore, Sri Lanka, Thailand, The Philippines, The United States, Timor Leste, Vietnam', '["Bias & Confounding", "Clinical Trial Design", "Biostatistics", "Regulatory/GCP Awareness", "Study Methodology", "Evidence-Based Medicine", "Data Interpretation", "Confounding", "Epidemiology", "Literature Review", "English", "Bias"]', '["Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts and gold-standard answers across clinical research methodology, interpretation, and scientific communication.", "Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to improve correctness, rigor, clarity, and contextual relevance.", "Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI outputs for inaccuracies, misleading evidence interpretation, unsafe recommendations, and bias; validate reliability across use cases."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=8b9ac2a6-9d4c-45c6-bdd6-7b94b93d31f1&jobPostingId=ClinicalResearcher-26-108');
