Bangladesh, Bhutan, Brazil, Cambodia, Germany, India, Indonesia, Malaysia, Nepal, Pakistan, Singapore, Sri Lanka, Thailand, The Philippines, The United States, Timor Leste, Vietnam', '["Regulatory Compliance", "Third-Party Risk", "Procedures", "Controls Testing", "Regulatory Research", "Reporting", "Monitoring", "Risk Assessment", "GRC", "English", "Audit Readiness", "Policy"]', '["Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts and gold-standard compliance outputs (policies, control descriptions, monitoring plans, risk assessments, regulatory summaries).", "Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to improve correctness, defensibility, clarity, and practical usefulness.", "Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI outputs for inaccuracies, unsafe/noncompliant guidance, misleading certainty, and bias; validate reliability across scenarios."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=09715847-5bfa-4fb4-bcf3-45deee98c237&jobPostingId=ComplandRegulat-26-145');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('28c19bea-8f10-5c3c-a410-35c3f2d3a53f', 'Computer Science & IT Team Lead', 'sme.careers', 'Finance', 'Remote (India)', 'Contract', 'Not Applicable', '$20/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Computer Science & IT Quality Assurance Lead (QAL) to oversee quality, consistency, and trainer performance across computer science, IT, software, systems, and technical AI training projects. You will review AI-generated computer science/IT content and trainer/QA work, evaluate output quality against project guidelines, provide precise written feedback, and ensure that all contributors follow the expected quality standards.

