• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor environment.', '["Issue Resolution", "Conflict Resolution", "Customer Service", "Escalation Management", "AI Training", "Voice Support", "English", "Complaint Handling", "Call Center"]', '["Develop AI Training Content: Create natural, human-enacted customer service conversations across realistic support scenarios.", "Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to enhance the model''s accuracy, fluency, and contextual relevance.", "Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI models for potential inaccuracies or biases, validating their reliability across use cases."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=f6adb111-73c6-4dcf-971c-6c464eb411b4&jobPostingId=CustomerService-26-130');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('2a6debf7-2a9c-5be4-9a8d-2b11bbb4c94b', 'Czech Language Expert', 'sme.careers', 'Languages', 'Remote (The Czech Republic)', 'Contract', 'Not Applicable', '$25/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Czech Language Expert (SME) to review AI-generated Czech content and/or create high-quality Czech reference content, evaluating language quality and step-by-step reasoning while providing precise written feedback. You will assess outputs for accuracy, fluency, grammar, spelling, tone, cultural appropriateness, and adherence to the prompt; identify errors in meaning, mistranslation, register, ambiguity, unnatural phrasing, terminology, and logical consistency; fact-check claims when needed; write high-quality rewrites and model answers that demonstrate best practices in Czech writing; and rate and compare multiple AI responses based on correctness and overall quality.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your Czech expertise directly helps improve the world’s premier AI models by making their Czech language output more natural, reliable, culturally accurate, and clearly written.


### Responsibilities
• Develop AI Training Content: Create prompts and gold-standard Czech answers across multiple domains, including general knowledge, customer support, education, conversational writing, translation, localization, and culturally sensitive content.
• Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI outputs to improve fluency, correctness, tone match, register consistency, meaning preservation, terminology quality, and cultural appropriateness.
• Ensure Model Integrity: Detect unsafe or misleading content, factual hallucinations, bias, mistranslations, ambiguity, policy-risk language, and culturally inappropriate phrasing; validate reliability across use cases.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree or higher in Linguistics, Czech Language, Czech Literature, English Literature, Communications, Journalism, Translation, or a related field, or equivalent professional experience.
• Native or near-native Czech proficiency, with strong reading and writing skills required.
• Strong professional proficiency in English, minimum C1, to follow guidelines and provide detailed feedback in English.
• 3+ years of professional experience in writing, editing, localization, translation, content QA, journalism, education, or related language-focused work.
• Deep understanding of Czech grammar, spelling conventions, punctuation, diacritics, cases, declension, conjugation, aspect, word order, tone, and style—able to explain why something is wrong and how to fix it.
• Comfortable handling multiple registers, including formal, neutral, conversational, professional, educational, and public-facing Czech, depending on audience and project requirements.
• High attention to detail when spotting subtle meaning shifts, awkward literal translations, incorrect case endings, agreement errors, hallucinated claims, Slovak- or English-influenced phrasing, or culturally mismatched wording.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Prior experience with AI data training/annotation, translation QA, editorial QA, localization QA, or rubric-based evaluation is strongly preferred.', '["Style", "Copyediting", "Translation Quality Review", "Localization", "Fact-Checking", "Tone & Register", "English", "Czech", "Proofreading", "Cultural Context", "Grammar"]', '["Develop AI Training Content: Create prompts and gold-standard Czech answers across multiple domains, including general knowledge, customer support, education, conversational writing, translation, localization, and culturally sensitive content.", "Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI outputs to improve fluency, correctness, tone match, register consistency, meaning preservation, terminology quality, and cultural appropriateness.", "Ensure Model Integrity: Detect unsafe or misleading content, factual hallucinations, bias, mistranslations, ambiguity, policy-risk language, and culturally inappropriate phrasing; validate reliability across use cases."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=24c70948-0d5c-49ec-aafe-560629901ade&jobPostingId=Czech-26-187');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('503864d5-4500-5f9d-a29b-c92150a0903e', 'Czech Team Lead', 'sme.careers', 'Languages', 'Remote (The Czech Republic)', 'Contract', 'Mid Senior Level', '$30/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Czech Quality Assurance Lead (QAL) to oversee quality, consistency, and trainer performance across Czech AI training projects. You will review AI-generated Czech content and trainer/QA work, evaluate output quality against project guidelines, provide precise written feedback, and ensure that all contributors follow the expected quality standards.

You will assess work for accuracy, fluency, grammar, spelling, tone, cultural appropriateness, meaning preservation, instruction-following, formatting, and adherence to project-specific rubrics. You will spot recurring quality issues, communicate updates to trainers and QAs, support onboarding, maintain documentation, and help activate contributors who are not working consistently. This role requires strong Czech and English skills, excellent attention to detail, structured communication, and the ability to manage quality workflows across remote teams.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your Czech quality leadership will directly help improve the world’s premier AI models by ensuring that Czech training data is natural, accurate, culturally appropriate, well-documented, and aligned with client expectations.

Selection process involves an AI interview, a domain-specific task, and an interview with a recruiter.


### Responsibilities
• Quality monitoring: Spot-check Czech items, identify quality issues, provide ongoing feedback through DMs, and escalate recurring or critical issues.
• Trainer and QA communication: Update trainers and QAs on Discord about new item guidelines, project changes, workflow updates, and quality expectations.
• Question handling: Respond to trainer/QA questions clearly and promptly, especially around Czech wording, grammar, diacritics, register, translation fidelity, cultural context, terminology, and edge cases.
• Trainer/QA activation management: DM contributors who are inactive or not working, encourage activation, track follow-ups, and flag availability issues when needed.
• Documentation: Create and maintain Czech project documentation, including style guides, trackers, FAQs, quality notes, examples, honeypots, and onboarding materials.
• Onboarding and training: Schedule and run onboarding/training calls with trainers and QAs to explain project expectations, workflows, rubrics, quality standards, and Czech-specific style requirements.
• Quality alignment: Ensure all trainers and QAs apply Czech language guidelines consistently and understand updates as projects evolve.
• Process improvement: Identify recurring quality gaps, propose workflow improvements, and help build scalable QA processes for Czech-language projects.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Czech, Linguistics, Translation, Communications, Journalism, English, Education, Quality Assurance, or a relevant domain/related field.
• Native or near-native Czech proficiency with strong reading and writing skills.
• Strong grasp of the English language to follow project guidelines, communicate with teams, and provide clear feedback in English.
• 3+ years of professional experience in Czech writing, editing, translation, localization, content QA, AI training, education, annotation, or related language-review workflows.
• Strong understanding of Czech grammar, spelling conventions, punctuation, diacritics, declension, gender agreement, word order, tone, register, and cultural context.
• Ability to evaluate Czech content against detailed rubrics and identify issues such as mistranslation, literal phrasing, unnatural tone, incorrect case usage, missing diacritics, hallucinated claims, ambiguity, or inconsistent terminology.
• Experience leading or supporting remote teams of trainers, annotators, reviewers, editors, or QAs is strongly preferred.
• Comfortable working in fast-moving remote environments using tools such as Discord, Google Sheets, Google Docs, trackers, dashboards, and project management systems.
• Highly detail-oriented and organized, with the ability to maintain style guides, FAQs, trackers, onboarding materials, honeypots, and other quality documentation.
