• Experience with AI training, data annotation, LLM evaluation, spreadsheet QA, or rubric-based review is a strong plus.', '["LLM Evaluation", "Spreadsheet QA", "Data Analysis", "Formula Review", "Financial Modeling", "Excel", "AI Training", "Documentation", "Trainer Feedback", "Pivot Tables"]', '["Spot-check Excel/spreadsheet items and provide feedback through DMs.", "Review AI-generated formulas, spreadsheet workflows, financial models, data-cleaning steps, pivot-table guidance, charts, and explanations.", "Communicate guideline changes and Excel-specific standards on Discord.", "Answer questions around formulas, references, lookup logic, dynamic arrays, pivot tables, Power Query, modeling assumptions, and rubric interpretation.", "DM inactive contributors and manage activation follow-ups.", "Create Excel documentation, style guides, examples, trackers, FAQs, honeypots, and onboarding materials.", "Run onboarding/training calls for Excel contributors.", "Flag misleading analysis, fragile spreadsheet logic, incorrect formulas, or risky business/financial assumptions.", "Improve QA processes based on recurring spreadsheet-quality gaps."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=f4c522a3-fda4-424d-895a-c21b36d2233b&jobPostingId=ExcelQAL-25-615');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('1db43ce3-be6f-5af4-89d9-2aef705f6402', 'Explosives & Energetic Materials Expert for AI Safety Audit', 'sme.careers', 'Science', 'Remote (32 Countries: Australia, Austria, Belgium…)', 'Contract', 'Not Applicable', '$1 - $100/hr', '## Description

SME Careers is hiring explosives and energetic materials professionals to audit how AI models respond to sensitive questions in the field. Each task gives you a user request and the answers three different models gave to it. You classify the request (benign, dual-use or adversarial), mark each answer as safe or unsafe and say why, rank the three against each other, and write the answer the model should have given. For dual-use requests you also note what makes it sensitive, what legitimate purpose it serves, and who should be able to get an answer.

The requests are realistic: what mining and blasting engineers, pyrotechnicians, propellant chemists, bomb technicians, investigators and occasionally bad actors actually ask. Some are ordinary professional questions that models wrongly refuse, and catching those matters as much as catching the dangerous ones.

## Who we''re looking for

Commercial blasting engineers and mining/quarry explosives specialists; military or police EOD and bomb technicians; energetic materials, propellant or pyrotechnics chemists; post-blast investigators and forensic examiners; explosives safety officers and regulators (ATF, HSE, DoD explosives safety, or equivalent). Usually a relevant degree or certification plus five or more years of hands-on professional experience. Experience writing incident reports, safety cases or expert opinions is a strong plus.

## Before you apply

Open only to citizens or permanent residents of the US, UK, Canada, Australia, New Zealand and The European Union


### Responsibilities
• Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts in various topics and responses to guide AI learning, ensuring the models reflect a comprehensive understanding of diverse subjects.
• Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to enhance the model''s accuracy, fluency, and contextual relevance.
• Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI models for potential inaccuracies or biases, validating their reliability across use cases.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree or higher in Chemistry, Chemical Engineering, Materials Science, Energetic Materials, Explosives Engineering, Safety Engineering, Hazardous Materials Management, Environmental Health & Safety, or a closely related field; advanced degree or professional safety certification is a strong plus.
• 3+ years of professional experience in explosives safety, energetic materials, hazardous materials safety, chemical safety, defense safety, industrial safety, EHS, regulatory compliance, risk assessment, technical safety review, or related work.
• Strong understanding of explosives and energetic materials safety concepts, including hazard classification, sensitivity, compatibility, storage principles, transport considerations, environmental conditions, blast/fire risk, and safe handling frameworks.
• Familiarity with safety documentation and frameworks such as Safety Data Sheets, GHS hazard communication, hazardous materials classification, SOPs, risk assessments, incident escalation procedures, and applicable safety/regulatory guidance.
• Ability to review AI-generated explosives or energetic-materials content for technical accuracy, safety alignment, misuse risk, inappropriate specificity, hallucinated claims, and potentially dangerous procedural guidance.
• Strong judgment in distinguishing between safe high-level educational or safety content and content that could enable unsafe handling, synthesis, acquisition, weaponization, evasion, or harmful experimentation.
• Excellent written English skills, with the ability to provide clear, structured feedback explaining why a response is safe, unsafe, incomplete, misleading, or technically incorrect.
• High attention to detail when reviewing terminology, hazard categories, material properties, units, risk assumptions, safety controls, storage/transport considerations, and emergency-response guidance.
• Comfortable applying detailed project rubrics consistently across ambiguous or sensitive scenarios involving explosives, energetic materials, pyrotechnics, propellants, reactive chemicals, or hazardous mixtures.
• Prior experience with AI safety, red-team review, model evaluation, content moderation, data annotation, technical QA, scientific review, EHS review, hazardous-materials review, or rubric-based evaluation is preferred.


### Eligible Countries (32)
Australia, Austria, Belgium, Bulgaria, Canada, Croatia, Cyprus, Denmark, Estonia, Finland, France, Germany, Greece, Hungary, Ireland, Italy, Latvia, Lithuania, Luxembourg, Malta, New Zealand, Poland, Portugal, Romania, Slovakia, Slovenia, Spain, Sweden, The Czech Republic, The United Kingdom, The United States, the Netherlands', '[]', '["Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts in various topics and responses to guide AI learning, ensuring the models reflect a comprehensive understanding of diverse subjects.", "Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to enhance the model''s accuracy, fluency, and contextual relevance.", "Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI models for potential inaccuracies or biases, validating their reliability across use cases."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=fae56a12-f6b1-4604-9614-6e9d12497719&jobPostingId=EXPLOSIVE-26-100');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('e6238ac2-395b-5f77-a353-f904db9187a5', 'Filipino (Tagalog) Language Expert', 'sme.careers', 'Languages', 'Remote (The Philippines)', 'Contract', 'Mid Senior Level', '$20/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Filipino (Tagalog) Language Specialist (SME) to review AI-generated Filipino/Tagalog content and/or create high-quality Tagalog reference content, evaluating language quality and step-by-step reasoning while providing precise written feedback. You will assess outputs for accuracy, fluency, grammar, spelling, tone, cultural appropriateness, and adherence to the prompt; identify errors in meaning, mistranslation, register (formal vs informal), ambiguity, code-switching control (Taglish), and logical consistency; fact-check claims when needed; write high-quality rewrites and model answers that demonstrate best practices in Filipino writing; and rate and compare multiple AI responses based on correctness and overall quality.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your Filipino/Tagalog expertise directly helps improve the world’s premier AI models by making their Filipino language output more natural, reliable, culturally accurate, and clearly written.

Important: There is no immediate project for this role; however, if qualified, you will be among the first experts we reach out to when relevant opportunities arise. This will also provide you with access to future projects available through our expert network.


### Responsibilities
• Develop AI Training Content: Create prompts and gold-standard Filipino/Tagalog answers across multiple domains (general knowledge, customer support, education, conversational writing).
• Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI outputs to improve fluency, correctness, tone match, and cultural appropriateness.
• Ensure Model Integrity: Detect unsafe or misleading content, factual hallucinations, bias, and policy-risk language; validate reliability across use cases.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree (or higher) in Linguistics, Filipino/English Literature, Communications, Journalism, Translation, or a related field (or equivalent professional experience).
• Native or near-native Filipino/Tagalog proficiency (reading and writing required).
• Strong professional proficiency in English (minimum C1) to follow guidelines and provide detailed feedback in English.
• 3+ years of professional experience in writing, editing, localization, translation, content QA, journalism, education, or related language-focused work.
• Deep understanding of Filipino/Tagalog grammar, spelling conventions, punctuation, and style—able to explain why something is wrong and how to fix it.
• Comfortable handling multiple registers (formal/informal), polite forms, and Taglish vs pure Tagalog depending on target audience requirements.
• High attention to detail when spotting subtle meaning shifts, awkward literal translations, hallucinated claims, or culturally mismatched phrasing.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Prior experience with AI data training/annotation, translation QA, editorial QA, or rubric-based evaluation is strongly preferred.', '["Style", "Copyediting", "Translation Quality Review", "Tagalog", "Localization", "Fact-Checking", "Filipino", "Tone & Register", "English", "Proofreading", "Cultural Context", "Grammar"]', '["Develop AI Training Content: Create prompts and gold-standard Filipino/Tagalog answers across multiple domains (general knowledge, customer support, education, conversational writing).", "Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI outputs to improve fluency, correctness, tone match, and cultural appropriateness.", "Ensure Model Integrity: Detect unsafe or misleading content, factual hallucinations, bias, and policy-risk language; validate reliability across use cases."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=e3f6b00f-dc47-4fad-81f2-70d8f4e97aa0&jobPostingId=Filipino-26-173');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('70b8d558-9ffc-54eb-8ae1-facd7016c6a1', 'Filipino / Tagalog Team Lead', 'sme.careers', 'Languages', 'Remote (3 Countries: Saudi Arabia, The Philippines, The United States…)', 'Contract', 'Mid Senior Level', '$25/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Filipino / Tagalog Quality Assurance Lead (QAL) to oversee quality, consistency, and trainer performance across Filipino/Tagalog AI training projects. You will review AI-generated Filipino/Tagalog content and trainer/QA work, evaluate output quality against project guidelines, provide precise written feedback, and ensure that all contributors follow the expected quality standards.

