• Native or near-native Filipino/Tagalog proficiency with strong reading and writing skills.
• Strong grasp of the English language to follow project guidelines, communicate with teams, and provide clear feedback in English.
• 3+ years of professional experience in Filipino/Tagalog writing, editing, translation, localization, content QA, AI training, education, annotation, or related language-review workflows.
• Strong understanding of Filipino/Tagalog grammar, spelling conventions, punctuation, tone, register, cultural context, and natural usage.
• Comfortable handling formal Filipino, conversational Tagalog, and Taglish/code-switching when required, while keeping style consistent with project guidelines.
• Ability to evaluate Filipino/Tagalog content against detailed rubrics and identify issues such as mistranslation, literal phrasing, unnatural tone, incorrect code-switching, hallucinated claims, ambiguity, or inconsistent terminology.
• Experience leading or supporting remote teams of trainers, annotators, reviewers, editors, or QAs is strongly preferred.
• Comfortable working in fast-moving remote environments using tools such as Discord, Google Sheets, Google Docs, trackers, dashboards, and project management systems.
• Highly detail-oriented and organized, with the ability to maintain style guides, FAQs, trackers, onboarding materials, honeypots, and other quality documentation.
• Experience with AI training, data annotation, large language models, prompt/response evaluation, or rubric-based LLM QA is a strong plus.


### Eligible Countries (3)
Saudi Arabia, The Philippines, The United States', '["LLM Evaluation", "Translation Quality Review", "Tagalog", "Filipino Quality Assurance", "Style Guides", "AI Training", "Filipino", "Trainer Feedback", "English", "Localization QA"]', '["Quality monitoring: Spot-check Filipino/Tagalog items, identify quality issues, provide ongoing feedback through DMs, and escalate recurring or critical issues.", "Trainer and QA communication: Update trainers and QAs on Discord about new item guidelines, project changes, workflow updates, and quality expectations.", "Question handling: Respond to trainer/QA questions clearly and promptly, especially around Filipino/Tagalog wording, tone, register, translation fidelity, Taglish usage, cultural context, and edge cases.", "Trainer/QA activation management: DM contributors who are inactive or not working, encourage activation, track follow-ups, and flag availability issues when needed.", "Documentation: Create and maintain Filipino/Tagalog project documentation, including style guides, trackers, FAQs, quality notes, examples, honeypots, and onboarding materials.", "Onboarding and training: Schedule and run onboarding/training calls with trainers and QAs to explain project expectations, workflows, rubrics, quality standards, and Filipino/Tagalog-specific style requirements.", "Quality alignment: Ensure all trainers and QAs apply Filipino/Tagalog language guidelines consistently and understand updates as projects evolve.", "Process improvement: Identify recurring quality gaps, propose workflow improvements, and help build scalable QA processes for Filipino/Tagalog-language projects."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=ee66d28d-aa66-4e72-be4e-bf4f00fd5087&jobPostingId=FilipinoQAL-26-173');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('524ef4e7-aa15-5c16-b61d-cc9d01f23e26', 'Finance & Accounting Specialist – Rubric Design', 'sme.careers', 'Finance', 'Remote (The United States)', 'Contract', 'Not Applicable', '$100/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Finance & Accounting Subject Matter Expert (SME) to create realistic professional tasks, evaluate AI-generated financial work, and design detailed rubrics defining what a high-quality professional response should contain.

You will develop challenging questions and work products involving areas such as financial analysis, accounting, corporate finance, investment analysis, valuation, financial modeling, reporting, audit, risk, or related disciplines. You will assess whether AI outputs use appropriate assumptions, methodologies, calculations, professional judgment, and supporting reasoning.

A major focus of this role is rubric design and evaluation writing. You will translate professional finance and accounting judgment into structured criteria covering accuracy, methodology, completeness, materiality, assumptions, calculations, risk considerations, and quality of reasoning. You may also critique and improve rubrics developed by other experts.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your expertise directly helps improve the world’s premier AI models by making financial outputs more accurate, rigorous, and professionally useful.


### Responsibilities
• Create professional finance tasks: Develop challenging financial, accounting, valuation, investment, audit, or analytical problems.
• Design scoring rubrics: Define the calculations, assumptions, reasoning, and professional considerations expected in strong responses.
• Evaluate financial outputs: Review AI-generated analyses for accuracy, methodology, logic, and completeness.
• Assess professional judgment: Determine whether assumptions and conclusions are reasonable and sufficiently supported.
• Identify material errors: Detect incorrect calculations, accounting treatment, valuation logic, financial interpretation, or risk analysis.
• Critique peer rubrics: Review criteria for ambiguity, missing components, duplication, excessive subjectivity, or technical errors.
• Develop reference content: Produce high-quality analyses, solutions, critiques, and explanations.
• Support AI training: Generate tasks, rubrics, evaluations, preferences, and reference-answer pairs suitable for RL and SFT.
• Maintain professional standards: Ensure outputs reflect appropriate finance and accounting conventions and terminology.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree or higher in Finance, Accounting, Economics, Business, Applied Mathematics, or a related discipline.
• Relevant professional certifications such as CPA, CFA, ACCA, ACA, CMA, FRM, or equivalent are strongly preferred where applicable.
• Strong professional proficiency in English, minimum C1.
• 3+ years of professional experience in finance, accounting, investment analysis, corporate finance, financial reporting, audit, consulting, risk, or a related field.
• Strong knowledge of professional methodologies, calculations, assumptions, and analytical standards relevant to your specialty.
• Ability to create realistic professional finance or accounting tasks that require judgment rather than simple factual recall.
• Strong ability to design detailed rubrics covering accuracy, methodology, assumptions, completeness, materiality, reasoning quality, and professional presentation.
• Ability to distinguish between calculation errors, methodological errors, unsupported assumptions, and reasonable professional differences.
• Comfortable critiquing rubrics created by other finance or accounting experts.
• High attention to detail when reviewing numerical accuracy, financial logic, terminology, assumptions, reconciliations, and conclusions.
• Experience with training, examination writing, audit review, investment committee review, financial QA, research review, or professional assessment is strongly preferred.
• Prior experience with AI evaluation, model benchmarking, annotation, RLHF, or rubric-based scoring is preferred.', '["Accounting", "Audit", "Model Evaluation", "Rubric Design", "Financial Modeling", "Financial Reporting", "Expert Review", "Finance", "Valuation", "Corporate Finance", "Risk Management", "English", "Rubric Writing", "AI Evaluation", "Investment Analysis", "Professional Judgment"]', '["Create professional finance tasks: Develop challenging financial, accounting, valuation, investment, audit, or analytical problems.", "Design scoring rubrics: Define the calculations, assumptions, reasoning, and professional considerations expected in strong responses.", "Evaluate financial outputs: Review AI-generated analyses for accuracy, methodology, logic, and completeness.", "Assess professional judgment: Determine whether assumptions and conclusions are reasonable and sufficiently supported.", "Identify material errors: Detect incorrect calculations, accounting treatment, valuation logic, financial interpretation, or risk analysis.", "Critique peer rubrics: Review criteria for ambiguity, missing components, duplication, excessive subjectivity, or technical errors.", "Develop reference content: Produce high-quality analyses, solutions, critiques, and explanations.", "Support AI training: Generate tasks, rubrics, evaluations, preferences, and reference-answer pairs suitable for RL and SFT.", "Maintain professional standards: Ensure outputs reflect appropriate finance and accounting conventions and terminology."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=ab48ef6c-9e35-4351-9f56-4ffa47f2a18a&jobPostingId=FinanceRubric-26-512');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('8ba07a36-38e6-5d2e-a931-45bba96feec8', 'Financial Analyst', 'sme.careers', 'Finance', 'Remote (17 Countries: Bangladesh, Bhutan, Brazil…)', 'Contract', 'Mid Senior Level', '$85/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Financial Analysis Subject Matter Expert (SME) to review AI-generated financial analysis and business-finance responses and/or create expert finance content, evaluating reasoning quality and step-by-step analytical problem-solving while providing precise written feedback. You will assess solutions for accuracy, clarity, and adherence to the prompt; identify errors in financial modeling logic, assumptions, unit economics, valuation reasoning, forecasting, and metric interpretation; fact-check finance concepts and calculations; write high-quality explanations and model solutions that demonstrate correct methods; and rate and compare multiple responses based on correctness and reasoning quality. This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs.

Important:
There is no immediate project for this role; however, if qualified, you will be among the first experts we reach out to when relevant opportunities arise. This will also provide you with access to future projects available through our expert network.


### Responsibilities
• Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts and gold-standard finance outputs (models, assumptions tables, narratives, sensitivity analyses, investment-style summaries).
• Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to improve numeric correctness, rigor, clarity, and practical usefulness.
• Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI outputs for calculation errors, misleading interpretations, unsafe assumptions, and bias; validate reliability across business scenarios.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree (or higher) in Finance, Accounting, Economics, Business, Mathematics/Statistics, or a related field; CFA/MBA is a strong plus.
• 5+ years of professional experience in financial analysis (FP&A, corporate finance, investment banking, equity research, consulting, or similar).
• Strong command of core finance concepts: 3-statement logic, cash flow drivers, working capital, margin analysis, capital allocation, and basic corporate accounting linkage.
• Proven experience building and reviewing financial models (forecasting, scenario/sensitivity analysis, cohort/unit economics, pricing/packaging analyses).
• Comfortable with valuation reasoning (DCF mechanics, comps selection, multiple drivers) and clearly stating assumptions and limitations.
• Strong quantitative rigor and attention to detail (units, sign conventions, time horizons, circularity, error-checks).
• Ability to communicate complex analyses clearly in writing (executive summary, key drivers, risks, recommendations); minimum C1 English proficiency.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Prior experience with AI data training/annotation, finance QA, investment memo review, or analytics editorial work is strongly preferred.


