• Hands-on experience using Firebase for app setup, authentication, databases, storage, hosting, security rules, deployment, or troubleshooting workflows.
• English proficiency at B2 level or higher to understand project instructions, document tasks clearly, and communicate with the project team.
• Comfortable using a computer, browser-based consoles, developer tools, terminals where needed, project files, and recording workflows.
• Ability to come up with realistic and challenging Firebase tasks that reflect actual web, mobile, backend, admin, data, or app-development use cases.
• Strong understanding of Firebase basics such as projects, apps, Authentication, Firestore, Realtime Database, Storage, Hosting, security rules, SDK configuration, and deployments.
• Ability to ensure your setup supports the task, including having Firebase access, test projects, safe sample data, local files, and required tools ready before recording.
