Bangladesh, India, Pakistan', '["Digital Drawing", "Layers", "Inkscape", "Vector Design", "SVG", "Screen Recording", "Graphic Design", "Illustration", "Paths", "English"]', '["Create realistic Inkscape tasks: Come up with realistic and challenging tasks that can be executed on the computer using Inkscape, then document the task clearly in SuperAnnotate.", "Prepare the work environment: Ensure your setup supports the task, including having Inkscape installed, files/assets available, fonts/images prepared, and any required references ready before recording.", "Record task execution: Record yourself executing the Inkscape task on your computer while following project instructions and ensuring the workflow is clear, complete, and realistic.", "Document task context: Provide enough task context, steps, goals, files, assets, and notes so reviewers can understand what the task is and how it was completed.", "Demonstrate practical software use: Complete workflows involving vector paths, node editing, shapes, text, layers, alignment, gradients, clipping, masking, tracing, SVG cleanup, or exports where relevant.", "Maintain submission quality: Review your recording and documentation before submission to ensure the task is complete, understandable, realistic, and aligned with project guidelines."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=e52300af-f603-49f0-9213-3d9c8d61cb38&jobPostingId=Inkscape-26-208');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('f4bbfc4e-f9ee-5bed-a26a-dc39f528f908', 'Insurance Expert', 'sme.careers', 'Legal', 'Remote (17 Countries: Bangladesh, Bhutan, Brazil…)', 'Contract', 'Mid Senior Level', '$70/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as an Insurance Subject Matter Expert (SME) to review AI-generated insurance responses and/or create expert insurance content, evaluating reasoning quality and step-by-step decision-making while providing precise written feedback. You will assess solutions for accuracy, clarity, regulatory/compliance awareness, and adherence to the prompt; identify errors in policy interpretation, coverage analysis, claims handling logic, underwriting reasoning, risk assessment, exclusions/endorsements, and terminology; fact-check technical insurance information; write high-quality explanations and model solutions that demonstrate correct methods; and rate and compare multiple responses based on correctness and reasoning quality. This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs.

Important:
There is no immediate project for this role; however, if qualified, you will be among the first experts we reach out to when relevant opportunities arise. This will also provide you with access to future projects available through our expert network.


### Responsibilities
• Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts and gold-standard outputs across coverage analysis, claims scenarios, underwriting decisions, and policy communication.
• Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to improve correctness, completeness, clarity, and compliance-aware reasoning.
• Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI outputs for inaccuracies, misleading guidance, inappropriate certainty, and bias; validate reliability across use cases.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree (or higher) in Business, Finance, Risk Management, Insurance, Law, or a related field (or equivalent professional experience).
• 5+ years of professional experience in insurance (claims, underwriting, brokerage, actuarial support, risk management, compliance, or operations).
• Strong understanding of insurance fundamentals: policy structure (insuring agreement, definitions, conditions, exclusions), endorsements, limits/deductibles, and coverage triggers.
• Comfortable with coverage and claims reasoning across one or more lines (e.g., P&C, commercial lines, auto, homeowners, liability, health, life).
• Ability to evaluate decisions for internal consistency (facts → policy language → coverage position → documentation), including edge cases and ambiguity.
• Strong attention to detail when identifying missing facts, incorrect assumptions, misapplied definitions, or unsafe/unsupported recommendations; minimum C1 English proficiency.
• Clear written communication skills, including the ability to explain complex policy concepts in plain language.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Professional designations (e.g., CPCU, AINS, ARM, CIC, AU) are a plus.
• Prior experience with AI data training/annotation, claims QA, underwriting QA, policy drafting/review, or insurance editorial work is strongly preferred.


### Eligible Countries (17)
Bangladesh, Bhutan, Brazil, Cambodia, Germany, India, Indonesia, Malaysia, Nepal, Pakistan, Singapore, Sri Lanka, Thailand, The Philippines, The United States, Timor Leste, Vietnam', '["Insurance Coverage", "Customer Communication", "Loss Prevention", "Regulation", "Underwriting", "Claims Handling", "Risk Assessment", "Compliance", "Exclusions And Endorsements", "Policy Interpretation", "English"]', '["Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts and gold-standard outputs across coverage analysis, claims scenarios, underwriting decisions, and policy communication.", "Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to improve correctness, completeness, clarity, and compliance-aware reasoning.", "Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI outputs for inaccuracies, misleading guidance, inappropriate certainty, and bias; validate reliability across use cases."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=9ffdfe5d-e932-425c-98e9-f538db6bc4e7&jobPostingId=Insurance-26-140');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('ae65efbd-8e54-562a-af2c-64c611894b52', 'IntelliJ IDEA Specialist', 'sme.careers', 'Data Annotation & RLHF', 'Remote (3 Countries: Bangladesh, India, Pakistan…)', 'Contract', 'Not Applicable', '$25/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as an IntelliJ IDEA Specialist (SME) to create realistic, challenging computer-based tasks using IntelliJ IDEA and related software development workflows. You will design practical IDE tasks, document them clearly in SuperAnnotate, ensure your setup supports the task, and record yourself executing the task on your computer.

Tasks may include creating Java/Kotlin projects, configuring SDKs, running and debugging code, using Maven or Gradle, managing packages, refactoring, using Git integration, navigating code, writing tests, or troubleshooting build issues. Your work will help train advanced AI models to better understand how real users complete software development workflows in IntelliJ IDEA.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your IntelliJ IDEA expertise directly helps improve the world’s premier AI models by teaching them how real users complete practical coding, debugging, and project-management tasks in a professional IDE.


### Responsibilities
• Create realistic IntelliJ IDEA tasks: Come up with realistic and challenging tasks that can be executed on the computer using IntelliJ IDEA, then document the task clearly in SuperAnnotate.
• Prepare the work environment: Ensure your setup supports the task, including having IntelliJ IDEA installed, projects/files available, SDK configured, dependencies installed, and any required references ready before recording.
• Record task execution: Record yourself executing the IntelliJ IDEA task on your computer while following project instructions and ensuring the workflow is clear, complete, and realistic.
• Document task context: Provide enough task context, steps, goals, project files, dependencies, and notes so reviewers can understand what the task is and how it was completed.
• Demonstrate practical software use: Complete workflows involving coding, debugging, refactoring, Maven/Gradle builds, tests, terminal use, Git integration, project setup, or troubleshooting where relevant.
• Maintain submission quality: Review your recording and documentation before submission to ensure the task is complete, understandable, realistic, and aligned with project guidelines.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Hands-on experience using IntelliJ IDEA for Java, Kotlin, backend development, debugging, project setup, refactoring, build tools, or Git workflows.
• English proficiency at B2 level or higher to understand project instructions, document tasks clearly, and communicate with the project team.
• Comfortable using a computer, managing files, opening projects, configuring SDKs, installing dependencies, and recording workflows.
• Ability to come up with realistic and challenging IntelliJ IDEA tasks that reflect actual coding, debugging, testing, build, or project-setup use cases.
• Strong understanding of IntelliJ IDEA basics such as project structure, SDKs, run configurations, debugger, refactoring, Maven/Gradle, terminal, code navigation, and version control.
• Ability to ensure your setup supports the task, including having IntelliJ IDEA installed, projects/files available, SDK configured, dependencies installed, and references ready before recording.
• High attention to detail when preparing the task, executing the workflow, and checking that the recording is complete and understandable.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Additional professional skills are appreciated, including Java, Kotlin, backend development, QA, GitHub, DevOps, technical writing, coding, or other computer-based workflows.


### Eligible Countries (3)
Bangladesh, India, Pakistan', '["IntelliJ IDEA", "Git", "IDE", "Kotlin", "Java", "Screen Recording", "Maven", "Gradle", "English", "Debugging"]', '["Create realistic IntelliJ IDEA tasks: Come up with realistic and challenging tasks that can be executed on the computer using IntelliJ IDEA, then document the task clearly in SuperAnnotate.", "Prepare the work environment: Ensure your setup supports the task, including having IntelliJ IDEA installed, projects/files available, SDK configured, dependencies installed, and any required references ready before recording.", "Record task execution: Record yourself executing the IntelliJ IDEA task on your computer while following project instructions and ensuring the workflow is clear, complete, and realistic.", "Document task context: Provide enough task context, steps, goals, project files, dependencies, and notes so reviewers can understand what the task is and how it was completed.", "Demonstrate practical software use: Complete workflows involving coding, debugging, refactoring, Maven/Gradle builds, tests, terminal use, Git integration, project setup, or troubleshooting where relevant.", "Maintain submission quality: Review your recording and documentation before submission to ensure the task is complete, understandable, realistic, and aligned with project guidelines."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=371bb0ab-6574-4cd9-a7bd-d53a3d815e65&jobPostingId=IntelliJIDEA-26-136');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('ffe5059a-8bbb-5983-9be9-c82441a933ff', 'Italian Language Expert', 'sme.careers', 'Languages', 'Remote (Italy)', 'Contract', 'Mid Senior Level', '$37/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will review AI-generated Italian-language responses and/or generate expert language content, evaluating reasoning quality and step-by-step edits while providing precise, actionable feedback. You will assess solutions for accuracy, clarity, and adherence to the prompt; identify errors in logic, meaning, methodology, or conceptual understanding; fact-check information when needed; write high-quality explanations and model revisions that demonstrate correct methods; and rate and compare multiple AI responses based on correctness and reasoning quality. This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate that provides AI training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your language expertise directly helps improve the world’s premier AI models by making their outputs more accurate, natural, and clearly explained.

Important:
There is no immediate project for this role; however, if qualified, you will be among the first experts we reach out to when relevant opportunities arise. This will also provide you with access to future projects available through our expert network.


### Responsibilities
• Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts in various topics and responses to guide AI learning, ensuring the models reflect a comprehensive understanding of diverse subjects.
• Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to enhance the model''s accuracy, fluency, and contextual relevance.
• Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI models for potential inaccuracies or biases, validating their reliability across use cases.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree (or higher) in Linguistics, Italian, Translation/Localization, Communications, or a related field.
• Native or near-native Italian proficiency (C2 preferred) and Minimum C1 English proficiency required; multilingual ability beyond Italian/English is a plus.
• Strong command of Italian grammar (incl. clitics, tense/aspect, mood), semantics, pragmatics, and discourse-level editing across registers.
• Exceptional attention to detail in identifying meaning drift, ambiguity, locale inconsistencies, and subtle errors; able to explain corrections clearly in writing.
• Comfortable applying style guides and enforcing terminology and tone consistency for specific audiences and locales.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Previous experience with AI data training/annotation, editorial QA, translation/localization QA, or professional editing is strongly preferred.
• Location requirement: Only candidates based in Italy will be considered for this role', '["Pragmatics", "Copyediting", "Italian", "Multilingual Communication", "Localization", "Tone", "Semantics", "Register", "English", "Italian Grammar", "Morphosyntax"]', '["Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts in various topics and responses to guide AI learning, ensuring the models reflect a comprehensive understanding of diverse subjects.", "Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to enhance the model''s accuracy, fluency, and contextual relevance.", "Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI models for potential inaccuracies or biases, validating their reliability across use cases."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=b414162e-acad-4e1f-bffe-0e083c86e846&jobPostingId=Italian-25-317');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('e1db109b-b812-529f-99f4-25fe25ab268d', 'Italian Quality Assurance Lead (QAL)', 'sme.careers', 'Languages', 'Remote (Italy)', 'Contract', 'Mid Senior Level', '$45/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as an Italian Quality Assurance Lead (QAL) to oversee quality, consistency, and trainer performance across Italian AI training projects. You will review AI-generated Italian content and trainer/QA work, evaluate output quality against project guidelines, provide precise written feedback, and ensure that all contributors follow the expected quality standards.

You will assess work for accuracy, fluency, grammar, spelling, tone, cultural appropriateness, meaning preservation, instruction-following, formatting, and adherence to project-specific rubrics. You will spot recurring quality issues, communicate updates to trainers and QAs, support onboarding, maintain documentation, and help activate contributors who are not working consistently.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your Italian quality leadership will directly help improve the world’s premier AI models by ensuring that Italian training data is natural, accurate, culturally appropriate, well-documented, and aligned with client expectations.

Selection process involves an AI interview, a domain-specific task, and an interview with a recruiter.

Important:
There is no immediate project for this role; however, if qualified, you will be among the first experts we reach out to when relevant opportunities arise. This will also provide you with access to future projects available through our expert network.


### Responsibilities
• Spot-check Italian items, identify quality issues, provide feedback through DMs, and escalate recurring or critical issues.
• Update trainers/QAs on Discord about guidelines, project changes, workflow updates, and quality expectations.
• Respond to questions around Italian grammar, accents, register, verb moods, translation fidelity, terminology, and cultural context.
• DM inactive contributors, encourage activation, track follow-ups, and flag availability issues.
• Create and maintain Italian documentation, style guides, trackers, FAQs, examples, honeypots, and onboarding materials.
• Run onboarding/training calls for Italian contributors.
• Ensure Italian language guidelines are applied consistently.
• Identify recurring quality gaps and improve QA workflows.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Italian, Linguistics, Translation, Communications, Journalism, English, Education, Quality Assurance, or a relevant domain/related field.
• Native or near-native Italian proficiency with strong reading and writing skills.
• Strong grasp of the English language to follow project guidelines, communicate with teams, and provide clear feedback in English.
• 3+ years of professional experience in Italian writing, editing, translation, localization, content QA, AI training, education, annotation, or related workflows.
• Strong understanding of Italian grammar, spelling conventions, punctuation, accents, gender/number agreement, verb moods, tone, register, and cultural context.
• Ability to evaluate Italian content against rubrics and identify issues such as mistranslation, literal phrasing, unnatural tone, incorrect subjunctive usage, hallucinated claims, ambiguity, or inconsistent terminology.
• Experience leading or supporting remote teams of trainers, annotators, reviewers, editors, or QAs is strongly preferred.
• Comfortable with Discord, Google Sheets, Google Docs, trackers, dashboards, and project management systems.
• Highly detail-oriented and organized, with the ability to maintain style guides, FAQs, trackers, onboarding materials, honeypots, and documentation.
• Experience with AI training, data annotation, LLM evaluation, prompt/response evaluation, or rubric-based LLM QA is a strong plus.', '["LLM Evaluation", "Italian Quality Assurance", "Translation Quality Review", "Italian", "Style Guides", "AI Training", "Documentation", "Trainer Feedback", "English", "Localization QA"]', '["Spot-check Italian items, identify quality issues, provide feedback through DMs, and escalate recurring or critical issues.", "Update trainers/QAs on Discord about guidelines, project changes, workflow updates, and quality expectations.", "Respond to questions around Italian grammar, accents, register, verb moods, translation fidelity, terminology, and cultural context.", "DM inactive contributors, encourage activation, track follow-ups, and flag availability issues.", "Create and maintain Italian documentation, style guides, trackers, FAQs, examples, honeypots, and onboarding materials.", "Run onboarding/training calls for Italian contributors.", "Ensure Italian language guidelines are applied consistently.", "Identify recurring quality gaps and improve QA workflows."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=6877bcad-4382-42bf-b689-c900be38b954&jobPostingId=ItalianQAL-25-317');
