y usage, authentication, browser security, data handling, and production readiness.", "Process improvement: Identify recurring quality gaps, propose workflow improvements, and help build scalable QA processes for JavaScript AI training projects."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=c07328cf-d497-44e5-b099-1a1b5bac20cc&jobPostingId=JSQAL-25-112');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('f5c401db-e77f-5cc4-a2dc-8d3994b1ec84', 'Jupyter Notebook Specialist', 'sme.careers', 'Coding', 'Remote (3 Countries: Bangladesh, India, Pakistan…)', 'Contract', 'Not Applicable', '$20/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Jupyter Notebook Specialist (SME) to create realistic, challenging computer-based tasks using Jupyter Notebook, JupyterLab, or notebook-based data workflows. You will design practical notebook tasks, document them clearly in SuperAnnotate, ensure your setup supports the task, and record yourself executing the task on your computer.

Tasks may include creating notebooks, running Python cells, data cleaning, exploratory analysis, visualization, markdown explanations, package imports, debugging, CSV/Excel handling, simple machine learning workflows, or reproducible data-science demonstrations. Your work will help train advanced AI models to better understand how real users complete notebook-based coding and data-analysis workflows.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your Jupyter Notebook expertise directly helps improve the world’s premier AI models by teaching them how real users complete practical data, coding, analysis, and documentation workflows.


### Responsibilities
• Create realistic Jupyter Notebook tasks: Come up with realistic and challenging tasks that can be executed on the computer using Jupyter Notebook or JupyterLab, then document the task clearly in SuperAnnotate.
• Prepare the work environment: Ensure your setup supports the task, including having Jupyter available, datasets prepared, packages installed, notebooks created, and any required references ready before recording.
• Record task execution: Record yourself executing the Jupyter Notebook task on your computer while following project instructions and ensuring the workflow is clear, complete, and realistic.
• Document task context: Provide enough task context, steps, goals, files, dataset details, and notes so reviewers can understand what the task is and how it was completed.
• Demonstrate practical software use: Complete workflows involving Python cells, markdown explanations, data cleaning, pandas, charts, debugging, imports, file handling, notebook outputs, or exports where relevant.
• Maintain submission quality: Review your recording and documentation before submission to ensure the task is complete, reproducible, understandable, realistic, and aligned with project guidelines.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Hands-on experience using Jupyter Notebook or JupyterLab for Python, data analysis, visualization, teaching, research, automation, or documentation workflows.
• English proficiency at B2 level or higher to understand project instructions, document tasks clearly, and communicate with the project team.
• Comfortable using a computer, managing files, running notebooks, installing packages where needed, using browser/local environments, and recording workflows.
• Ability to come up with realistic and challenging Jupyter Notebook tasks that reflect actual data analysis, coding, education, research, reporting, or technical documentation use cases.
• Strong understanding of notebook basics such as code cells, markdown cells, execution order, kernels, imports, file paths, pandas, charts, outputs, and exports.
• Ability to ensure your setup supports the task, including having Jupyter available, files/datasets prepared, packages installed, and any required references ready before recording.
• High attention to detail when preparing the task, executing the workflow, and checking that the recording is complete and understandable.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Additional professional skills are appreciated, including Python, data analysis, machine learning, statistics, research, teaching, coding, reporting, or other computer-based workflows.


### Eligible Countries (3)
Bangladesh, India, Pakistan', '["Pandas", "Python", "Data Science", "Data Analysis", "Visualization", "Screen Recording", "JupyterLab", "Computer Use", "English", "Jupyter Notebook"]', '["Create realistic Jupyter Notebook tasks: Come up with realistic and challenging tasks that can be executed on the computer using Jupyter Notebook or JupyterLab, then document the task clearly in SuperAnnotate.", "Prepare the work environment: Ensure your setup supports the task, including having Jupyter available, datasets prepared, packages installed, notebooks created, and any required references ready before recording.", "Record task execution: Record yourself executing the Jupyter Notebook task on your computer while following project instructions and ensuring the workflow is clear, complete, and realistic.", "Document task context: Provide enough task context, steps, goals, files, dataset details, and notes so reviewers can understand what the task is and how it was completed.", "Demonstrate practical software use: Complete workflows involving Python cells, markdown explanations, data cleaning, pandas, charts, debugging, imports, file handling, notebook outputs, or exports where relevant.", "Maintain submission quality: Review your recording and documentation before submission to ensure the task is complete, reproducible, understandable, realistic, and aligned with project guidelines."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=555f420b-4775-4aad-aa57-a64caf46d50f&jobPostingId=JupyterNotebook-26-131');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('76b228fd-5e12-5713-83e9-1f9261d6f689', 'Kannada Expert with Mathematical Background', 'sme.careers', 'Languages', 'Remote (5 Countries: India, Malaysia, Saudi Arabia…)', 'Contract', 'Mid Senior Level', '$20/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Kannada Language Specialist (SME) to review AI-generated Kannada content and/or create high-quality Kannada reference content, evaluating language quality and step-by-step reasoning while providing precise written feedback. You will assess outputs for accuracy, fluency, grammar, spelling, tone, cultural appropriateness, and adherence to the prompt; identify errors in meaning, mistranslation, register (formal vs informal), ambiguity, and logical consistency; fact-check claims when needed; write high-quality rewrites and model answers that demonstrate best practices in Kannada writing; and rate and compare multiple AI responses based on correctness and overall quality.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your Kannada expertise directly helps improve the world’s premier AI models by making their Kannada language output more natural, reliable, culturally accurate, and clearly written.

Selection process involves an AI interview, a domain-specific task, and an interview with a recruiter.


### Responsibilities
• Develop AI Training Content: Create prompts and gold-standard Kannada answers across multiple domains (general knowledge, customer support, education, conversational writing).
• Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI outputs to improve fluency, correctness, tone match, and cultural appropriateness.
• Ensure Model Integrity: Detect unsafe or misleading content, factual hallucinations, bias, and policy-risk language; validate reliability across use cases.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree (or higher) in Mathematics
• Native or near-native Kannada proficiency (reading and writing required).
• Strong professional proficiency in English (minimum C1) to follow guidelines and provide detailed feedback in English.
• 3+ years of professional experience in writing, editing, localization, translation, content QA, journalism, education, or related language-focused work.
• Deep understanding of Kannada grammar, spelling conventions, punctuation, and style—able to explain why something is wrong and how to fix it.
• Comfortable handling multiple registers (formal/informal), regional variation (e.g., Bengaluru/standard usage vs regional dialect influence), and audience adaptation (India vs diaspora).
• High attention to detail when spotting subtle meaning shifts, hallucinated claims, or culturally awkward phrasing.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Prior experience with AI data training/annotation, translation QA, editorial QA, or rubric-based evaluation is strongly preferred.


### Eligible Countries (5)
India, Malaysia, Saudi Arabia, The United States, United Arab Emirates', '["Style", "Copyediting", "Translation Quality Review", "Kannada", "Localization", "Fact-Checking", "Tone & Register", "English", "Proofreading", "Cultural Context", "Grammar"]', '["Develop AI Training Content: Create prompts and gold-standard Kannada answers across multiple domains (general knowledge, customer support, education, conversational writing).", "Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI outputs to improve fluency, correctness, tone match, and cultural appropriateness.", "Ensure Model Integrity: Detect unsafe or misleading content, factual hallucinations, bias, and policy-risk language; validate reliability across use cases."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=820efc5a-117f-4140-8dfd-8063b89882fb&jobPostingId=KannadaMath-26-162');
