India, Malaysia, Saudi Arabia, The United States, United Arab Emirates', '["LLM Evaluation", "Translation Quality Review", "Kannada", "Kannada Quality Assurance", "Style Guides", "AI Training", "Documentation", "Trainer Feedback", "English", "Localization QA"]', '["Quality monitoring: Spot-check Kannada items, identify quality issues, provide ongoing feedback through DMs, and escalate recurring or critical issues.", "Trainer and QA communication: Update trainers and QAs on Discord about new item guidelines, project changes, workflow updates, and quality expectations.", "Question handling: Respond to trainer/QA questions clearly and promptly, especially around Kannada wording, register, translation fidelity, cultural context, regional variation, and edge cases.", "Trainer/QA activation management: DM contributors who are inactive or not working, encourage activation, track follow-ups, and flag availability issues when needed.", "Documentation: Create and maintain Kannada project documentation, including style guides, trackers, FAQs, quality notes, examples, honeypots, and onboarding materials.", "Onboarding and training: Schedule and run onboarding/training calls with trainers and QAs to explain project expectations, workflows, rubrics, quality standards, and Kannada-specific style requirements.", "Quality alignment: Ensure all trainers and QAs apply Kannada language guidelines consistently and understand updates as projects evolve.", "Process improvement: Identify recurring quality gaps, propose workflow improvements, and help build scalable QA processes for Kannada-language projects."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=54703812-44b2-4dbc-884f-cc98ead269d4&jobPostingId=KannadaQALMath-26-162');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('cc990831-74c3-53b3-b797-c2e1a9a7ca97', 'KiCad Specialist', 'sme.careers', 'Data Annotation & RLHF', 'Remote (3 Countries: Bangladesh, India, Pakistan…)', 'Contract', 'Not Applicable', '$20/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a KiCad Specialist (SME) to create realistic, challenging computer-based tasks using KiCad and related PCB design workflows. You will design practical KiCad tasks, document them clearly in SuperAnnotate, ensure your setup supports the task, and record yourself executing the task on your computer.

Tasks may include creating schematics, placing components, assigning footprints, routing PCB traces, managing layers, checking design rules, generating Gerber files, editing symbols/footprints, organizing projects, or troubleshooting common PCB design issues. Your work will help train advanced AI models to better understand how real users complete electronic design and PCB layout workflows.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your KiCad expertise directly helps improve the world’s premier AI models by teaching them how real users complete practical electronics, schematic capture, and PCB design workflows.


### Responsibilities
• Create realistic KiCad tasks: Come up with realistic and challenging tasks that can be executed on the computer using KiCad, then document the task clearly in SuperAnnotate.
• Prepare the work environment: Ensure your setup supports the task, including having KiCad installed, project files prepared, component libraries available, schematic references ready, and any required assets prepared before recording.
• Record task execution: Record yourself executing the KiCad task on your computer while following project instructions and ensuring the workflow is clear, complete, and realistic.
• Document task context: Provide enough task context, steps, goals, circuit details, project files, component notes, and references so reviewers can understand what the task is and how it was completed.
• Demonstrate practical software use: Complete workflows involving schematic capture, footprint assignment, PCB routing, layer setup, ERC/DRC checks, symbol/footprint editing, fabrication outputs, or troubleshooting where relevant.
• Maintain submission quality: Review your recording and documentation before submission to ensure the task is complete, understandable, realistic, and aligned with project guidelines.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Hands-on experience using KiCad for schematic design, PCB layout, footprints, routing, design-rule checks, Gerber export, or electronics design workflows.
• English proficiency at B2 level or higher to understand project instructions, document tasks clearly, and communicate with the project team.
• Comfortable using a computer, managing project files, installing/opening required programs, navigating engineering/design software, and recording workflows.
• Ability to come up with realistic and challenging KiCad tasks that reflect actual electronics, PCB design, prototyping, engineering, repair, or hardware-development use cases.
• Strong understanding of KiCad basics such as projects, schematic symbols, footprints, nets, PCB layers, routing, design rules, vias, zones, ERC/DRC checks, and fabrication outputs.
• Ability to ensure your setup supports the task, including having KiCad installed, sample projects/components available, libraries configured, and any required references ready before recording.
• High attention to detail when preparing the task, executing the workflow, and checking that the recording is complete, accurate, and understandable.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Additional professional skills are appreciated, including electronics, electrical engineering, embedded systems, hardware prototyping, CAD, technical documentation, or other computer-based workflows.


### Eligible Countries (3)
Bangladesh, India, Pakistan', '["KiCAD", "Footprints", "Gerber Files", "Electronics", "Screen Recording", "Schematic Capture", "Computer Use", "English", "PCB Design", "Circuit Design"]', '["Create realistic KiCad tasks: Come up with realistic and challenging tasks that can be executed on the computer using KiCad, then document the task clearly in SuperAnnotate.", "Prepare the work environment: Ensure your setup supports the task, including having KiCad installed, project files prepared, component libraries available, schematic references ready, and any required assets prepared before recording.", "Record task execution: Record yourself executing the KiCad task on your computer while following project instructions and ensuring the workflow is clear, complete, and realistic.", "Document task context: Provide enough task context, steps, goals, circuit details, project files, component notes, and references so reviewers can understand what the task is and how it was completed.", "Demonstrate practical software use: Complete workflows involving schematic capture, footprint assignment, PCB routing, layer setup, ERC/DRC checks, symbol/footprint editing, fabrication outputs, or troubleshooting where relevant.", "Maintain submission quality: Review your recording and documentation before submission to ensure the task is complete, understandable, realistic, and aligned with project guidelines."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=1c995d25-53b7-48a2-83a2-2b3a1bb81775&jobPostingId=KiCad-26-207');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('3dd65e96-70e1-5fdb-9bbd-7bc2ed84c53d', 'Korean Document Annotation Expert', 'sme.careers', 'Languages', 'Remote (South Korea)', 'Contract', 'Not Applicable', '$40/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Korean QA Expert reviewing OCR-processed Korean-language PDF documents and ensuring that annotations meet project quality standards. You will review document layouts, revise/add/classify bounding boxes, validate table structures, check reading order, and ensure Korean text is accurately captured and correctly interpreted.

You will also provide clear feedback to annotators on Korean-language correctness, OCR transcription issues, layout errors, entity classification mistakes, and guideline adherence. This role requires strong Korean language expertise, excellent attention to detail, comfort with complex document annotation workflows, and the ability to consistently apply detailed QA guidelines across large volumes of work.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your Korean QA expertise will directly support high-quality OCR and document understanding datasets by ensuring Korean-language documents are accurately structured, annotated, and ready for model training.


### Responsibilities
• Work through a daily queue of annotated Korean PDF documents assigned for QA review.
• Check that all document fields have been captured with correctly placed bounding boxes.
• Verify that Korean content is accurately transcribed and presented in the correct reading order.
• Review and correct OCR-generated pre-annotations, flagging subtle character-level errors in Korean text.
• Validate entity classifications, including tables, charts, text blocks, key-value pairs, headers, footers, and other structured document elements.
• Review table structures for correct boundaries, row/column alignment, merged cells, headers, and logical hierarchy.
• Correct annotation errors directly when appropriate or return them to annotators with clear, actionable notes.
• Provide feedback to annotators on Korean usage correctness, OCR transcription quality, layout interpretation, and guideline adherence.
• Escalate recurring error patterns, unclear edge cases, or guideline ambiguities to project leads.
• Participate in regular team syncs to align on edge cases, annotation standards, and quality expectations.
• Confirm all reviewed documents meet the required quality bar before approving them for submission.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Korean language: Native or fluent proficiency in Korean, with strong ability to review Korean text for accuracy, character-level correctness, spacing, grammar, and usage.
• English proficiency: Strong professional English proficiency, C1/C2 level, to understand detailed project guidelines, participate in team communication, and provide clear written feedback.
• QA or annotation experience: Prior experience in QA, data annotation, document review, content review, OCR validation, or a closely related role.
• OCR and document parsing: Hands-on familiarity with OCR systems, document parsing workflows, PDF annotation, or structured document review.
• Bounding box review: Ability to verify, revise, add, and classify bounding boxes around text fields, tables, charts, key-value pairs, and other document elements.
• Korean text review: Ability to identify and interpret subtle OCR errors in Korean writing, including incorrect characters, spacing issues, line breaks, reading-order issues, and mistranscribed text.
• Table and layout understanding: Ability to review dense or complex document layouts, table structures, merged cells, headers, footers, multi-column text, and hierarchical document sections.
• Attention to detail: Exceptional attention to detail, particularly when reviewing dense Korean document layouts and character-level OCR output.
• Ability to follow complex guidelines: Proven ability to absorb, retain, and consistently apply detailed, multi-step guidelines across large volumes of work.
• Self-review and accuracy mindset: Strong quality-first mindset, with the discipline to thoroughly self-review all work before sign-off, including AI-generated or OCR-generated outputs that may appear plausible but contain subtle errors.
• Clear communication: Ability to provide concise, actionable feedback to annotators when work needs correction.
• Consistency: Ability to make repeatable QA decisions across similar cases and escalate ambiguous edge cases when needed.
• Reliability: Self-directed and comfortable working in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.', '["Table Annotation", "PDF Annotation", "Data Annotation", "Korean Language QA", "English", "Korean", "Bounding Boxes", "OCR QA", "Document Parsing", "Document Annotation"]', '["Work through a daily queue of annotated Korean PDF documents assigned for QA review.", "Check that all document fields have been captured with correctly placed bounding boxes.", "Verify that Korean content is accurately transcribed and presented in the correct reading order.", "Review and correct OCR-generated pre-annotations, flagging subtle character-level errors in Korean text.", "Validate entity classifications, including tables, charts, text blocks, key-value pairs, headers, footers, and other structured document elements.", "Review table structures for correct boundaries, row/column alignment, merged cells, headers, and logical hierarchy.", "Correct annotation errors directly when appropriate or return them to annotators with clear, actionable notes.", "Provide feedback to annotators on Korean usage correctness, OCR transcription quality, layout interpretation, and guideline adherence.", "Escalate recurring error patterns, unclear edge cases, or guideline ambiguities to project leads.", "Participate in regular team syncs to align on edge cases, annotation standards, and quality expectations.", "Confirm all reviewed documents meet the required quality bar before approving them for submission."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=540a76ea-bc98-48b5-adc9-e0e0ee8ef175&jobPostingId=PDFKor-102');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('ea22467c-7159-5c04-9f89-bf4ae856a24d', 'Korean Language Expert', 'sme.careers', 'Languages', 'Remote (South Korea)', 'Contract', 'Mid Senior Level', '$40/hr', 'In this hourly-paid, fully remote contractor role, you will review AI-generated responses and/or generate language content, evaluate reasoning quality and step-by-step problem-solving, and provide expert feedback so outputs are accurate, logical, and clearly explained. You will assess solutions for accuracy, clarity, and adherence to the prompt; identify errors in methodology or conceptual understanding; fact-check information; write high-quality explanations and model solutions that demonstrate correct methods; and rate and compare multiple AI responses based on correctness and reasoning quality. You will apply senior-level Korean localization/translation judgment alongside Minimum C1 English proficiency to ensure terminology, tone, and cultural nuance are consistently correct across use cases. This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and a subsidiary of SuperAnnotate that provides AI training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your work directly helps improve the world’s premier AI models.

Important:
There is no immediate project for this role; however, if qualified, you will be among the first experts we reach out to when relevant opportunities arise. This will also provide you with access to future projects available through our expert network.


### Responsibilities
• Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts in various topics and responses to guide AI learning, ensuring the models reflect a comprehensive understanding of diverse subjects.
• Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to enhance the model''s accuracy, fluency, and contextual relevance.
• Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI models for potential inaccuracies or biases, validating their reliability across use cases.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree or higher in Translation, Linguistics, Localization, Communications, or a related field.
• Native or near-native Korean proficiency and strong command of the locale conventions for South Korea.
• Minimum C1 English proficiency (reading/writing) for interpreting prompts, sources, and evaluation guidelines.
• 5+ years of professional localization/translation experience (multilingual localization experience strongly preferred).
• Demonstrated ability to apply MQM/LQA concepts (severity, category, and root-cause thinking) to produce consistent quality decisions.
• Proficiency with CAT tools and QA workflows (translation memory, termbases, automated checks) and comfort working with structured guidelines.
• Excellent editorial judgment (register, tone, inclusivity, and cultural nuance) with extreme attention to detail.
• Ability to rigorously fact-check localized content (units, references, names, dates) using reliable sources and consistent reasoning.
• Comfort working as an hourly contractor: dependable throughput, clear documentation, and responsiveness across time zones.
• Previous experience with AI data training / annotation / evaluation is preferred.
• Location requirement: Only candidates based in South Korea will be considered for this role', '["Translation", "Copyediting", "Linguistic QA", "LQA", "CAT Tools", "Localization", "Style Guides", "Terminology Management", "MQM Error Typology", "English", "Korean"]', '["Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts in various topics and responses to guide AI learning, ensuring the models reflect a comprehensive understanding of diverse subjects.", "Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to enhance the model''s accuracy, fluency, and contextual relevance.", "Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI models for potential inaccuracies or biases, validating their reliability across use cases."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=63eaa1e1-c0f3-48fa-b5d2-8db26056f51c&jobPostingId=Korean-25-318');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('4c95db1c-3b5f-50a3-b7df-754db6261334', 'Korean Quality Assurance Lead (QAL)', 'sme.careers', 'Languages', 'Remote (South Korea)', 'Contract', 'Mid Senior Level', '$45/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Korean Quality Assurance Lead (QAL) to oversee quality, consistency, and trainer performance across Korean AI training projects. You will review AI-generated Korean content and trainer/QA work, evaluate output quality against project guidelines, provide precise written feedback, and ensure that all contributors follow the expected quality standards.

You will assess work for accuracy, fluency, grammar, spelling, tone, cultural appropriateness, meaning preservation, instruction-following, formatting, and adherence to project-specific rubrics. You will spot recurring quality issues, communicate updates to trainers and QAs, support onboarding, maintain documentation, and help activate contributors who are not working consistently. This role requires strong Korean and English skills, excellent attention to detail, structured communication, and the ability to manage quality workflows across remote teams.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your Korean quality leadership will directly help improve the world’s premier AI models by ensuring that Korean training data is natural, accurate, culturally appropriate, well-documented, and aligned with client expectations.

Selection process involves an AI interview, a domain-specific task, and an interview with a recruiter.

Important:
There is no immediate project for this role; however, if qualified, you will be among the first experts we reach out to when relevant opportunities arise. This will also provide you with access to future projects available through our expert network.


### Responsibilities
• Quality monitoring: Spot-check Korean items, identify quality issues, provide ongoing feedback through DMs, and escalate recurring or critical issues.
• Trainer and QA communication: Update trainers and QAs on Discord about new item guidelines, project changes, workflow updates, and quality expectations.
• Question handling: Respond to trainer/QA questions clearly and promptly, especially around Korean wording, honorifics, speech level, register, translation fidelity, cultural context, and edge cases.
• Trainer/QA activation management: DM contributors who are inactive or not working, encourage activation, track follow-ups, and flag availability issues when needed.
• Documentation: Create and maintain Korean project documentation, including style guides, trackers, FAQs, quality notes, examples, honeypots, and onboarding materials.
• Onboarding and training: Schedule and run onboarding/training calls with trainers and QAs to explain project expectations, workflows, rubrics, quality standards, and Korean-specific style requirements.
• Quality alignment: Ensure all trainers and QAs apply Korean language guidelines consistently and understand updates as projects evolve.
• Process improvement: Identify recurring quality gaps, propose workflow improvements, and help build scalable QA processes for Korean-language projects.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Korean, Linguistics, Translation, Communications, Journalism, English, Education, Quality Assurance, or a relevant domain/related field.
• Native or near-native Korean proficiency with strong reading and writing skills.
• Strong grasp of the English language to follow project guidelines, communicate with teams, and provide clear feedback in English.
• 3+ years of professional experience in Korean writing, editing, translation, localization, content QA, AI training, education, annotation, or related language-review workflows.
• Strong understanding of Korean grammar, spelling conventions, punctuation, honorifics, speech levels, tone, register, and cultural context.
• Ability to evaluate Korean content against detailed rubrics and identify issues such as mistranslation, literal phrasing, unnatural tone, incorrect honorifics, hallucinated claims, ambiguity, or inconsistent terminology.
• Comfortable handling formal vs informal Korean, honorific usage, product/UI localization terminology, and audience adaptation for South Korean users.
• Experience leading or supporting remote teams of trainers, annotators, reviewers, editors, or QAs is strongly preferred.
• Comfortable working in fast-moving remote environments using tools such as Discord, Google Sheets, Google Docs, trackers, dashboards, and project management systems.
• Highly detail-oriented and organized, with the ability to maintain style guides, FAQs, trackers, onboarding materials, honeypots, and other quality documentation.
• Experience with AI training, data annotation, large language models, prompt/response evaluation, or rubric-based LLM QA is a strong plus.', '["LLM Evaluation", "Translation Quality Review", "Style Guides", "AI Training", "Documentation", "Trainer Feedback", "English", "Korean", "Korean Quality Assurance", "Localization QA"]', '["Quality monitoring: Spot-check Korean items, identify quality issues, provide ongoing feedback through DMs, and escalate recurring or critical issues.", "Trainer and QA communication: Update trainers and QAs on Discord about new item guidelines, project changes, workflow updates, and quality expectations.", "Question handling: Respond to trainer/QA questions clearly and promptly, especially around Korean wording, honorifics, speech level, register, translation fidelity, cultural context, and edge cases.", "Trainer/QA activation management: DM contributors who are inactive or not working, encourage activation, track follow-ups, and flag availability issues when needed.", "Documentation: Create and maintain Korean project documentation, including style guides, trackers, FAQs, quality notes, examples, honeypots, and onboarding materials.", "Onboarding and training: Schedule and run onboarding/training calls with trainers and QAs to explain project expectations, workflows, rubrics, quality standards, and Korean-specific style requirements.", "Quality alignment: Ensure all trainers and QAs apply Korean language guidelines consistently and understand updates as projects evolve.", "Process improvement: Identify recurring quality gaps, propose workflow improvements, and help build scalable QA processes for Korean-language projects."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=f755db4e-e39c-4340-8ff7-d516abe2a1f4&jobPostingId=KoreanQAL-25-318');
