INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('0a819fa0-1908-5aff-88ef-e76c3af0fc1a', 'Nepali Expert with Mathematical Background', 'sme.careers', 'Languages', 'Remote (4 Countries: Bangladesh, Bhutan, India…)', 'Contract', 'Not Applicable', '$15/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Nepali Language Expert (SME) to review AI-generated Nepali content and/or create high-quality Nepali reference content, evaluating language quality and step-by-step reasoning while providing precise written feedback. You will assess outputs for accuracy, fluency, grammar, spelling, tone, cultural appropriateness, and adherence to the prompt; identify errors in meaning, mistranslation, register, ambiguity, unnatural phrasing, terminology, script/formatting, and logical consistency; fact-check claims when needed; write high-quality rewrites and model answers that demonstrate best practices in Nepali writing; and rate and compare multiple AI responses based on correctness and overall quality.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your Nepali expertise directly helps improve the world’s premier AI models by making their Nepali language output more natural, reliable, culturally accurate, and clearly written.


### Responsibilities
• Develop AI Training Content: Create prompts and gold-standard Gujarati answers across multiple domains (general knowledge, customer support, education, conversational writing).
• Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI outputs to improve fluency, correctness, tone match, and cultural appropriateness.
• Ensure Model Integrity: Detect unsafe or misleading content, factual hallucinations, bias, and policy-risk language; validate reliability across use cases.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree (or higher) in Mathematics.
• Native or near-native Nepali proficiency (reading and writing required).
• Strong professional proficiency in English (minimum C1) to follow guidelines and provide detailed feedback in English.
• 3+ years of professional experience in writing, editing, localization, translation, content QA, journalism, education, or related language-focused work.
• Deep understanding of Nepali grammar, Devanagari script, spelling conventions, punctuation, honorifics, and style—able to explain why something is wrong and how to fix it.
