• Prepare the work environment: Ensure your setup supports the task, including having OBS installed, scenes/sources ready, audio/video inputs configured, permissions enabled, and references ready before recording.
• Record task execution: Record yourself executing the OBS Studio task on your computer while following project instructions and ensuring the workflow is clear, complete, and realistic.
• Document task context: Provide enough task context, steps, goals, recording settings, files, and notes so reviewers can understand what the task is and how it was completed.
• Demonstrate practical software use: Complete workflows involving scenes, sources, audio setup, display/window capture, overlays, output settings, recording profiles, or troubleshooting where relevant.
• Maintain submission quality: Review your recording and documentation before submission to ensure the task is complete, understandable, realistic, and aligned with project guidelines.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Hands-on experience using OBS Studio for screen recording, streaming, audio/video setup, scenes, sources, overlays, or capture workflows.
• English proficiency at B2 level or higher to understand project instructions, document tasks clearly, and communicate with the project team.
• Comfortable using a computer, managing media files, configuring devices, adjusting software settings, and recording workflows.
• Ability to come up with realistic and challenging OBS Studio tasks that reflect actual recording, streaming, tutorial, content creation, or troubleshooting use cases.
• Strong understanding of OBS basics such as scenes, sources, display capture, window capture, audio mixer, recording settings, output formats, hotkeys, and profiles.
• Ability to ensure your setup supports the task, including having OBS installed, recording permissions enabled, audio/video devices available, and required files/assets ready before recording.
• High attention to detail when preparing the task, executing the workflow, and checking that the recording is complete, clear, and understandable.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Additional professional skills are appreciated, including video production, content creation, streaming, teaching, technical support, admin, operations, or other computer-based workflows.


### Eligible Countries (3)
Bangladesh, India, Pakistan', '["Screen Capture", "Scenes", "Video Recording", "Screen Recording", "Computer Use", "OBS Studio", "audio setup", "English", "Streaming", "Sources"]', '["Create realistic OBS Studio tasks: Come up with realistic and challenging tasks that can be executed on the computer using OBS Studio, then document the task clearly in SuperAnnotate.", "Prepare the work environment: Ensure your setup supports the task, including having OBS installed, scenes/sources ready, audio/video inputs configured, permissions enabled, and references ready before recording.", "Record task execution: Record yourself executing the OBS Studio task on your computer while following project instructions and ensuring the workflow is clear, complete, and realistic.", "Document task context: Provide enough task context, steps, goals, recording settings, files, and notes so reviewers can understand what the task is and how it was completed.", "Demonstrate practical software use: Complete workflows involving scenes, sources, audio setup, display/window capture, overlays, output settings, recording profiles, or troubleshooting where relevant.", "Maintain submission quality: Review your recording and documentation before submission to ensure the task is complete, understandable, realistic, and aligned with project guidelines."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=45737ed2-61f7-47d4-9b41-8663a08b7055&jobPostingId=OBSStudio-26-137');
