• Deep understanding of imaging modalities and tradeoffs (sensitivity/specificity, limitations, artifacts, protocol impacts).
• Excellent safety judgment: contrast reactions, nephrotoxicity risk, pregnancy considerations, anticoagulation/procedure risks, radiation dose principles.
• Exceptional attention to detail when fact-checking and identifying unsafe assumptions, missed “can’t-miss” diagnoses, or misleading explanations; minimum C1 English proficiency.
