• Experience with AI training, data annotation, LLM evaluation, educational QA, curriculum QA, or rubric-based review is a strong plus.', '["Science Education", "LLM Evaluation", "School Science", "Child-Friendly Explanations", "Curriculum Review", "Elementary Science", "AI Training", "Trainer Feedback", "STEM Education", "English"]', '["Quality monitoring: Spot-check elementary science items, identify quality issues, provide ongoing feedback through DMs, and escalate recurring or critical issues.", "Science education review: Evaluate AI-generated science explanations, worksheets, activities, short answers, lesson-style content, examples, quizzes, and student-facing explanations for accuracy and grade-level fit.", "Trainer and QA communication: Update trainers and QAs on Discord about new item guidelines, project changes, workflow updates, quality expectations, and elementary science review standards.", "Question handling: Respond to trainer/QA questions clearly and promptly, especially around grade-level appropriateness, scientific concepts, safe activities, student misconceptions, and rubric interpretation.", "Trainer/QA activation management: DM contributors who are inactive or not working, encourage activation, track follow-ups, and flag availability issues when needed.", "Documentation: Create and maintain elementary science project documentation, including style guides, trackers, FAQs, quality notes, examples, honeypots, calibration tasks, and onboarding materials.", "Onboarding and training: Schedule and run onboarding/training calls with trainers and QAs to explain project expectations, workflows, rubrics, quality standards, and school-science-specific requirements.", "Quality alignment: Ensure all trainers and QAs apply elementary science review guidelines consistently and understand updates as projects evolve.", "Safety review: Flag unsafe experiments, misleading health/environment claims, overly advanced explanations, incorrect science facts, or age-inappropriate content.", "Process improvement: Identify recurring quality gaps, propose workflow improvements, and help build scalable QA processes for elementary science AI training projects.", "Native fluency in Punjabi"]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=d353a5e3-c4d7-4d33-9d11-1e07722604f6&jobPostingId=SchoolScience-26-142');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('cd465451-e5d2-5c3a-aad4-a474f263ac88', 'Senior Video Editor', 'sme.careers', 'Data Annotation & RLHF', 'Remote (28 Countries: Argentina, Australia, Bulgaria…)', 'Contract', 'Not Applicable', '$51/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Senior Video Editing Quality Assurance Specialist (SME) to review and evaluate AI-generated and human-edited video content, ensuring professional post-production quality, technical accuracy, visual consistency, and adherence to project-specific guidelines.

You will assess video outputs for editing quality, pacing, continuity, transitions, color grading, audio synchronization, storytelling, technical specifications, and overall production standards. You will identify editing errors, provide precise written feedback, compare multiple video outputs, and help establish consistent quality expectations across video editing and AI training projects.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your professional video editing expertise will directly help improve the world’s premier AI models by making their video understanding, editing, and generation capabilities more accurate, consistent, and aligned with professional production standards.

Portfolio requirement

Mandatory: As a part of selection process, applicants must ready to provide a working link to a professional video demo reel or portfolio that can be accessed by the SuperAnnotate team.

The portfolio should demonstrate professional editing capabilities, preferably including commercial, broadcast, film, television, or advanced digital video projects.


### Responsibilities
• Evaluate video editing quality: Review edited and AI-generated video content for pacing, continuity, transitions, storytelling, visual consistency, audio quality, and professional production standards.
• Perform technical quality assurance: Identify frame-rate inconsistencies, dropped frames, codec issues, color mismatches, synchronization problems, compression artifacts, and export-related defects.
• Optimize AI video performance: Evaluate and compare AI-generated video outputs, identifying visual artifacts, temporal inconsistencies, unnatural motion, continuity problems, and editing-quality issues.
• Develop AI training content: Create expert-level editing scenarios, reference examples, quality assessments, and structured feedback that reflect real-world post-production standards.
• Ensure production consistency: Evaluate adherence to creative briefs, editing instructions, style guides, technical specifications, and project-specific rubrics.
• Provide expert feedback: Clearly document video editing errors, explain their impact, and recommend appropriate corrections using professional editing terminology.
• Support quality calibration: Help establish consistent evaluation standards across editors, reviewers, and video quality assessment workflows.
• Maintain professional standards: Ensure reviewed content meets expectations for visual storytelling, technical delivery, audio-visual coherence, and overall production quality.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• 5+ years of professional video editing experience in film, television, broadcast, advertising, commercial production, digital media, or related post-production environments.
• English proficiency at C1–C2 level to understand complex project guidelines, communicate technical feedback, and provide detailed written evaluations in English.
• Advanced proficiency in at least two non-linear editing (NLE) systems, with Adobe Premiere Pro and DaVinci Resolve strongly preferred. Experience with Avid Media Composer or Final Cut Pro is also valuable.
• Previous experience as a Lead Editor, Senior Video Editor, Post-Production Supervisor, QC Coordinator, or in a comparable quality-focused production role.
• A shareable professional video demo reel or portfolio is mandatory, and must be accessible to the SuperAnnotate team for evaluation.
• Deep understanding of editing fundamentals, including pacing, continuity, shot selection, narrative structure, transitions, visual composition, and storytelling.
• Strong knowledge of video technical standards, including frame rates, resolutions, codecs, containers, aspect ratios, color spaces, export settings, and broadcast/digital delivery specifications.
• Experience with color correction, color grading, audio editing, synchronization, sound mixing, subtitles, captions, and motion graphics.
• Ability to identify subtle editing defects, including jump cuts, continuity errors, dropped frames, audio drift, inconsistent color, compression artifacts, inappropriate transitions, and technical delivery issues.
• Strong analytical judgment and attention to detail, with the ability to explain why an edit does or does not meet professional standards.
• Experience reviewing other editors'' work, providing structured feedback, conducting technical QC, or supervising post-production workflows.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to maintain consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor environment across time zones.
• Prior experience with AI-generated video evaluation, AI data training, video annotation, multimedia QA, or rubric-based evaluation is a strong plus.


### Eligible Countries (28)
Argentina, Australia, Bulgaria, Canada, China, Colombia, Germany, Greece, Hungary, India, Indonesia, Japan, Malaysia, Mexico, Poland, Portugal, Romania, Serbia, South Africa, South Korea, Thailand, The Czech Republic, The Philippines, The United Kingdom, The United States, Ukraine, United Arab Emirates, Vietnam', '["Video Quality Assurance", "Color Grading", "DaVinci Resolve", "Audio Synchronization", "Video Editing", "Adobe Premiere Pro", "AI Training", "English", "Non-Linear Editing", "Continuity", "Post-Production"]', '["Evaluate video editing quality: Review edited and AI-generated video content for pacing, continuity, transitions, storytelling, visual consistency, audio quality, and professional production standards.", "Perform technical quality assurance: Identify frame-rate inconsistencies, dropped frames, codec issues, color mismatches, synchronization problems, compression artifacts, and export-related defects.", "Optimize AI video performance: Evaluate and compare AI-generated video outputs, identifying visual artifacts, temporal inconsistencies, unnatural motion, continuity problems, and editing-quality issues.", "Develop AI training content: Create expert-level editing scenarios, reference examples, quality assessments, and structured feedback that reflect real-world post-production standards.", "Ensure production consistency: Evaluate adherence to creative briefs, editing instructions, style guides, technical specifications, and project-specific rubrics.", "Provide expert feedback: Clearly document video editing errors, explain their impact, and recommend appropriate corrections using professional editing terminology.", "Support quality calibration: Help establish consistent evaluation standards across editors, reviewers, and video quality assessment workflows.", "Maintain professional standards: Ensure reviewed content meets expectations for visual storytelling, technical delivery, audio-visual coherence, and overall production quality."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=76adc10a-fd7e-4d36-a9e3-5c64048912d2&jobPostingId=VideoEditor-26-900');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('84576557-0a32-532e-8ad1-cea52c1cbc7b', 'Slovak Language Expert', 'sme.careers', 'Languages', 'Remote (Slovakia)', 'Contract', 'Not Applicable', '$20/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Slovak Language Expert (SME) to review AI-generated Slovak content and/or create high-quality Slovak reference content, evaluating language quality and step-by-step reasoning while providing precise written feedback. You will assess outputs for accuracy, fluency, grammar, spelling, tone, cultural appropriateness, and adherence to the prompt; identify errors in meaning, mistranslation, register, ambiguity, unnatural phrasing, terminology, and logical consistency; fact-check claims when needed; write high-quality rewrites and model answers that demonstrate best practices in Slovak writing; and rate and compare multiple AI responses based on correctness and overall quality.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your Slovak expertise directly helps improve the world’s premier AI models by making their Slovak language output more natural, reliable, culturally accurate, and clearly written.


### Responsibilities
• Develop AI Training Content: Create prompts and gold-standard Slovak answers across multiple domains, including general knowledge, customer support, education, conversational writing, translation, localization, and culturally sensitive content.
• Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI outputs to improve fluency, correctness, tone match, register consistency, meaning preservation, terminology quality, and cultural appropriateness.
• Ensure Model Integrity: Detect unsafe or misleading content, factual hallucinations, bias, mistranslations, ambiguity, policy-risk language, and culturally inappropriate phrasing; validate reliability across use cases.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree or higher in Linguistics, Slovak Language, Slovak Literature, English Literature, Communications, Journalism, Translation, or a related field, or equivalent professional experience.
• Native or near-native Slovak proficiency, with strong reading and writing skills required.
• Strong professional proficiency in English, minimum C1, to follow guidelines and provide detailed feedback in English.
• 3+ years of professional experience in writing, editing, localization, translation, content QA, journalism, education, or related language-focused work.
• Deep understanding of Slovak grammar, spelling conventions, punctuation, diacritics, cases, declension, conjugation, aspect, word order, tone, and style—able to explain why something is wrong and how to fix it.
• Comfortable handling multiple registers, including formal, neutral, conversational, professional, educational, and public-facing Slovak, depending on audience and project requirements.
• High attention to detail when spotting subtle meaning shifts, awkward literal translations, incorrect case endings, agreement errors, hallucinated claims, Czech- or English-influenced phrasing, or culturally mismatched wording.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Prior experience with AI data training/annotation, translation QA, editorial QA, localization QA, or rubric-based evaluation is strongly preferred.', '["Style", "Copyediting", "Slovak", "Translation Quality Review", "Localization", "Fact-Checking", "Tone & Register", "English", "Proofreading", "Cultural Context", "Grammar"]', '["Develop AI Training Content: Create prompts and gold-standard Slovak answers across multiple domains, including general knowledge, customer support, education, conversational writing, translation, localization, and culturally sensitive content.", "Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI outputs to improve fluency, correctness, tone match, register consistency, meaning preservation, terminology quality, and cultural appropriateness.", "Ensure Model Integrity: Detect unsafe or misleading content, factual hallucinations, bias, mistranslations, ambiguity, policy-risk language, and culturally inappropriate phrasing; validate reliability across use cases."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=b6c88964-25ce-4293-925c-7c3a37091ba0&jobPostingId=Slovak-26-194');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('7c8ccb9c-5477-5945-b6d9-f0d79012bebf', 'Slovak Team Lead', 'sme.careers', 'Languages', 'Remote (Slovakia)', 'Contract', 'Mid Senior Level', '$25/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Slovak Quality Assurance Lead (QAL) to oversee quality, consistency, and trainer performance across Slovak AI training projects. You will review AI-generated Slovak content and trainer/QA work, evaluate output quality against project guidelines, provide precise written feedback, and ensure that all contributors follow the expected quality standards.

You will assess work for accuracy, fluency, grammar, spelling, tone, cultural appropriateness, meaning preservation, instruction-following, formatting, and adherence to project-specific rubrics. You will spot recurring quality issues, communicate updates to trainers and QAs, support onboarding, maintain documentation, and help activate contributors who are not working consistently. This role requires strong Slovak and English skills, excellent attention to detail, structured communication, and the ability to manage quality workflows across remote teams.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your Slovak quality leadership will directly help improve the world’s premier AI models by ensuring that Slovak training data is natural, accurate, culturally appropriate, well-documented, and aligned with client expectations.

Selection process involves an AI interview, a domain-specific task, and an interview with a recruiter.


### Responsibilities
• Quality monitoring: Spot-check Slovak items, identify quality issues, provide ongoing feedback through DMs, and escalate recurring or critical issues.
• Trainer and QA communication: Update trainers and QAs on Discord about new item guidelines, project changes, workflow updates, and quality expectations.
• Question handling: Respond to trainer/QA questions clearly and promptly, especially around Slovak wording, grammar, case endings, diacritics, register, translation fidelity, Czech-influenced wording, cultural context, terminology, and edge cases.
• Trainer/QA activation management: DM contributors who are inactive or not working, encourage activation, track follow-ups, and flag availability issues when needed.
• Documentation: Create and maintain Slovak project documentation, including style guides, trackers, FAQs, quality notes, examples, honeypots, and onboarding materials.
• Onboarding and training: Schedule and run onboarding/training calls with trainers and QAs to explain project expectations, workflows, rubrics, quality standards, and Slovak-specific style requirements.
• Quality alignment: Ensure all trainers and QAs apply Slovak language guidelines consistently and understand updates as projects evolve.
• Process improvement: Identify recurring quality gaps, propose workflow improvements, and help build scalable QA processes for Slovak-language projects.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Slovak, Linguistics, Translation, Communications, Journalism, English, Education, Quality Assurance, or a relevant domain/related field.
• Native or near-native Slovak proficiency with strong reading and writing skills.
• Strong grasp of the English language to follow project guidelines, communicate with teams, and provide clear feedback in English.
• 3+ years of professional experience in Slovak writing, editing, translation, localization, content QA, AI training, education, annotation, or related language-review workflows.
• Strong understanding of Slovak grammar, spelling conventions, punctuation, diacritics, declension, case endings, gender agreement, word order, tone, register, and cultural context.
• Comfortable distinguishing Slovak from Czech usage where relevant, including vocabulary, spelling, terminology, and localization expectations.
• Ability to evaluate Slovak content against detailed rubrics and identify issues such as mistranslation, literal phrasing, unnatural tone, incorrect case usage, missing diacritics, Czech-influenced wording, hallucinated claims, ambiguity, or inconsistent terminology.
• Experience leading or supporting remote teams of trainers, annotators, reviewers, editors, or QAs is strongly preferred.
• Comfortable working in fast-moving remote environments using tools such as Discord, Google Sheets, Google Docs, trackers, dashboards, and project management systems.
• Highly detail-oriented and organized, with the ability to maintain style guides, FAQs, trackers, onboarding materials, honeypots, and other quality documentation.
• Experience with AI training, data annotation, large language models, prompt/response evaluation, or rubric-based LLM QA is a strong plus.', '["LLM Evaluation", "Slovak", "Translation Quality Review", "Style Guides", "AI Training", "Documentation", "Trainer Feedback", "English", "Localization QA", "Slovak Quality Assurance"]', '["Quality monitoring: Spot-check Slovak items, identify quality issues, provide ongoing feedback through DMs, and escalate recurring or critical issues.", "Trainer and QA communication: Update trainers and QAs on Discord about new item guidelines, project changes, workflow updates, and quality expectations.", "Question handling: Respond to trainer/QA questions clearly and promptly, especially around Slovak wording, grammar, case endings, diacritics, register, translation fidelity, Czech-influenced wording, cultural context, terminology, and edge cases.", "Trainer/QA activation management: DM contributors who are inactive or not working, encourage activation, track follow-ups, and flag availability issues when needed.", "Documentation: Create and maintain Slovak project documentation, including style guides, trackers, FAQs, quality notes, examples, honeypots, and onboarding materials.", "Onboarding and training: Schedule and run onboarding/training calls with trainers and QAs to explain project expectations, workflows, rubrics, quality standards, and Slovak-specific style requirements.", "Quality alignment: Ensure all trainers and QAs apply Slovak language guidelines consistently and understand updates as projects evolve.", "Process improvement: Identify recurring quality gaps, propose workflow improvements, and help build scalable QA processes for Slovak-language projects."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=4cc1c08c-75f5-4290-a23f-4cd5d6b73875&jobPostingId=SlovakQAL-26-194');
