INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('e30487c9-7b49-5f08-9802-2a8c85cc8d11', 'Tamil Team Lead with Mathematical Background', 'sme.careers', 'Languages', 'Remote (4 Countries: India, Malaysia, Singapore…)', 'Contract', 'Mid Senior Level', '$25/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Tamil Quality Assurance Lead (QAL) to oversee quality, consistency, and trainer performance across Tamil AI training projects. You will review AI-generated Tamil content and trainer/QA work, evaluate output quality against project guidelines, provide precise written feedback, and ensure that all contributors follow the expected quality standards.

You will assess work for accuracy, fluency, grammar, spelling, tone, cultural appropriateness, meaning preservation, instruction-following, formatting, and adherence to project-specific rubrics. You will spot recurring quality issues, communicate updates to trainers and QAs, support onboarding, maintain documentation, and help activate contributors who are not working consistently. This role requires strong Tamil and English skills, excellent attention to detail, structured communication, and the ability to manage quality workflows across remote teams.

This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs. Your Tamil quality leadership will directly help improve the world’s premier AI models by ensuring that Tamil training data is natural, accurate, culturally appropriate, well-documented, and aligned with client expectations.

Selection process involves an AI interview, a domain-specific task, and an interview with a recruiter.


### Responsibilities
• Quality monitoring: Spot-check Tamil items, identify quality issues, provide ongoing feedback through DMs, and escalate recurring or critical issues.
• Trainer and QA communication: Update trainers and QAs on Discord about new item guidelines, project changes, workflow updates, and quality expectations.
• Question handling: Respond to trainer/QA questions clearly and promptly, especially around Tamil wording, register, translation fidelity, cultural context, regional variation, and edge cases.
• Trainer/QA activation management: DM contributors who are inactive or not working, encourage activation, track follow-ups, and flag availability issues when needed.
• Documentation: Create and maintain Tamil project documentation, including style guides, trackers, FAQs, quality notes, examples, honeypots, and onboarding materials.
• Onboarding and training: Schedule and run onboarding/training calls with trainers and QAs to explain project expectations, workflows, rubrics, quality standards, and Tamil-specific style requirements.
• Quality alignment: Ensure all trainers and QAs apply Tamil language guidelines consistently and understand updates as projects evolve.
• Process improvement: Identify recurring quality gaps, propose workflow improvements, and help build scalable QA processes for Tamil-language projects.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Mathematics
• Native or near-native Tamil proficiency with strong reading and writing skills.
• Strong grasp of the English language to follow project guidelines, communicate with teams, and provide clear feedback in English.
• 3+ years of professional experience in Tamil writing, editing, translation, localization, content QA, AI training, education, annotation, or related language-review workflows.
• Strong understanding of Tamil grammar, spelling conventions, punctuation, tone, register, regional variation, and cultural context.
• Ability to evaluate Tamil content against detailed rubrics and identify issues such as mistranslation, literal phrasing, unnatural tone, hallucinated claims, ambiguity, or inconsistent terminology.
• Experience leading or supporting remote teams of trainers, annotators, reviewers, editors, or QAs is strongly preferred.
• Comfortable working in fast-moving remote environments using tools such as Discord, Google Sheets, Google Docs, trackers, dashboards, and project management systems.
• Highly detail-oriented and organized, with the ability to maintain style guides, FAQs, trackers, onboarding materials, honeypots, and other quality documentation.
• Experience with AI training, data annotation, large language models, prompt/response evaluation, or rubric-based LLM QA is a strong plus.


### Eligible Countries (4)
India, Malaysia, Singapore, Sri Lanka', '["LLM Evaluation", "Tamil Quality Assurance", "Translation Quality Review", "Style Guides", "Tamil", "AI Training", "Documentation", "Trainer Feedback", "English", "Localization QA"]', '["Quality monitoring: Spot-check Tamil items, identify quality issues, provide ongoing feedback through DMs, and escalate recurring or critical issues.", "Trainer and QA communication: Update trainers and QAs on Discord about new item guidelines, project changes, workflow updates, and quality expectations.", "Question handling: Respond to trainer/QA questions clearly and promptly, especially around Tamil wording, register, translation fidelity, cultural context, regional variation, and edge cases.", "Trainer/QA activation management: DM contributors who are inactive or not working, encourage activation, track follow-ups, and flag availability issues when needed.", "Documentation: Create and maintain Tamil project documentation, including style guides, trackers, FAQs, quality notes, examples, honeypots, and onboarding materials.", "Onboarding and training: Schedule and run onboarding/training calls with trainers and QAs to explain project expectations, workflows, rubrics, quality standards, and Tamil-specific style requirements.", "Quality alignment: Ensure all trainers and QAs apply Tamil language guidelines consistently and understand updates as projects evolve.", "Process improvement: Identify recurring quality gaps, propose workflow improvements, and help build scalable QA processes for Tamil-language projects."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=00bc2fe8-9048-455a-a818-d982f82fbda2&jobPostingId=TamilQALMath-26-166');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('cf05b03b-def7-5a5b-83f3-b3c601d2eaaf', 'Tax and Audit Expert', 'sme.careers', 'Legal', 'Remote (17 Countries: Bangladesh, Bhutan, Brazil…)', 'Contract', 'Mid Senior Level', '$80/hr', 'In this hourly, remote contractor role, you will work as a Tax & Audit Subject Matter Expert (SME) to review AI-generated tax and audit responses and/or create expert accounting content, evaluating reasoning quality and step-by-step problem-solving while providing precise written feedback. You will assess solutions for accuracy, clarity, completeness, and adherence to the prompt; identify errors in tax treatment, compliance logic, audit methodology, risk assessment, internal controls, and financial reporting linkages; fact-check technical claims; write high-quality explanations and model solutions that demonstrate correct methods; and rate and compare multiple responses based on correctness and reasoning quality. This role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI Data Services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate, delivering training data for many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation-model labs.

Important:
There is no immediate project for this role; however, if qualified, you will be among the first experts we reach out to when relevant opportunities arise. This will also provide you with access to future projects available through our expert network.


### Responsibilities
• Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts and gold-standard outputs across tax and audit topics (tax scenarios, audit programs, workpaper examples, control assessments, and technical explanations).
• Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to improve technical correctness, clarity, compliance alignment, and practical usefulness.
• Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI outputs for inaccuracies, unsafe/noncompliant guidance, and bias; validate reliability across business scenarios.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree (or higher) in Accounting, Finance, Taxation, or a related field; CPA/ACCA/EA/CIA (or local equivalent) is a strong plus.
• 5+ years of professional experience in tax and/or audit (public accounting, advisory, internal audit, or industry).
• Strong command of tax fundamentals relevant to your jurisdiction(s): corporate/individual basics, taxable income adjustments, credits/deductions, nexus/permanent establishment awareness, withholding/VAT/GST concepts (as applicable).
• Strong command of audit fundamentals: planning, materiality, risk assessment, control testing, substantive procedures, sampling concepts, and audit evidence quality.
• Proven ability to review or prepare workpapers, reconciliations, and documentation that is clear, defensible, and audit-ready.
• Solid understanding of internal controls (segregation of duties, approvals, access controls) and familiarity with SOX concepts is a plus.
• Exceptional attention to detail when fact-checking and identifying unsupported conclusions, missing steps, incorrect citations, or noncompliant recommendations; minimum C1 English proficiency.
• Comfortable evaluating answers for internal consistency (debits/credits, timing/cutoff, tax logic, and financial statement impacts).
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Prior experience with AI data training/annotation, audit QA, tax technical writing, or policy interpretation is strongly preferred.


### Eligible Countries (17)
