• Record task execution: Record yourself executing the VS Code task on your computer while following project instructions and ensuring the workflow is clear, complete, and realistic.
• Document task context: Provide enough task context, steps, goals, project files, and notes so reviewers can understand what the task is and how it was completed.
• Demonstrate practical software use: Complete workflows involving editing, searching, debugging, formatting, running scripts, using the terminal, source control, extensions, or project organization where relevant.
• Maintain submission quality: Review your recording and documentation before submission to ensure the task is complete, understandable, realistic, and aligned with project guidelines.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Hands-on experience using Visual Studio Code (VS Code) for coding, editing files, debugging, extensions, terminal workflows, Git integration, or development tasks.
• English proficiency at B2 level or higher to understand project instructions, document tasks clearly, and communicate with the project team.
• Comfortable using a computer, managing files, installing extensions, opening folders/projects, navigating code, and recording workflows.
• Ability to come up with realistic and challenging VS Code tasks that reflect actual coding, editing, debugging, scripting, documentation, or developer-tool use cases.
• Strong understanding of VS Code basics such as Explorer, search, extensions, terminal, debugging, settings, formatting, source control, and workspace organization.
• Ability to ensure your setup supports the task, including having VS Code installed, files/projects available, extensions ready, and any required runtimes or references prepared before recording.
• High attention to detail when preparing the task, executing the workflow, and checking that the recording is complete and understandable.
• Reliable, self-directed, and able to deliver consistent quality in an hourly, remote contractor workflow across time zones.
• Additional professional skills are appreciated, including coding, QA, technical writing, GitHub, web development, data analysis, admin, operations, or other computer-based workflows.


### Eligible Countries (3)
Bangladesh, India, Pakistan', '["VS Code", "Git", "Developer Tools", "Screen Recording", "Visual Studio Code", "English", "Coding Workflow", "Debugging", "Terminal", "Code Editor"]', '["Create realistic VS Code tasks: Come up with realistic and challenging tasks that can be executed on the computer using VS Code, then document the task clearly in SuperAnnotate.", "Prepare the work environment: Ensure your setup supports the task, including having VS Code installed, files/projects available, extensions installed, dependencies ready, and any required references prepared before recording.", "Record task execution: Record yourself executing the VS Code task on your computer while following project instructions and ensuring the workflow is clear, complete, and realistic.", "Document task context: Provide enough task context, steps, goals, project files, and notes so reviewers can understand what the task is and how it was completed.", "Demonstrate practical software use: Complete workflows involving editing, searching, debugging, formatting, running scripts, using the terminal, source control, extensions, or project organization where relevant.", "Maintain submission quality: Review your recording and documentation before submission to ensure the task is complete, understandable, realistic, and aligned with project guidelines."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=cea7b1b6-c7dc-4485-b592-f1ab62609742&jobPostingId=VSCode-26-126');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('23b5011f-0930-5131-893c-02bfd42fdf1a', 'Workforce Experience Specialists', 'sme.careers', 'Data Annotation & RLHF', 'Remote (Bangladesh)', 'Contract', 'Associate', 'BDT 35000 - BDT 50000/mo', '# About SuperAnnotate

SuperAnnotate helps the world’s leading AI teams build responsible, next-generation models powered by high-quality human data. We’re a fast-growing Series B startup bridging the gap between advanced AI innovation and the data that drives it. Our global network of expert specialists, scalable managed operations, precise talent matching, and full project transparency ensure unmatched data quality at scale. Trusted by innovators like Databricks and ServiceNow - and backed by NVIDIA, Dell Technologies Capital, Databricks Ventures, Cox Enterprises, and Lionel Messi’s Play Time VC - SuperAnnotate is proud to be the top-ranked AI data company on G2 for multiple consecutive years, including 2025.

# About the team

SME Careers is our platform for recruiting, onboarding and paying the domain experts and annotators behind our AI projects. The team works across Dhaka, Armenia and the United States. Our Mirpur DOHS office in Dhaka is home to core engineering, workforce experience, forward-deployed engineering and part of project management. You''ll be part of the Dhaka team, with hybrid and remote work supported. You''ll report to a manager in San Francisco and work regularly with our teams in the US and Europe.

# The role

From the moment someone applies to SME Careers until they''re paid for their work, you''re the person they come to when something goes wrong. That might be a stuck application, a missing interview invite, a confusing guideline, lost platform access or a late payment. You fix it or route it to the right team, notice when the same problem keeps happening, and keep projects moving. The job will be contracted through our local partner in Bangladesh.

# What you''ll do

- Help applicants and contractors at every stage, from application, assessment and onboarding through project work and payments, using Slack, Discord and our support tools.
- Resolve issues with Talent, Engineering, Finance and project leads. Escalate clearly when something needs a decision.
- Keep an eye on project progress and contractor capacity, and help reassign work when a project falls behind.
- Spot recurring problems and turn them into fixes: better FAQs, templates, SOPs or guideline updates.
- Keep issue tracking and handover notes clean so nothing slips between shifts.

# Your first weeks
You''ll shadow the Dhaka team, learn our platform and project workflows, and start handling applicant and contractor questions on your own by week three or four.

# What you''ll bring

- 1–3 years in support, community or operations, ideally at an AI data, tech or BPO company.
- Excellent written English. Most of your work is written communication with contractors around the world.
- Comfort managing several workstreams in spreadsheets and tools like Slack, Discord or Jira.
- A habit of noticing when something''s off and chasing it until it''s fixed.
- Nice to have: data annotation or QA experience, a basic understanding of LLMs, Python or advanced Sheets formulas.

# Schedule

We support projects around the clock. You''ll work 5 days a week on a rotating roster that can include weekends and night shifts. Shifts are published in advance.

# Salary and benefits

- BDT 35,000–50,000 per month, based on skills and experience
- Two festival bonuses a year
- Performance-based incentives
- Group health insurance
- Earned leave encashment
- Yearly performance and salary review
- Learning and development support in AI operations
- Team events: Pahela Baishakh, Falgun, year-end, New Year and an annual outing
- Morning snacks at the office

# Why this role

You''ll sit at the center of how SuperAnnotate recruits and supports its global expert workforce, and see up close how AI training data is produced for some of the most advanced AI teams in the world. People who do well here move into lead, talent or project operations roles.

# Equal Opportunity

We are an equal-opportunity employer and value diversity at our company. At SuperAnnotate diversity means to us making an effort to reflect the many experiences and identities of the outside world, and treating each other with fairness and without bias. Every day we foster an environment where people of all backgrounds not only belong, but excel to succeed as a company and grow together. We offer equal opportunity regardless of sex, sexual orientation, national origin, color, race, age, marital status, disability, gender identity, veterans and more.

We may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support parts of the hiring process, such as reviewing applications, analyzing resumes, or assessing responses. These tools assist our recruitment team but do not replace human judgment. Final hiring decisions are ultimately made by humans. If you would like more information about how your data is processed, please contact us.


### Responsibilities
• Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts in various topics and responses to guide AI learning, ensuring the models reflect a comprehensive understanding of diverse subjects.
• Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to enhance the model''s accuracy, fluency, and contextual relevance.
• Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI models for potential inaccuracies or biases, validating their reliability across use cases.', '[]', '["Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts in various topics and responses to guide AI learning, ensuring the models reflect a comprehensive understanding of diverse subjects.", "Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to enhance the model''s accuracy, fluency, and contextual relevance.", "Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI models for potential inaccuracies or biases, validating their reliability across use cases."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=9b1bf78f-9e80-4cc0-b5c2-aae8951f3fb0&jobPostingId=WFE-26-001');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO jobs (id, title, company, category, location, type, experience, compensation, description, skills, responsibilities, status, created_at, updated_at, external_url) VALUES ('6fb6836d-035a-50b6-a5bb-a8f773ecb749', 'iOS Engineer (Swift and Objective-C)', 'sme.careers', 'Coding', 'Remote (6 Countries: Germany, India, Thailand…)', 'Contract', 'Mid Senior Level', '$110/hr', 'As an iOS Engineer (Swift / Objective-C), you will work remotely on an hourly paid basis to review AI-generated iOS code, mobile architectures, and technical explanations, as well as produce high-quality reference implementations and step-by-step reasoning for complex engineering problems. You will assess solutions for correctness, clarity, security, performance, reliability, and adherence to the prompt; identify issues in UIKit/SwiftUI implementation, concurrency, memory management, threading, app lifecycle, networking, persistence, and build/release practices; fact-check technical information; write high-quality explanations and model solutions that demonstrate best practices; and rate and compare multiple AI responses based on correctness and reasoning quality.

This fully remote, hourly paid contractor role is with SME Careers, a fast-growing AI data services company and subsidiary of SuperAnnotate that provides AI training data to many of the world’s largest AI companies and foundation model labs—where your frontend expertise will directly help improve the world’s premier AI models used by millions of developers worldwide.

Important:
There is no immediate project for this role; however, if qualified, you will be among the first experts we reach out to when relevant opportunities arise. This will also provide you with access to future projects available through our expert network.


### Responsibilities
• Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts across iOS topics and write high-quality reference answers to guide AI learning.
• Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to enhance correctness, security, performance, and maintainability.
• Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI outputs for inaccuracies or unsafe recommendations, validating reliability across real-world iOS use cases.


### Requirements & Qualifications
• Bachelor’s degree or higher in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a closely related technical field (or equivalent practical experience).
• 4+ years of professional experience building production iOS applications, including work in Swift and (ideally) Objective-C codebases.
• Expert-level proficiency in Swift (Swift 5+): value/reference semantics, generics, protocols, error handling, and modern language features.
• Strong iOS fundamentals: app lifecycle, view/controller architecture, navigation, state management, and background execution constraints.
• Solid concurrency experience: GCD, OperationQueue, and modern async/await patterns; ability to reason about race conditions and thread-safety.
• Strong understanding of ARC and iOS memory patterns (retain cycles, weak/unowned, leaks, Instruments).
• Experience with networking and data: URLSession, JSON parsing, caching, retries, offline strategies, and persistence (Core Data/SQLite/Realm).
• Experience with testing and quality: XCTest, UI testing, mocking strategies, CI/CD (Fastlane is a plus), and App Store release hygiene.
• Security awareness: secure storage (Keychain), transport security, auth flows, privacy permissions, and sensitive data handling.
• Minimum C1 English proficiency (written and spoken), with the ability to write clear technical explanations and follow detailed English-language guidelines.
• Previous experience with AI data training, annotation, or evaluating AI-generated technical content is a strong plus.
• Highly detail-oriented and systematic, with a methodical approach to evaluating reasoning quality and identifying subtle issues in complex iOS code.


### Eligible Countries (6)
Germany, India, Thailand, The United States, Timor Leste, Vietnam', '["Memory Management (ARC)", "Code Review", "SwiftUI", "iOS", "Networking", "Performance Optimization", "GCD", "Debugging", "Concurrency", "Objective-C", "Swift", "UIKit", "Async-Await"]', '["Develop AI Training Content: Create detailed prompts across iOS topics and write high-quality reference answers to guide AI learning.", "Optimize AI Performance: Evaluate and rank AI responses to enhance correctness, security, performance, and maintainability.", "Ensure Model Integrity: Test AI outputs for inaccuracies or unsafe recommendations, validating reliability across real-world iOS use cases."]', 'open', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', '2026-11-04T21:29:05.827928Z', 'https://sme.careers/apply?referral=rp--66f070&jobId=1badc85a-80a6-4a99-8920-135188f861cb&jobPostingId=iOS-26-157');

